1
00:00:04,266 --> 00:00:06,268
[dramatic music plays]

2
00:00:13,275 --> 00:00:15,360
[narrator] A long time ago…

3
00:00:19,740 --> 00:00:20,741
Wait a minute.

4
00:00:22,576 --> 00:00:24,453
That's not right. Hang on.

5
00:00:31,251 --> 00:00:33,586
[adventurous music plays]

6
00:00:33,587 --> 00:00:35,714
Perhaps in the distant future?

7
00:00:37,174 --> 00:00:40,469
TSUKUYOMI

8
00:00:48,351 --> 00:00:49,436
Wrong again.

9
00:00:49,936 --> 00:00:53,607
It's neither a long time ago
nor in the distant future.

10
00:00:55,317 --> 00:00:56,359
[grunts]

11
00:00:58,445 --> 00:01:00,946
It's just a teensy bit in the future,

12
00:01:00,947 --> 00:01:03,324
in a world not so different
from the present.

13
00:01:03,325 --> 00:01:05,744
- [gamer 1] A little help here!
- [gamer 2] On it.

14
00:01:07,079 --> 00:01:08,704
[gamer 1]
Your aiming skills are cracked, Iroha!

15
00:01:08,705 --> 00:01:10,081
SAME AS 4 SERVINGS PASTA
DON'T WASTE THEM!!

16
00:01:10,082 --> 00:01:11,874
[gamer 3] Totally.
So when are you gonna go pro?

17
00:01:11,875 --> 00:01:13,001
[Iroha] GGs.

18
00:01:13,585 --> 00:01:16,337
[narrator] This is Iroha,
a perfectly normal high school girl

19
00:01:16,338 --> 00:01:18,715
who also happens to be a gamer.

20
00:01:20,342 --> 00:01:23,803
Due to her not-so-great relationship
with her mother,

21
00:01:23,804 --> 00:01:26,556
she decided to move to Tokyo
and live on her own.

22
00:01:27,182 --> 00:01:30,851
In order to cover those pesky
living expenses and tuition fees,

23
00:01:30,852 --> 00:01:32,728
she somehow managed to make ends meet

24
00:01:32,729 --> 00:01:35,356
- by diligently working part-time jobs.
- No, thank you! Excuse me.

25
00:01:35,357 --> 00:01:40,027
At school, she had all the attributes
to excel in both academics and sports.

26
00:01:40,028 --> 00:01:42,738
She was a model student
admired by her peers.

27
00:01:42,739 --> 00:01:44,448
- [teacher] Miss Sakayori?
- Yes!

28
00:01:44,449 --> 00:01:46,117
"It has been a long time"
sentence structure.

29
00:01:46,118 --> 00:01:49,703
The past participle of the verb "to be",
combined with the auxiliary verb "has"

30
00:01:49,704 --> 00:01:51,122
creates the present perfect tense.

31
00:01:51,123 --> 00:01:53,290
- [students gasp, cheer]
- That is correct.

32
00:01:53,291 --> 00:01:54,542
Nice job.

33
00:01:54,543 --> 00:01:56,044
[chuckles, sighs]

34
00:01:56,962 --> 00:01:58,462
Yikes, that was too close!

35
00:01:58,463 --> 00:02:00,256
I passed out with my eyes still open.

36
00:02:00,257 --> 00:02:03,093
Good thing nobody noticed.
I really lucked out there!

37
00:02:06,304 --> 00:02:08,682
[narrator] As for her other activities…

38
00:02:09,933 --> 00:02:12,810
she prepped for class,
fangirled over her idols,

39
00:02:12,811 --> 00:02:16,105
cried herself to sleep,
played video games…

40
00:02:16,106 --> 00:02:17,189
YACHIYO RUNAMI VR CONCERT

41
00:02:17,190 --> 00:02:18,984
…and fangirled some more
in the VR world with her friends.

42
00:02:21,278 --> 00:02:22,361
IROHA SAKAYORI

43
00:02:22,362 --> 00:02:25,198
Gather around,
for this is the tale of Iroha Sakayori.

44
00:02:26,032 --> 00:02:28,535
- But you can just call her Iroha.
- [sighs]

45
00:02:29,452 --> 00:02:30,953
[narrator, on laptop] I feel very lucky,

46
00:02:30,954 --> 00:02:32,538
- and I'm grateful…
- [yawns]

47
00:02:32,539 --> 00:02:35,124
- …but sometimes I feel so trapped.
- Oh, crap!

48
00:02:35,125 --> 00:02:37,710
Empathizing with other people's pain
is appreciated,

49
00:02:37,711 --> 00:02:39,295
but you have to take care of yourself

50
00:02:39,296 --> 00:02:40,629
- as well.
- [grunting]

51
00:02:40,630 --> 00:02:43,216
- When you're feeling down, it's okay to…
- [sighs]

52
00:02:47,262 --> 00:02:49,388
[narrator] It's just another ordinary day

53
00:02:49,389 --> 00:02:52,308
for this busy bee
and her jam-packed schedule.

54
00:02:52,309 --> 00:02:53,392
[sighs]

55
00:02:53,393 --> 00:02:55,019
Uh, huh?

56
00:02:55,020 --> 00:02:57,188
[narrator] Yeah, so…

57
00:02:57,689 --> 00:02:59,189
Look, she's on her way back home.

58
00:02:59,190 --> 00:03:01,734
Um… [chuckles]

59
00:03:01,735 --> 00:03:03,694
OVER 100 MILLION USERS!
WELCOME TO TSUKUYOMI

60
00:03:03,695 --> 00:03:05,362
- Hi everyone!
- The long-awaited three-day weekend…

61
00:03:05,363 --> 00:03:06,614
- See you all soon!
-…has finally arrived.

62
00:03:06,615 --> 00:03:10,201
For the first time in forever,
I can get a whole six hours of sleep.

63
00:03:14,289 --> 00:03:16,749
YACHIYO RUNAMI

64
00:03:16,750 --> 00:03:19,335
[pop music playing]

65
00:03:19,336 --> 00:03:21,503
♪ I'm missing you again ♪

66
00:03:21,504 --> 00:03:25,007
♪ I'm wanting to see your smiling face ♪

67
00:03:25,008 --> 00:03:28,010
♪ I feel it when you're far away ♪

68
00:03:28,011 --> 00:03:31,388
♪ But even when the rain is falling ♪

69
00:03:31,389 --> 00:03:34,141
♪ Eventually, it dries away ♪

70
00:03:34,142 --> 00:03:37,811
♪ And leaves a rainbow in the sky ♪

71
00:03:37,812 --> 00:03:38,896
[crying]

72
00:03:38,897 --> 00:03:40,606
[narrator]
After being pushed to the limit,

73
00:03:40,607 --> 00:03:42,943
Iroha received a well-deserved break.

74
00:03:45,278 --> 00:03:47,780
♪ Give water to the withered plants ♪

75
00:03:47,781 --> 00:03:51,033
- ♪ We can gather, standing tall again ♪
- [gasps]

76
00:03:51,034 --> 00:03:53,118
♪ I promise it will be all right ♪

77
00:03:53,119 --> 00:03:54,370
A shooting star!

78
00:03:54,371 --> 00:03:56,205
I hope Mikado's wish is granted.

79
00:03:56,206 --> 00:03:57,289
That's all that matters.

80
00:03:57,290 --> 00:03:58,999
Should I make a wish?

81
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:00,168
Okay.

82
00:04:01,086 --> 00:04:04,589
Please send me money. [chuckles]

83
00:04:07,509 --> 00:04:10,428
[grunting]

84
00:04:13,556 --> 00:04:19,436
♪ In our hearts we've all got a song
It's a precious melody ♪

85
00:04:19,437 --> 00:04:24,984
♪ Straight from your soul
Singing so sweet ♪

86
00:04:24,985 --> 00:04:30,447
♪ And it never stops like a heartbeat
It just keeps driving along ♪

87
00:04:30,448 --> 00:04:36,204
♪ La, la, la, la, la, la-la ♪

88
00:04:38,623 --> 00:04:42,584
[narrator] Lo and behold,
Iroha saw something on her way home.

89
00:04:42,585 --> 00:04:46,797
The base of one of the utility poles
was glowing in seven different colors,

90
00:04:46,798 --> 00:04:48,383
kind of like a gaming rig.

91
00:04:49,175 --> 00:04:52,345
Curious yet weary, she took a closer look.

92
00:04:53,555 --> 00:04:55,764
[sighs]
Just the light messing with my eyes.

93
00:04:55,765 --> 00:04:57,683
- [yelps]
- [narrator] A brilliant light shone

94
00:04:57,684 --> 00:04:58,852
from inside the pole.

95
00:05:00,854 --> 00:05:03,440
[mysterious music plays]

96
00:05:04,482 --> 00:05:05,734
[music stops]

97
00:05:10,447 --> 00:05:11,905
- [music plays]
- [gasps]

98
00:05:11,906 --> 00:05:13,074
[music stops]

99
00:05:14,159 --> 00:05:15,869
[Iroha straining]

100
00:05:16,536 --> 00:05:18,246
- [music continues]
- You're not giving up, huh?

101
00:05:24,210 --> 00:05:25,920
[fussing]

102
00:05:26,755 --> 00:05:27,881
[sneezes]

103
00:05:29,090 --> 00:05:30,550
[baby chuckles]

104
00:05:35,096 --> 00:05:38,265
[narrator] Iroha didn't know
what to do, so she said this.

105
00:05:38,266 --> 00:05:39,392
[groans]

106
00:05:46,608 --> 00:05:48,777
- [gasps]
- [fusses]

107
00:05:49,569 --> 00:05:53,406
[chuckles] Sorry, but I'm kinda maxed
out with life stuff at the moment.

108
00:05:54,199 --> 00:05:55,366
[baby whimpers]

109
00:05:56,618 --> 00:05:57,701
[coos]

110
00:05:57,702 --> 00:05:59,662
[groaning]

111
00:06:00,955 --> 00:06:02,873
- Forgive me, I gotta go!
- [pedestrian] Screw this!

112
00:06:02,874 --> 00:06:04,958
I don't care what happens anymore!

113
00:06:04,959 --> 00:06:06,461
[chuckles]

114
00:06:08,171 --> 00:06:09,630
[cawing]

115
00:06:09,631 --> 00:06:10,964
[Iroha whimpers]

116
00:06:10,965 --> 00:06:13,593
Okay,
maybe this place isn't safe for a baby.

117
00:06:14,219 --> 00:06:16,011
Should I take you
to the police or something?

118
00:06:16,012 --> 00:06:17,388
[breathing heavily]

119
00:06:18,014 --> 00:06:20,349
Geez, how am I supposed
to carry something like this?

120
00:06:20,350 --> 00:06:22,851
[gasps] Hey, wait a minute! Hey!

121
00:06:22,852 --> 00:06:26,773
Excuse me! Open up. You forgot
something really important out here!

122
00:06:29,359 --> 00:06:30,442
[whimpers]

123
00:06:30,443 --> 00:06:32,319
Great,
now I look like some kind of criminal,

124
00:06:32,320 --> 00:06:34,030
kidnapping an innocent baby.

125
00:06:36,241 --> 00:06:38,367
- [coos]
- No, no, no, no, no!

126
00:06:38,368 --> 00:06:41,121
- [crying]
- [gasps]

127
00:06:45,416 --> 00:06:46,875
- [crying]
- Okay.

128
00:06:46,876 --> 00:06:48,293
Good baby. Nice baby.

129
00:06:48,294 --> 00:06:50,796
What am I gonna do?
I can't believe this is happening.

130
00:06:50,797 --> 00:06:52,006
[crying continues]

131
00:06:53,508 --> 00:06:55,008
BANG!

132
00:06:55,009 --> 00:06:56,802
Uh-oh, a bang on the wall.

133
00:06:56,803 --> 00:06:58,178
That's never happened before.

134
00:06:58,179 --> 00:07:00,139
- [crying continues]
- Why are you crying?

135
00:07:00,140 --> 00:07:01,557
There's nothing to be scared of.

136
00:07:01,558 --> 00:07:03,016
[babbles]

137
00:07:03,017 --> 00:07:04,643
- [banging on door]
- [gasps]

138
00:07:04,644 --> 00:07:05,811
HOW TO STOP BABY CRYING

139
00:07:05,812 --> 00:07:07,396
Stop babies from crying.

140
00:07:07,397 --> 00:07:10,900
Hey, how about a lullaby.
That usually works on babies, right?

141
00:07:11,901 --> 00:07:13,485
My memory escapes me.

142
00:07:13,486 --> 00:07:14,570
[baby fussing]

143
00:07:14,571 --> 00:07:15,572
[gasps]

144
00:07:16,823 --> 00:07:18,950
[baby fussing]

145
00:07:22,078 --> 00:07:26,248
♪ In our hearts we've all got a song ♪

146
00:07:26,249 --> 00:07:29,919
♪ It's a precious melody ♪

147
00:07:31,754 --> 00:07:35,257
♪ Straight from your soul ♪

148
00:07:35,258 --> 00:07:38,011
♪ Singing so sweet ♪

149
00:07:39,888 --> 00:07:41,931
Oh, Yachiyo's songs are magic.

150
00:07:47,145 --> 00:07:49,189
Finally! [groans]

151
00:07:49,856 --> 00:07:51,940
But what am I supposed to do now?

152
00:07:51,941 --> 00:07:54,151
Yeah,
I guess you could call it an incident.

153
00:07:54,152 --> 00:07:57,863
You see, this utility pole
was glowing rainbow colors,

154
00:07:57,864 --> 00:08:00,073
and all of a sudden a kid came out of it.

155
00:08:00,074 --> 00:08:01,575
Uh, I mean a baby.

156
00:08:01,576 --> 00:08:04,328
Yeah, I know it doesn't make any sense.
[chuckles]

157
00:08:04,329 --> 00:08:06,497
I honestly can't
make any sense of it either.

158
00:08:06,498 --> 00:08:07,582
[laughs]

159
00:08:08,333 --> 00:08:10,209
You know, on second thought,
everything's fine.

160
00:08:10,210 --> 00:08:12,294
I apologize for bothering you, officer.

161
00:08:12,295 --> 00:08:14,630
Yes! Thank you very much
and have a good night!

162
00:08:14,631 --> 00:08:15,964
[groans]

163
00:08:15,965 --> 00:08:17,217
I'm exhausted.

164
00:08:34,901 --> 00:08:36,276
[sighs]

165
00:08:36,277 --> 00:08:38,862
Was it a dream? No, it's real.

166
00:08:38,863 --> 00:08:40,448
Wait, was it this big?

167
00:08:41,115 --> 00:08:42,824
It peed itself! [groans]

168
00:08:42,825 --> 00:08:44,368
Seriously?

169
00:08:44,369 --> 00:08:46,119
BABY GOODS
NISHITAKEYA

170
00:08:46,120 --> 00:08:48,622
[Iroha sighs] Why is everything
so expensive in this store?

171
00:08:48,623 --> 00:08:50,874
And diapers are the worst!

172
00:08:50,875 --> 00:08:52,167
[baby babbles]

173
00:08:52,168 --> 00:08:55,712
That'll be 13,243 yen, please.

174
00:08:55,713 --> 00:08:56,880
Fuju~pay.

175
00:08:56,881 --> 00:08:57,965
AVAILABLE FUNDS: ¥23,532

176
00:08:57,966 --> 00:08:59,883
- [Iroha groans]
- [machine] Fuju~!

177
00:08:59,884 --> 00:09:02,845
Why am I doing this
for some random baby I found?

178
00:09:03,471 --> 00:09:06,975
Nope, I'm not gonna think about
my poor life choices until next week.

179
00:09:08,017 --> 00:09:09,810
[snoring]

180
00:09:09,811 --> 00:09:10,895
Huh?

181
00:09:15,191 --> 00:09:16,316
[gasps, yelps]

182
00:09:16,317 --> 00:09:17,402
[sighs]

183
00:09:23,783 --> 00:09:25,158
[soundtrack playing]

184
00:09:25,159 --> 00:09:27,286
What the hell do you know about me,
you hypocrite?

185
00:09:27,287 --> 00:09:30,539
I feel like everything is moving
at such a fast pace nowadays.

186
00:09:30,540 --> 00:09:32,916
- I wonder if I'm gonna be able to keep up.
- [gasps]

187
00:09:32,917 --> 00:09:34,210
[chuckling]

188
00:09:36,170 --> 00:09:38,005
I couldn't understand
what he was talking about.

189
00:09:38,006 --> 00:09:39,090
[sighs]

190
00:09:48,266 --> 00:09:49,934
[Iroha grunts] Heavy.

191
00:09:50,768 --> 00:09:51,811
[child grunts]

192
00:09:57,859 --> 00:09:59,152
A JOURNEY TO TSUKUYOMI

193
00:10:06,242 --> 00:10:08,536
[child] Hey, I'm hungry. Get up, get up.

194
00:10:09,037 --> 00:10:12,581
- Hang on. Give me a second.
- I want milk.

195
00:10:12,582 --> 00:10:16,501
[Iroha groans] Please wait a moment
while I put on the kettle.

196
00:10:16,502 --> 00:10:17,503
- [gasps]
- [gasps]

197
00:10:19,339 --> 00:10:20,839
Scary.

198
00:10:20,840 --> 00:10:22,466
[Iroha screaming]

199
00:10:22,467 --> 00:10:23,635
[panting]

200
00:10:25,553 --> 00:10:26,804
Kindly take your leave.

201
00:10:28,306 --> 00:10:32,142
This is seriously freaking me out.
How did you get so big so quickly?

202
00:10:32,143 --> 00:10:34,686
Hmm. Well,
everything moves so fast nowadays,

203
00:10:34,687 --> 00:10:37,105
and life passes you by
in the blink of an eye.

204
00:10:37,106 --> 00:10:40,192
Yeah, things that are a freak of nature.
No thanks.

205
00:10:40,193 --> 00:10:41,985
- [straining]
- [screaming]

206
00:10:41,986 --> 00:10:43,654
Come on, stand up and get out of here.

207
00:10:43,655 --> 00:10:45,073
[yelling]

208
00:10:45,782 --> 00:10:46,908
[groans]

209
00:10:47,408 --> 00:10:48,867
Oh, no. Are you okay?

210
00:10:48,868 --> 00:10:53,331
No, I bumped my head
and now it really hurts! [crying]

211
00:10:54,832 --> 00:10:56,792
Look,
I don't have the time nor the patience

212
00:10:56,793 --> 00:10:58,795
to be babysitting children right now.

213
00:10:59,337 --> 00:11:00,588
GRUMBLE

214
00:11:03,800 --> 00:11:05,009
[stomach grumbles]

215
00:11:06,636 --> 00:11:08,012
[grumbles]

216
00:11:09,055 --> 00:11:11,891
Hmm. I'm hungry too.

217
00:11:13,101 --> 00:11:15,435
[Iroha] 594 yen for takeout.

218
00:11:15,436 --> 00:11:16,978
That's five meals' worth.

219
00:11:16,979 --> 00:11:18,147
And it's 2:00 in the morning.

220
00:11:18,856 --> 00:11:19,857
Here.

221
00:11:24,112 --> 00:11:26,114
Huh? Huh.

222
00:11:29,325 --> 00:11:30,326
[grunts]

223
00:11:31,619 --> 00:11:33,454
What is this magic? It's so good!

224
00:11:34,831 --> 00:11:38,792
- Well, uh, it's omurice, I guess.
- Is that what it's called?

225
00:11:38,793 --> 00:11:40,794
- I love omurice!
- Really? That's great.

226
00:11:40,795 --> 00:11:42,170
I'm glad to hear it.

227
00:11:42,171 --> 00:11:43,255
[Yachiyo on tablet]

228
00:11:43,256 --> 00:11:45,132
Do you have any idea where you came from?

229
00:11:45,133 --> 00:11:47,592
[Yachiyo] …and support me
mean the entire universe to me.

230
00:11:47,593 --> 00:11:48,760
I'd never be where I am today

231
00:11:48,761 --> 00:11:50,054
- if it weren't for all of you.
- [grunts]

232
00:11:50,596 --> 00:11:52,139
[Iroha] Wait, the moon?

233
00:11:52,140 --> 00:11:53,265
[child] Maybe.

234
00:11:53,266 --> 00:11:54,724
[scoffs]

235
00:11:54,725 --> 00:11:58,603
So, why did you come here, Ms. Alien,
to invade us?

236
00:11:58,604 --> 00:12:02,191
[sighs] Now that I think about it,
I honestly don't remember.

237
00:12:02,942 --> 00:12:05,485
Where I come from,
every day was super boring.

238
00:12:05,486 --> 00:12:07,946
I wanted to run away
and find someplace fun and exciting

239
00:12:07,947 --> 00:12:09,030
where I could be happy.

240
00:12:09,031 --> 00:12:10,450
You shouldn't have run away.

241
00:12:10,992 --> 00:12:12,702
What? Why not?

242
00:12:13,202 --> 00:12:14,454
[groans, scoffs]

243
00:12:16,789 --> 00:12:20,334
So anyway, changing the subject,
does this look familiar to you at all?

244
00:12:21,085 --> 00:12:24,338
- Nope. What is it?
- The Tale of the Bamboo Cutter.

245
00:12:25,089 --> 00:12:28,092
A princess from the moon
appears out of a bamboo stalk,

246
00:12:28,593 --> 00:12:30,636
and an old man takes her
and then raises her,

247
00:12:31,137 --> 00:12:33,180
then she's pressured
into getting married and stuff.

248
00:12:33,181 --> 00:12:34,556
What? Married? [grunts]

249
00:12:34,557 --> 00:12:37,642
You came out of a glowing utility pole
instead of a bamboo stalk,

250
00:12:37,643 --> 00:12:40,687
but I have reason to believe
that you're the Princess Kaguya.

251
00:12:40,688 --> 00:12:42,440
- [straining]
- Stop it!

252
00:12:42,982 --> 00:12:45,026
- [straining]
- Hey!

253
00:12:46,194 --> 00:12:47,736
I'm so sorry, what was that again?

254
00:12:47,737 --> 00:12:48,946
- Please continue.
- What?

255
00:12:50,239 --> 00:12:52,866
Okay, that means you're
the old man in this picture. Right, Iroha?

256
00:12:52,867 --> 00:12:55,035
Sure, if it were 80 years from now
and I was a man.

257
00:12:55,036 --> 00:12:57,329
You know how insulting that sounds? Focus!

258
00:12:57,330 --> 00:12:58,788
[laughs]

259
00:12:58,789 --> 00:13:00,999
Wait, back up a minute.
How do you know my name?

260
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:04,252
On second thought, there's no way that
someone like you is the Princess Kaguya.

261
00:13:04,253 --> 00:13:06,422
[scoffs] I don't even know
what I'm saying anymore.

262
00:13:07,173 --> 00:13:09,925
[child] Hey. So what happens at the end
of the story?

263
00:13:09,926 --> 00:13:12,427
[Iroha] Uh, her people
take her back to the moon.

264
00:13:12,428 --> 00:13:16,056
The old men fought to keep her on Earth,
but unfortunately it was all in vain.

265
00:13:16,057 --> 00:13:18,016
The princess is dressed
in a celestial robe,

266
00:13:18,017 --> 00:13:20,602
she goes back to the moon,
and forgets everything about Earth.

267
00:13:20,603 --> 00:13:21,895
Huh.

268
00:13:21,896 --> 00:13:24,065
Uh. Huh?

269
00:13:25,691 --> 00:13:27,359
It won't move. What happens next?

270
00:13:27,360 --> 00:13:29,319
That's all there is. A happy ending.

271
00:13:29,320 --> 00:13:31,655
What? She goes back
to the moon and that's it?

272
00:13:31,656 --> 00:13:33,323
That's, like, the worst ending ever!

273
00:13:33,324 --> 00:13:35,159
- No!
- [laughs]

274
00:13:35,868 --> 00:13:39,079
Princess Kaguya's
definitely not okay with that ending!

275
00:13:39,080 --> 00:13:41,456
And the fact that it's supposed
to be a heartwarming story

276
00:13:41,457 --> 00:13:42,624
makes it so much worse!

277
00:13:42,625 --> 00:13:43,917
[crying]

278
00:13:43,918 --> 00:13:46,628
That's the way the cookie crumbles,
my friend. Get over it.

279
00:13:46,629 --> 00:13:49,548
I don't want a bad ending,
I want a happy ending!

280
00:13:49,549 --> 00:13:51,717
This is so unfair! I hate it!

281
00:13:52,885 --> 00:13:54,719
[Kaguya babbling]

282
00:13:54,720 --> 00:13:58,558
You can throw a fit all you want.
It's still not gonna change anything.

283
00:13:59,809 --> 00:14:02,061
If its true,
then it's already been decided.

284
00:14:04,272 --> 00:14:06,941
You just have to accept your fate
and be prepared.

285
00:14:07,692 --> 00:14:08,693
That's it.

286
00:14:10,444 --> 00:14:13,614
[gargling, spits]

287
00:14:14,699 --> 00:14:17,326
Figures. I've got more canker sores.
Great.

288
00:14:18,119 --> 00:14:20,537
[sighs]
This three-day weekend went by too fast.

289
00:14:20,538 --> 00:14:22,581
I got it! It's been decided!

290
00:14:22,582 --> 00:14:24,249
I'm gonna make my own happy ending!

291
00:14:24,250 --> 00:14:27,461
And you're gonna be my passenger
on this ride to the grand finale.

292
00:14:28,004 --> 00:14:29,046
Come on!

293
00:14:31,924 --> 00:14:33,550
I don't need a happy ending.

294
00:14:33,551 --> 00:14:36,052
A normal ending is perfectly fine with me.

295
00:14:36,053 --> 00:14:38,513
Listen to what you're saying.
You don't really mean that, do you?

296
00:14:38,514 --> 00:14:40,015
What are you doing? Get away from me,

297
00:14:40,016 --> 00:14:42,225
- you creepy alien!
- You're so mean.

298
00:14:42,226 --> 00:14:44,937
Why can't you just let me sleep?

299
00:14:48,983 --> 00:14:50,151
[groans]

300
00:14:53,446 --> 00:14:54,447
[gasps]

301
00:14:55,156 --> 00:14:56,616
Hmm?

302
00:14:57,408 --> 00:14:58,951
Well, I guess she left.

303
00:14:59,660 --> 00:15:02,580
Maybe it was just a dream
caused by my stressful schedule.

304
00:15:03,539 --> 00:15:04,540
Yes!

305
00:15:05,875 --> 00:15:07,710
Good morning. I'm hiding right here.

306
00:15:09,045 --> 00:15:10,170
Yo, Iroha!

307
00:15:10,171 --> 00:15:13,173
Who's this lady on the Internet
that you constantly watch?

308
00:15:13,174 --> 00:15:15,634
- You really like her?
- That's Yachiyo Runami,

309
00:15:15,635 --> 00:15:17,177
an AI live streamer.

310
00:15:17,178 --> 00:15:18,261
I'm a fan.

311
00:15:18,262 --> 00:15:19,805
[Kaguya] Whoa! AI?

312
00:15:20,306 --> 00:15:22,098
You mean, like,
she's a robot or something?

313
00:15:22,099 --> 00:15:23,725
She can clone herself, sing and dance,

314
00:15:23,726 --> 00:15:26,061
and she's 8,000 years old.
That's her backstory.

315
00:15:26,062 --> 00:15:28,981
Wow, no way!

316
00:15:31,025 --> 00:15:32,692
I gotta go to school. See ya.

317
00:15:32,693 --> 00:15:34,527
No, don't go!

318
00:15:34,528 --> 00:15:36,321
Have you grown again?

319
00:15:36,322 --> 00:15:37,989
- Stay with me. Please don't leave.
- Sorry,

320
00:15:37,990 --> 00:15:39,699
but I can't skip school.

321
00:15:39,700 --> 00:15:41,117
Don't go anywhere.

322
00:15:41,118 --> 00:15:42,535
Look, your food's over there.

323
00:15:42,536 --> 00:15:43,662
Pancakes.

324
00:15:43,663 --> 00:15:44,997
IROHA'S FLOUR AND WATER PANCAKES

325
00:15:48,084 --> 00:15:49,168
[groans]

326
00:15:50,002 --> 00:15:51,754
Ugh, super gross.

327
00:15:52,338 --> 00:15:53,922
Please don't go!

328
00:15:53,923 --> 00:15:55,716
Is school really that important?

329
00:15:56,217 --> 00:15:58,094
More important than anything.

330
00:15:58,928 --> 00:16:01,096
Getting involved with you
was my responsibility,

331
00:16:01,097 --> 00:16:03,515
but I'll make sure
everything goes back to normal.

332
00:16:03,516 --> 00:16:06,018
So, hurry up and remember
how to get back to the moon.

333
00:16:09,939 --> 00:16:11,232
[blows raspberry]

334
00:16:12,066 --> 00:16:13,483
[piano music playing]

335
00:16:13,484 --> 00:16:16,695
This is some assassin-level sleepiness.

336
00:16:16,696 --> 00:16:17,905
Not again.

337
00:16:19,031 --> 00:16:21,491
Would anyone like to
give this piece a shot?

338
00:16:21,492 --> 00:16:23,494
[snoring]

339
00:16:29,667 --> 00:16:30,751
[teacher] Hmm.

340
00:16:33,254 --> 00:16:35,088
That was flawlessly accurate.

341
00:16:35,089 --> 00:16:36,674
- Wonderful!
- Hmm.

342
00:16:37,508 --> 00:16:39,260
[Iroha] At least something's going right.

343
00:16:40,011 --> 00:16:43,680
[sighs] I hope that rapidly growing alien
is behaving herself at home.

344
00:16:43,681 --> 00:16:44,931
TARGET SCHOOL LIST

345
00:16:44,932 --> 00:16:48,853
Keep up the pace and it's totally doable.
I'm confident you can pull this off.

346
00:16:49,437 --> 00:16:51,480
Thanks. That's what I'm striving for.

347
00:16:52,356 --> 00:16:55,359
With all this hard work, I'm sure
your parents must be very proud of you.

348
00:16:56,819 --> 00:16:58,362
Yeah. Well, that would be nice.

349
00:16:59,071 --> 00:17:00,321
[sighs]

350
00:17:00,322 --> 00:17:02,491
There's still plenty of time
until the deadline.

351
00:17:03,034 --> 00:17:04,201
Think this through.

352
00:17:07,496 --> 00:17:08,664
[panting]

353
00:17:11,083 --> 00:17:13,126
Yikes. It's so hot!

354
00:17:13,127 --> 00:17:14,128
- [meows]
- [grunts]

355
00:17:14,712 --> 00:17:16,713
Ah! Come here. [chuckles]

356
00:17:16,714 --> 00:17:18,424
I want one of these cuties.

357
00:17:20,760 --> 00:17:23,636
Can I pick your brain about what
you're gonna do after graduation?

358
00:17:23,637 --> 00:17:25,638
Let me guess.
It's something to do with music,

359
00:17:25,639 --> 00:17:27,140
or maybe e-sports, right?

360
00:17:27,141 --> 00:17:29,809
Seriously?
I don't have that kind of talent.

361
00:17:29,810 --> 00:17:32,062
I highly doubt
my parents would approve of that.

362
00:17:32,063 --> 00:17:34,147
It's either Tokyo University
or something equivalent.

363
00:17:34,148 --> 00:17:37,525
[friend 1] That's the bare minimum?
Super harsh.

364
00:17:37,526 --> 00:17:40,446
[friend 2] Compared to you,
I guess my parents just spoil me rotten.

365
00:17:41,197 --> 00:17:44,324
Thankfully the only thing I don't have
to worry about is being unhealthy,

366
00:17:44,325 --> 00:17:46,367
'cause I ended up with good genes.

367
00:17:46,368 --> 00:17:49,287
[grunts] Hell yeah!
What a great time to be alive.

368
00:17:49,288 --> 00:17:50,455
Wouldn't expect any less

369
00:17:50,456 --> 00:17:53,625
from a superhuman who earns
her own tuition and living expenses.

370
00:17:53,626 --> 00:17:54,834
[Iroha chuckles]

371
00:17:54,835 --> 00:17:56,878
Iroha, you're pushing yourself too hard.

372
00:17:56,879 --> 00:17:58,880
You should learn to take it easy
once in a while.

373
00:17:58,881 --> 00:18:00,216
I'm gonna hit you with some logic.

374
00:18:01,509 --> 00:18:03,051
[Iroha] Okay, I'll take it easy.

375
00:18:03,052 --> 00:18:06,222
- [pedestrian 1] Look at that cute girl.
- [pedestrian 2] Is she stalking someone?

376
00:18:06,931 --> 00:18:09,099
[Iroha]
I wonder if she's okay all by herself.

377
00:18:09,100 --> 00:18:11,851
- [friend 1] It's this way, right?
- Yeah. It's up those stairs.

378
00:18:11,852 --> 00:18:13,895
We've got a surprise for you.

379
00:18:13,896 --> 00:18:15,188
Uh, what do you mean?

380
00:18:15,189 --> 00:18:16,731
A new café opened up.

381
00:18:16,732 --> 00:18:18,733
You promised you'd check it out with us.

382
00:18:18,734 --> 00:18:20,819
- Come on.
- But I don't know if I can today.

383
00:18:20,820 --> 00:18:21,903
Let's go.

384
00:18:21,904 --> 00:18:24,240
I really don't have a lot of free time.

385
00:18:28,410 --> 00:18:31,454
Since Iroha's notes saved us from failing,
behold!

386
00:18:31,455 --> 00:18:33,289
Here's a token of our thanks.

387
00:18:33,290 --> 00:18:35,625
[both] We hope you enjoy your present!

388
00:18:35,626 --> 00:18:36,961
Thanks a lot, you two.

389
00:18:37,711 --> 00:18:39,463
- This looks--
- [Kaguya grunts]

390
00:18:42,383 --> 00:18:44,135
[exclaims]

391
00:18:45,261 --> 00:18:46,553
'Sup, Iroha!

392
00:18:46,554 --> 00:18:48,888
She's so cute!
Iroha, is she one of your friends?

393
00:18:48,889 --> 00:18:50,640
I just noticed she's wearing your clothes.

394
00:18:50,641 --> 00:18:52,225
Do you like pancakes?

395
00:18:52,226 --> 00:18:54,061
- Do you wanna try this one too?
- Huh?

396
00:18:56,355 --> 00:18:58,481
These are pancakes? No way!

397
00:18:58,482 --> 00:19:00,568
They're nothing like the ones Iroha makes.

398
00:19:01,694 --> 00:19:03,946
Uh, well, she's not exactly a friend.
She, uh…

399
00:19:04,947 --> 00:19:06,198
I'm from the moon.

400
00:19:07,825 --> 00:19:10,451
Actually she meant
she's feeling over the moon.

401
00:19:10,452 --> 00:19:11,453
She's my cousin.

402
00:19:11,954 --> 00:19:15,290
I feel the same way.
These pancakes are really delicious.

403
00:19:15,291 --> 00:19:17,584
- What's your name?
- [Iroha stammers] Um…

404
00:19:17,585 --> 00:19:18,711
It's…

405
00:19:19,295 --> 00:19:20,670
It's Kaguya.

406
00:19:20,671 --> 00:19:22,964
- [friend 1] Kaguya! Super cute.
- Right?

407
00:19:22,965 --> 00:19:25,176
Kaguya?

408
00:19:25,843 --> 00:19:27,093
Kaguya!

409
00:19:27,094 --> 00:19:30,097
Kaguya. It's so cute! [chuckles]

410
00:19:31,348 --> 00:19:32,682
[Kaguya gobbling]

411
00:19:32,683 --> 00:19:34,184
[Iroha] Sorry, gotta run.
Thanks for the dessert!

412
00:19:34,185 --> 00:19:35,894
I'll make it up to you both later,
I promise!

413
00:19:35,895 --> 00:19:37,521
- [exclaims]
- [yells]

414
00:19:38,272 --> 00:19:41,524
Wow, it was so nice and cool
in that building, wasn't it?

415
00:19:41,525 --> 00:19:43,944
Why can't your place be like that, Iroha?

416
00:19:44,862 --> 00:19:46,738
Have you completely lost your mind?

417
00:19:46,739 --> 00:19:48,406
What if somebody found out
who you really are?

418
00:19:48,407 --> 00:19:49,616
Why the hell did you leave my place?

419
00:19:49,617 --> 00:19:51,701
- I told you to stay put.
- I left because I was bored.

420
00:19:51,702 --> 00:19:55,580
[grunts] Continue to live recklessly
and you'll end up destroying yourself.

421
00:19:55,581 --> 00:19:57,625
You gotta be more patient
and level-headed.

422
00:19:58,751 --> 00:19:59,834
[gasps]

423
00:19:59,835 --> 00:20:00,919
[no audible dialogue]

424
00:20:00,920 --> 00:20:03,005
[Kaguya] Hey,
can you show me how to use these?

425
00:20:03,881 --> 00:20:05,840
[Iroha] Are those my smart contacts?

426
00:20:05,841 --> 00:20:07,258
Did you bring them?

427
00:20:07,259 --> 00:20:09,135
Nah,
I bought my own pair with your laptop.

428
00:20:09,136 --> 00:20:10,554
What? [groans]

429
00:20:11,180 --> 00:20:12,388
WALLET BALANCE: ¥452

430
00:20:12,389 --> 00:20:13,807
CHANGE FROM YESTERDAY: ¥-124400

431
00:20:14,391 --> 00:20:16,851
I worked so hard to save up money.

432
00:20:16,852 --> 00:20:18,978
I worked so hard
to save all of that money!

433
00:20:18,979 --> 00:20:20,063
Hey, I've got an idea!

434
00:20:20,064 --> 00:20:22,690
Why don't we just go on your laptop
and rewrite the bank info?

435
00:20:22,691 --> 00:20:24,400
We can increase
the numbers in your account.

436
00:20:24,401 --> 00:20:28,864
Absolutely not! What's wrong with you?
No! Don't you dare touch those numbers.

437
00:20:30,157 --> 00:20:31,824
[Kaguya] Hope you're hungry!

438
00:20:31,825 --> 00:20:33,744
[chuckles] Ta-da!

439
00:20:34,286 --> 00:20:38,206
For our first course, we have some
corn potage made with the freshest corn.

440
00:20:38,207 --> 00:20:40,917
Next, a crispy salad with burdock root
and asparagus!

441
00:20:40,918 --> 00:20:44,337
And for the main course, a delicious
hamburger steak simmered in tomato sauce.

442
00:20:44,338 --> 00:20:46,381
Last but certainly not least, zucchini.

443
00:20:46,382 --> 00:20:48,549
You used my money for this too,
didn't you?

444
00:20:48,550 --> 00:20:51,177
Well, of course. Impressed?

445
00:20:51,178 --> 00:20:53,055
[screeches] Huh?

446
00:20:57,393 --> 00:20:58,727
[whimpers]

447
00:20:59,311 --> 00:21:00,312
[Kaguya] Eat.

448
00:21:02,022 --> 00:21:04,774
Now I'm poor and destitute
without a yen to my name.

449
00:21:04,775 --> 00:21:07,111
I've been working endlessly
to pay for my tuition.

450
00:21:07,903 --> 00:21:09,988
What the hell? This is delicious.

451
00:21:09,989 --> 00:21:11,323
Who even are you?

452
00:21:11,991 --> 00:21:14,575
I can't remember the last time
I had a meal this good.

453
00:21:14,576 --> 00:21:16,328
All my body wants to do is cry.

454
00:21:16,829 --> 00:21:18,663
Is the last of my money worth it? [groans]

455
00:21:18,664 --> 00:21:19,789
You devil.

456
00:21:19,790 --> 00:21:21,541
What are you talking about?
I'm not a devil.

457
00:21:21,542 --> 00:21:22,626
I'm Kaguya.

458
00:21:23,127 --> 00:21:24,128
[Iroha groans]

459
00:21:25,004 --> 00:21:26,338
[crying] You're so annoying.

460
00:21:27,089 --> 00:21:28,090
- Damn, it's good.
- [chuckles]

461
00:21:32,428 --> 00:21:33,803
Hey, listen.

462
00:21:33,804 --> 00:21:35,848
I cannot possibly keep hiding you here.

463
00:21:36,515 --> 00:21:37,932
I'm already dealing with a lot,

464
00:21:37,933 --> 00:21:39,934
like living on my own
against my parents' wishes.

465
00:21:39,935 --> 00:21:41,854
I just don't want any trouble, okay?

466
00:21:42,521 --> 00:21:45,024
Ah! [humming]

467
00:21:46,108 --> 00:21:47,942
[humming]

468
00:21:47,943 --> 00:21:48,986
It's done!

469
00:21:49,611 --> 00:21:51,446
[gasps] Why are you on my laptop?

470
00:21:51,447 --> 00:21:53,323
You're not doing
anything illegal, are you?

471
00:21:53,324 --> 00:21:55,616
Nah, I bought a mobile gaming kit!

472
00:21:55,617 --> 00:21:58,453
Now InuDOGE can always be with me
wherever I go!

473
00:21:58,454 --> 00:22:01,664
By the way, what kind of grub do you want
to tickle your taste buds tomorrow?

474
00:22:01,665 --> 00:22:02,749
Any requests?

475
00:22:02,750 --> 00:22:05,710
She's planning on living here forever,
isn't she? [groans]

476
00:22:05,711 --> 00:22:08,671
Well, of course I have to live here.
Where else am I gonna go?

477
00:22:08,672 --> 00:22:11,924
What if a scientist finds me and they want
to put me in a lab and dissect me?

478
00:22:11,925 --> 00:22:14,011
Help! [screams]

479
00:22:15,637 --> 00:22:16,722
Uh.

480
00:22:17,389 --> 00:22:18,390
[sighs]

481
00:22:19,725 --> 00:22:21,601
You can stay until someone picks you up.

482
00:22:21,602 --> 00:22:22,769
For real?

483
00:22:22,770 --> 00:22:23,853
Don't stand out.

484
00:22:23,854 --> 00:22:25,897
- Don't go outside without permission.
- [groans]

485
00:22:25,898 --> 00:22:27,482
And don't get in my way.

486
00:22:27,483 --> 00:22:30,778
As long as you follow these three
simple rules, then you can stay here.

487
00:22:31,361 --> 00:22:34,405
What? So you're saying I'm doomed
to live my life in a prison,

488
00:22:34,406 --> 00:22:37,367
confined without any fun
or human interaction!

489
00:22:37,993 --> 00:22:40,286
You said you're gonna make
your own happy ending.

490
00:22:40,287 --> 00:22:41,704
Just don't get me involved.

491
00:22:41,705 --> 00:22:42,830
[blows raspberry]

492
00:22:42,831 --> 00:22:44,957
Let's pretend this conversation
didn't happen.

493
00:22:44,958 --> 00:22:46,834
But I want a happy ending together.

494
00:22:46,835 --> 00:22:49,378
- Please. Pretty please?
- [whistling]

495
00:22:49,379 --> 00:22:50,463
Stop that!

496
00:22:50,464 --> 00:22:52,299
Ignoring me is strictly forbidden!

497
00:22:53,217 --> 00:22:54,801
- [grumbles]
- Seriously?

498
00:22:54,802 --> 00:22:56,010
ALARM

499
00:22:56,011 --> 00:22:57,386
[gasps]

500
00:22:57,387 --> 00:22:58,805
[groans]

501
00:22:58,806 --> 00:23:00,098
- My homework.
- No!

502
00:23:00,099 --> 00:23:01,182
Where are you going?

503
00:23:01,183 --> 00:23:03,935
Please don't leave me behind again.
I'm begging you to spare my life.

504
00:23:03,936 --> 00:23:05,436
I can't spend another minute

505
00:23:05,437 --> 00:23:07,563
in this boring, charmless,
decrepit place all alone! Please.

506
00:23:07,564 --> 00:23:09,440
WELL, SORRY MY APARTMENT'S UGLY…

507
00:23:09,441 --> 00:23:12,193
I'm serious, you can only stay
till someone collects you.

508
00:23:12,194 --> 00:23:13,361
Got it?

509
00:23:13,362 --> 00:23:14,612
Oh, that's right!

510
00:23:14,613 --> 00:23:16,280
You have to pay for your own food!

511
00:23:16,281 --> 00:23:17,491
More rules?

512
00:23:19,993 --> 00:23:21,745
[chuckles]

513
00:23:23,664 --> 00:23:24,665
[gasps]

514
00:23:25,833 --> 00:23:26,834
Are you ready?

515
00:23:29,503 --> 00:23:31,130
Here we go.

516
00:23:42,724 --> 00:23:44,267
Oh.

517
00:23:44,268 --> 00:23:46,645
Huh? Iroha, where'd you run off to?

518
00:23:47,271 --> 00:23:49,230
Wait! It's Yachiyo!

519
00:23:49,231 --> 00:23:50,566
You're Yachiyo, right?

520
00:23:52,442 --> 00:23:55,320
The sun has finally set
and night begins to fall.

521
00:23:58,532 --> 00:23:59,950
[gasps]

522
00:24:01,743 --> 00:24:02,870
[Yachiyo chuckles]

523
00:24:07,082 --> 00:24:10,084
Welcome to the virtual world
of Tsukuyomi, friend.

524
00:24:10,085 --> 00:24:12,545
I'm the caretaker, Yachiyo Runami!

525
00:24:12,546 --> 00:24:14,380
- This fun little fluff's FUSHI!
- [chuckles]

526
00:24:14,381 --> 00:24:17,259
Yachiyo brought Tsukuyomi to life
and created me too!

527
00:24:17,759 --> 00:24:19,677
Now, before you head out there,

528
00:24:19,678 --> 00:24:22,764
that attire is a little unbecoming,
don't you think?

529
00:24:23,390 --> 00:24:25,058
[Kaguya gasps, chuckles]

530
00:24:28,061 --> 00:24:30,980
Okay. Wow,
these clothes look super adorable!

531
00:24:30,981 --> 00:24:32,232
And I love this hairstyle.

532
00:24:32,816 --> 00:24:35,985
[Yachiyo] Perfect, I think you're ready
to join the rest of us.

533
00:24:35,986 --> 00:24:39,697
Come on. Off you go!

534
00:24:39,698 --> 00:24:41,158
[yells]

535
00:24:43,076 --> 00:24:44,077
[chuckles]

536
00:24:46,830 --> 00:24:48,999
[screams, chuckles]

537
00:24:50,500 --> 00:24:51,501
[grunts]

538
00:24:54,963 --> 00:24:55,964
Blonde, huh?

539
00:24:56,798 --> 00:24:58,549
Princess Kaguya's trendy.

540
00:24:58,550 --> 00:25:00,886
Hod up. Are you Iroha?

541
00:25:01,511 --> 00:25:03,763
- Who's that little guy?
- No way! It's InuDOGE.

542
00:25:03,764 --> 00:25:05,432
I didn't know you could come in here.

543
00:25:06,099 --> 00:25:07,267
[barks]

544
00:25:09,186 --> 00:25:10,604
[gasps]

545
00:25:12,814 --> 00:25:13,815
Let's go.

546
00:25:14,983 --> 00:25:15,984
[Kaguya] Let's go.

547
00:25:22,074 --> 00:25:24,076
[adventurous music plays]

548
00:25:39,841 --> 00:25:41,884
This is so cool!

549
00:25:41,885 --> 00:25:43,845
[FUSHI]
Congratulations on your very first login!

550
00:25:44,972 --> 00:25:47,348
In Tsukuyomi, everyone is a creator.

551
00:25:47,349 --> 00:25:49,976
If you can warm the hearts
and impress the other members,

552
00:25:49,977 --> 00:25:52,354
then the admins
will reward you with a Fuju~!

553
00:25:53,146 --> 00:25:56,190
To kick things off,
here's a welcome login bonus!

554
00:25:56,191 --> 00:25:59,193
You can also use your Fuju~
to support your favorite creators,

555
00:25:59,194 --> 00:26:01,697
who work tirelessly
to provide unlimited entertainment.

556
00:26:05,701 --> 00:26:06,702
[gasps]

557
00:26:08,620 --> 00:26:10,079
[Kaguya] Awesome sauce!

558
00:26:10,080 --> 00:26:13,207
I can't believe how much cool stuff
is in this place!

559
00:26:13,208 --> 00:26:15,002
[shrieks, chuckles]

560
00:26:15,502 --> 00:26:17,921
So happy!

561
00:26:18,547 --> 00:26:19,548
[chuckles]

562
00:26:24,052 --> 00:26:28,557
Even a poor person like me can really
enjoy everything Tsukuyomi has to offer.

563
00:26:29,433 --> 00:26:31,809
[sighs, exclaims]

564
00:26:31,810 --> 00:26:33,019
[groans]

565
00:26:33,020 --> 00:26:34,895
I can't taste it.

566
00:26:34,896 --> 00:26:38,233
They haven't been able to create
virtual taste and smell simulators.

567
00:26:38,734 --> 00:26:41,193
Don't they sell the real thing anywhere?

568
00:26:41,194 --> 00:26:43,446
Well, you can order whatever you want
and have it delivered.

569
00:26:43,447 --> 00:26:45,781
But then you have to pay for it
with real money that I don't have.

570
00:26:45,782 --> 00:26:48,826
The best I can do
is make a little money playing games.

571
00:26:48,827 --> 00:26:51,705
I don't have any special skills
to make some serious cash.

572
00:26:55,625 --> 00:26:57,627
It's time. Come on.

573
00:27:01,298 --> 00:27:02,381
[fans chattering]

574
00:27:02,382 --> 00:27:03,799
[fan 1] I can't wait!

575
00:27:03,800 --> 00:27:05,260
Ah.

576
00:27:08,096 --> 00:27:09,181
[chuckles]

577
00:27:11,016 --> 00:27:14,310
By the way, Iroha,
I talked to Yachiyo earlier.

578
00:27:14,311 --> 00:27:16,771
[shushes]
That was just the tutorial program.

579
00:27:16,772 --> 00:27:18,523
You'll see the real thing in a minute.

580
00:27:20,150 --> 00:27:21,193
[fan cheers]

581
00:27:23,612 --> 00:27:25,988
Yo! What's up, everybody?

582
00:27:25,989 --> 00:27:28,741
Let's get this party started
in Tsukuyomi tonight!

583
00:27:28,742 --> 00:27:30,743
We've got a spectacular Yachiyo concert!

584
00:27:30,744 --> 00:27:33,496
And it's being broadcast live
to all of Tsukuyomi.

585
00:27:33,497 --> 00:27:36,500
So, grab your popcorn,
because the show's about to begin!

586
00:27:37,459 --> 00:27:39,877
[all] Ten! Nine!

587
00:27:39,878 --> 00:27:41,879
Eight! Seven!

588
00:27:41,880 --> 00:27:44,549
Six! Five! Four!

589
00:27:45,050 --> 00:27:48,386
Three! Two! One!

590
00:27:48,387 --> 00:27:49,596
[gong sounds]

591
00:27:52,265 --> 00:27:53,392
Hi, everyone.

592
00:27:53,892 --> 00:27:55,060
[chuckles]

593
00:27:55,977 --> 00:27:57,061
Are you ready?

594
00:27:57,062 --> 00:27:58,896
Then let's do this.

595
00:27:58,897 --> 00:28:00,648
Did you all have a wonderful day?

596
00:28:00,649 --> 00:28:02,149
[crowd cheers]

597
00:28:02,150 --> 00:28:03,318
[exclaiming]

598
00:28:03,902 --> 00:28:04,945
[chuckles]

599
00:28:05,445 --> 00:28:06,529
Let's go!

600
00:28:06,530 --> 00:28:09,782
Tonight I'm taking you all
on a spectacular adventure!

601
00:28:09,783 --> 00:28:13,328
It'll be the trip of a lifetime!

602
00:28:15,455 --> 00:28:18,374
♪ I've waited for you ♪

603
00:28:18,375 --> 00:28:21,586
♪ Can't believe we finally met ♪

604
00:28:22,087 --> 00:28:25,548
♪ It must've been a thousand years ♪

605
00:28:25,549 --> 00:28:29,385
♪ And now I never wanna lose you ♪

606
00:28:29,386 --> 00:28:31,554
♪ So just grab my hand ♪

607
00:28:31,555 --> 00:28:36,560
♪ And don't let go ♪

608
00:28:38,311 --> 00:28:41,648
[vocalizes]

609
00:28:53,785 --> 00:28:57,413
♪ Hey now
If you listen close enough ♪

610
00:28:57,414 --> 00:29:03,210
♪ You can hear the sound of stars
Coming down all around us ♪

611
00:29:03,211 --> 00:29:07,047
♪ Hey now, come on closer
Listen up ♪

612
00:29:07,048 --> 00:29:12,511
♪ There's a brand-new world that's waiting
Where anything's possible ♪

613
00:29:12,512 --> 00:29:16,432
♪ Let's hold hands
Let's hold hands and just dance ♪

614
00:29:16,433 --> 00:29:21,061
♪ And when we hear the tune playing loud
We'll know ♪

615
00:29:21,062 --> 00:29:23,481
♪ We can sing, la, la, la ♪

616
00:29:23,482 --> 00:29:25,524
♪ Ringing out, la, la, la ♪

617
00:29:25,525 --> 00:29:30,196
♪ And even if the path to walk
Looks dark ♪

618
00:29:30,197 --> 00:29:33,658
♪ The moonlit sky
Will light the way for us ♪

619
00:29:35,327 --> 00:29:39,163
♪ I wonder if you'll see the sky ♪

620
00:29:39,164 --> 00:29:42,833
♪ If you'll smell the ocean around you ♪

621
00:29:42,834 --> 00:29:46,128
♪ Or have you paid attention all along? ♪

622
00:29:46,129 --> 00:29:48,547
♪ So no matter when ♪

623
00:29:48,548 --> 00:29:51,885
♪ And no matter where you might be ♪

624
00:29:52,385 --> 00:29:55,846
♪ You know that
I'll be watching over you ♪

625
00:29:55,847 --> 00:30:01,811
♪ Go on and count up all the days
When you laughed so hard ♪

626
00:30:01,812 --> 00:30:05,356
♪ And you
Can weave them all together now ♪

627
00:30:05,357 --> 00:30:09,777
♪ And even the thought
Of what our future will bring ♪

628
00:30:09,778 --> 00:30:15,991
♪ Is sure to have my heart singing ♪

629
00:30:15,992 --> 00:30:18,495
♪ Singing ♪

630
00:30:22,624 --> 00:30:26,753
♪ And it'll all come true ♪

631
00:30:27,379 --> 00:30:33,260
♪ I'll write my story
And journey on with you ♪

632
00:30:33,844 --> 00:30:34,845
[music ends]

633
00:30:35,428 --> 00:30:36,971
- Ah.
- [Iroha crying]

634
00:30:36,972 --> 00:30:38,974
[crowd cheering]

635
00:30:40,350 --> 00:30:41,810
Yachiyo…

636
00:30:43,061 --> 00:30:44,145
Hmm?

637
00:30:45,689 --> 00:30:47,190
[fan 2] Yachiyo!

638
00:30:49,067 --> 00:30:53,779
Yay! Sending sprinkles of gratitude
and joy with a cherry on top to you!

639
00:30:53,780 --> 00:30:57,284
[chuckles] I'm so lucky
to have such wonderful friends and fans.

640
00:30:57,909 --> 00:31:00,077
Oh! It's announcement time.

641
00:31:00,078 --> 00:31:03,581
We're hosting an exciting event
called the Yachiyo Cup!

642
00:31:03,582 --> 00:31:07,710
[FUSHI] All you awesome Tsukuyomi
streamers are eligible to participate.

643
00:31:07,711 --> 00:31:09,003
Here's your challenge.

644
00:31:09,004 --> 00:31:11,672
The streamer who gains
the most new followers in one month

645
00:31:11,673 --> 00:31:13,591
will be declared the winner!

646
00:31:13,592 --> 00:31:14,842
The prize for the winner

647
00:31:14,843 --> 00:31:18,929
will be an exclusive opportunity for
a live performance collab with Yachiyo!

648
00:31:18,930 --> 00:31:20,014
Let's work together

649
00:31:20,015 --> 00:31:23,685
to create the most breathtaking
live collab performance in the world!

650
00:31:25,687 --> 00:31:28,147
- [both chuckle]
- A collab?

651
00:31:28,148 --> 00:31:30,441
- Is this event a big deal?
- Of course it is!

652
00:31:30,442 --> 00:31:32,234
I mean, she's done collabs
with other streamers,

653
00:31:32,235 --> 00:31:34,445
but she's never
performed live with anyone before.

654
00:31:34,446 --> 00:31:37,239
- This is insane! Who's it gonna be?
- [gasps]

655
00:31:37,240 --> 00:31:39,366
Come on, Iroha. Let's compete!

656
00:31:39,367 --> 00:31:42,119
There's no way she'd perform
with nobodies like us.

657
00:31:42,120 --> 00:31:45,498
Usually these kinds of things
are prearranged anyway. It's all for show.

658
00:31:46,499 --> 00:31:48,668
- Yachiyo!
- Hmm!

659
00:31:54,007 --> 00:31:56,009
[growls]

660
00:31:59,554 --> 00:32:02,057
[fans scream]

661
00:32:04,309 --> 00:32:06,644
Yo! What up, my little rabid bunnies?

662
00:32:06,645 --> 00:32:08,312
Your Mikado has arrived!

663
00:32:08,313 --> 00:32:09,731
[crowd cheers]

664
00:32:10,440 --> 00:32:11,441
Ha!

665
00:32:12,943 --> 00:32:14,945
[dramatic music playing]

666
00:32:27,540 --> 00:32:31,168
Let's do that too. I wanna try that epic
fighting stuff just like they're doing!

667
00:32:31,169 --> 00:32:33,088
[music continues]

668
00:32:34,839 --> 00:32:37,091
[crowd cheering]

669
00:32:37,092 --> 00:32:40,011
Perfect. Another festival has begun.

670
00:32:40,553 --> 00:32:43,013
An arrow of love to your heart.

671
00:32:43,014 --> 00:32:44,599
[chuckles] Meow.

672
00:32:45,183 --> 00:32:48,310
Just end this charade and say we won, okay?

673
00:32:48,311 --> 00:32:51,271
I'll give you all a performance
that'll feel like a dream!

674
00:32:51,272 --> 00:32:54,024
[crowd cheering]

675
00:32:54,025 --> 00:32:56,652
Wow, look at all the sparkles. [chuckles]

676
00:32:56,653 --> 00:33:00,114
It's been decided.
We're gonna win this competition.

677
00:33:00,115 --> 00:33:02,783
Looking forward to that collab…
[kisses] …Yachiyo.

678
00:33:02,784 --> 00:33:04,535
Wha…

679
00:33:04,536 --> 00:33:08,581
If you win, I'll happily oblige.
But let's see what fate has in store.

680
00:33:09,165 --> 00:33:11,875
I promise it'll be
the most spectacular concert.

681
00:33:11,876 --> 00:33:13,919
So good luck to all the participants.

682
00:33:13,920 --> 00:33:17,173
Let's share the joy,
and seal it with a happily ever after!

683
00:33:17,674 --> 00:33:19,550
Happy ever after…

684
00:33:19,551 --> 00:33:21,094
[groans]

685
00:33:21,720 --> 00:33:22,721
- Hmph.
- [chuckles]

686
00:33:27,559 --> 00:33:34,523
Yachiyo!

687
00:33:34,524 --> 00:33:36,442
- [FUSHI grumbles]
- [chuckles]

688
00:33:36,443 --> 00:33:39,194
I, Kaguya, will win the Yachiyo Cup!

689
00:33:39,195 --> 00:33:41,363
That collab performance is gonna be mine!

690
00:33:41,364 --> 00:33:44,199
[muffled chatter]

691
00:33:44,200 --> 00:33:45,201
[whistles]

692
00:33:47,662 --> 00:33:49,080
What an adorable girl.

693
00:33:50,081 --> 00:33:52,709
Are you crazy? You can't just
say and do whatever you want.

694
00:33:53,460 --> 00:33:56,379
That's a wrap.
I hope you enjoyed today's concert.

695
00:33:56,880 --> 00:33:59,590
I'd love to have a quick chat
with all of you before I leave.

696
00:33:59,591 --> 00:34:01,592
- Have a good night!
- Good night!

697
00:34:01,593 --> 00:34:03,802
This event is gonna be fun.

698
00:34:03,803 --> 00:34:06,681
Later! Stay cute now,
my good little bunnies!

699
00:34:08,433 --> 00:34:10,601
[Iroha] Have you already forgotten
the promise you made?

700
00:34:10,602 --> 00:34:12,562
Iroha, let's do this together!

701
00:34:13,188 --> 00:34:16,607
- No! It's not gonna work.
- No! That's not gonna happen.

702
00:34:16,608 --> 00:34:17,733
Be nice.

703
00:34:17,734 --> 00:34:19,318
[Iroha gasps] Yachiyo?

704
00:34:19,319 --> 00:34:21,028
You forgot something.

705
00:34:21,029 --> 00:34:24,865
I'm afraid the Yachiyo Cup competition
is only open to streamers. Sorry!

706
00:34:24,866 --> 00:34:26,742
Hmm. That's right!

707
00:34:26,743 --> 00:34:28,745
Then I guess
I'll have to become a streamer!

708
00:34:29,412 --> 00:34:31,039
Let's get ready, Iroha.

709
00:34:32,957 --> 00:34:35,417
[gasps] Uh, sorry.

710
00:34:35,418 --> 00:34:38,004
- Uh, I'll be going too.
- Please wait.

711
00:34:39,589 --> 00:34:41,257
You forgot something.

712
00:34:43,468 --> 00:34:44,677
[Iroha stammers]

713
00:34:45,678 --> 00:34:47,097
- Thank you very much!
- [chuckles]

714
00:34:54,646 --> 00:34:56,648
Thank you so much for always coming here.

715
00:34:58,274 --> 00:34:59,275
Iroha.

716
00:35:01,236 --> 00:35:02,445
[keyboard clacking]

717
00:35:04,114 --> 00:35:07,074
How to become a streamer.

718
00:35:07,075 --> 00:35:08,867
Whoa, how are you blonde?

719
00:35:08,868 --> 00:35:10,494
What? You don't like it?

720
00:35:10,495 --> 00:35:11,871
Okay. [grunts]

721
00:35:15,291 --> 00:35:17,126
[Kaguya grunting]

722
00:35:17,127 --> 00:35:19,170
Nah, I like this one the best. [chuckles]

723
00:35:19,963 --> 00:35:22,465
Yep, there's no doubt about it.
She's definitely an alien.

724
00:35:22,966 --> 00:35:25,008
This is just beyond
the bounds of comprehension.

725
00:35:25,009 --> 00:35:28,262
Okay, let's see now.
What should I do as a live streamer?

726
00:35:28,263 --> 00:35:29,555
Hmm.

727
00:35:29,556 --> 00:35:32,684
I guess I could try that fighting stuff
we saw earlier. [chuckles]

728
00:35:33,268 --> 00:35:35,519
Yo, Iroha! Can you teach me that?

729
00:35:35,520 --> 00:35:37,814
- That cool fighting stuff!
- [groans]

730
00:35:39,983 --> 00:35:41,233
[groans]

731
00:35:41,234 --> 00:35:42,485
WORK, STUDY, WORK, FOOD

732
00:35:43,444 --> 00:35:45,195
- Right.
- What?

733
00:35:45,196 --> 00:35:46,739
What is this?

734
00:35:47,448 --> 00:35:48,992
[Iroha] This is my summer break schedule.

735
00:35:49,701 --> 00:35:52,077
[whimpers] You can't be serious.

736
00:35:52,078 --> 00:35:54,413
I don't see anything about playtime.

737
00:35:54,414 --> 00:35:57,333
I can't waste a single day.
So that means don't bother me.

738
00:35:58,084 --> 00:35:59,209
What?

739
00:35:59,210 --> 00:36:02,005
That's so unfair!

740
00:36:02,672 --> 00:36:04,548
Ow! Ouch!

741
00:36:04,549 --> 00:36:05,967
If you wanna live here…

742
00:36:06,551 --> 00:36:07,844
[growls]

743
00:36:08,678 --> 00:36:09,970
What is that crap?

744
00:36:09,971 --> 00:36:11,221
It's for streaming!

745
00:36:11,222 --> 00:36:13,098
Don't worry,
I got it from the dollar store.

746
00:36:13,099 --> 00:36:14,975
Check it out! Look! I started streaming.

747
00:36:14,976 --> 00:36:16,810
What do you think? [chuckles]

748
00:36:16,811 --> 00:36:17,895
HELLO FROM THE MOON!

749
00:36:17,896 --> 00:36:20,899
Yoo-hoo! Hi, everyone.
My name is Kaguya and I'm from the moon!

750
00:36:21,524 --> 00:36:24,359
I can't think of anything to do today,
so that's all for now!

751
00:36:24,360 --> 00:36:25,444
[guitar playing out of tune]

752
00:36:25,445 --> 00:36:26,988
Catch you later!

753
00:36:28,156 --> 00:36:30,324
Uh, how do you turn this off?

754
00:36:30,325 --> 00:36:32,075
[Iroha] No, no, no.

755
00:36:32,076 --> 00:36:35,954
What was that god-awful, unsettling,
cringeworthy dissonance?

756
00:36:35,955 --> 00:36:37,206
That's my jingle.

757
00:36:37,207 --> 00:36:38,624
- [humming]
- [groans]

758
00:36:38,625 --> 00:36:40,167
Stop, please.

759
00:36:40,168 --> 00:36:42,502
Hold on. How did you make that music?

760
00:36:42,503 --> 00:36:43,630
[grunts, gasps]

761
00:36:44,297 --> 00:36:45,672
Did you use my keyboard?

762
00:36:45,673 --> 00:36:47,925
You can't just take things without asking!

763
00:36:47,926 --> 00:36:51,011
Ha-ha!
You can play this, can't you, Iroha?

764
00:36:51,012 --> 00:36:53,931
I couldn't figure it out
for the life of me. [chuckles]

765
00:36:53,932 --> 00:36:56,726
Okay. I'm ready
for my first lesson, teacher.

766
00:37:00,355 --> 00:37:03,149
First of all,
there are these combinations…

767
00:37:04,859 --> 00:37:06,027
…called chords.

768
00:37:10,782 --> 00:37:13,785
[young Iroha laughing]

769
00:37:14,285 --> 00:37:15,953
[parent 1 chuckles]

770
00:37:15,954 --> 00:37:19,414
Iroha, music is something
you should enjoy freely.

771
00:37:19,415 --> 00:37:22,585
[parent 2] If you're going to play, then
you should play with a flawless intent.

772
00:37:23,836 --> 00:37:26,256
[young Iroha]
Then I don't wanna play anymore.

773
00:37:31,219 --> 00:37:33,304
[exclaims]

774
00:37:34,597 --> 00:37:35,765
[grunts]

775
00:37:40,395 --> 00:37:42,397
[playing lively song]

776
00:37:44,440 --> 00:37:46,192
[squeals]

777
00:37:48,027 --> 00:37:49,319
- Wow!
- How does that sound?

778
00:37:49,320 --> 00:37:53,198
[chuckles] That was amazing!
You're a genius!

779
00:37:53,199 --> 00:37:55,284
[chuckles] Not really.

780
00:37:55,285 --> 00:37:57,787
I can do a lot of things
but I'm not perfect.

781
00:37:58,538 --> 00:37:59,539
Oh.

782
00:38:00,248 --> 00:38:02,499
[chuckles] One more time.

783
00:38:02,500 --> 00:38:04,419
I want you to make it endless.

784
00:38:05,086 --> 00:38:07,588
[plays dramatically]

785
00:38:22,061 --> 00:38:24,438
[cheering]

786
00:38:24,439 --> 00:38:26,064
Oh, lightbulb!

787
00:38:26,065 --> 00:38:29,610
If you write me a song and I sing it,
then it'll definitely go viral!

788
00:38:30,111 --> 00:38:32,154
[chuckling]

789
00:38:32,155 --> 00:38:34,114
Write a piece for me, pretty please.

790
00:38:34,115 --> 00:38:36,491
No, a cover song will do just fine.

791
00:38:36,492 --> 00:38:37,784
No!

792
00:38:37,785 --> 00:38:43,041
I want an original piece!

793
00:38:44,083 --> 00:38:47,377
I wrote this a long time ago
at kind of a dark time in my life.

794
00:38:47,378 --> 00:38:50,464
Sorry, but I don't have any time
to write anything new for you.

795
00:38:50,465 --> 00:38:51,758
[cheers]

796
00:38:52,467 --> 00:38:53,717
Wow.

797
00:38:53,718 --> 00:38:57,012
Did you really write all of these songs?
Wowee!

798
00:38:57,013 --> 00:38:58,513
Glad you like them.

799
00:38:58,514 --> 00:39:00,475
You can just sing them however you want.

800
00:39:01,559 --> 00:39:03,436
[humming]

801
00:39:06,689 --> 00:39:10,317
♪ And now nobody can keep me down ♪

802
00:39:10,318 --> 00:39:14,613
♪ And I just can't help myself
But sing ♪

803
00:39:14,614 --> 00:39:15,822
Iroha, produce this.

804
00:39:15,823 --> 00:39:19,326
And with our powers combined
we can win the Yachiyo Cup together!

805
00:39:19,327 --> 00:39:22,245
In this old shabby apartment
begins the tale of our triumph!

806
00:39:22,246 --> 00:39:24,206
What do you mean? It's not shabby.

807
00:39:24,207 --> 00:39:27,292
- I can't.
- What? No!

808
00:39:27,293 --> 00:39:29,294
But it'll be so much fun!

809
00:39:29,295 --> 00:39:32,465
Look, I said you could stay here
as long as you don't get in my way.

810
00:39:32,965 --> 00:39:34,634
[yelling]

811
00:39:36,344 --> 00:39:38,303
Please, Iroha. I beg of you.

812
00:39:38,304 --> 00:39:39,639
Nope. Not falling for that.

813
00:39:41,391 --> 00:39:44,976
[sniffles] But I don't want our story
to end like this.

814
00:39:44,977 --> 00:39:47,814
All I ever wanted was a happy ending,
you know?

815
00:39:49,065 --> 00:39:50,775
[groaning]

816
00:39:53,486 --> 00:39:55,905
You're really making this hard to resist.

817
00:39:57,365 --> 00:39:58,740
THE ROAD TO THE YACHIYO CUP

818
00:39:58,741 --> 00:39:59,825
8910TH PLACE - KAGUYA

819
00:39:59,826 --> 00:40:01,828
[upbeat music playing]

820
00:40:06,082 --> 00:40:08,418
[no audible dialogue]

821
00:40:19,762 --> 00:40:21,263
Nah, I don't care about that.

822
00:40:21,264 --> 00:40:23,849
What's the sense in worrying?
Just move on, right?

823
00:40:23,850 --> 00:40:25,142
[yelling]

824
00:40:25,143 --> 00:40:28,478
That's the worst ending ever.
I can't handle this garbage. Damn it!

825
00:40:28,479 --> 00:40:29,855
3006TH PLACE
40594 FANS

826
00:40:29,856 --> 00:40:32,399
♪ Let's disrupt the rules
For how we live our lives ♪

827
00:40:32,400 --> 00:40:34,651
♪ Think out of the box
Color outside the lines ♪

828
00:40:34,652 --> 00:40:37,738
♪ Let's repaint the world in our design ♪

829
00:40:39,532 --> 00:40:41,741
♪ Being dull's a drag ♪

830
00:40:41,742 --> 00:40:44,120
♪ And I can't really do that ♪

831
00:40:44,620 --> 00:40:46,496
♪ I'm gonna pave my path ♪

832
00:40:46,497 --> 00:40:50,834
♪ So if you're sticking out your tongue
Then bring it on! Let's go! ♪

833
00:40:50,835 --> 00:40:51,836
DON'T YOU DARE UPLOAD THIS!

834
00:40:53,171 --> 00:40:55,840
[Iroha] For an alien,
you fit in a little too well.

835
00:40:56,883 --> 00:41:00,178
Also, I don't think Princess Kaguya
is supposed to be this cheerful.

836
00:41:00,720 --> 00:41:02,429
So, what do you wanna eat today?

837
00:41:02,430 --> 00:41:03,848
[music continues]

838
00:41:04,765 --> 00:41:06,224
[Iroha] Why am I doing this?

839
00:41:06,225 --> 00:41:07,310
It isn't like me.

840
00:41:08,227 --> 00:41:11,313
[Kaguya] ♪ I wanna know more
Get out and explore ♪

841
00:41:11,314 --> 00:41:12,814
♪ Get a taste of the world ♪

842
00:41:12,815 --> 00:41:15,484
♪ And now nobody can keep me down ♪

843
00:41:15,485 --> 00:41:18,487
♪ I just can't help myself
But sing ♪

844
00:41:18,488 --> 00:41:19,489
THIS STREAM HAS ENDED

845
00:41:22,825 --> 00:41:24,326
[chuckles]

846
00:41:24,327 --> 00:41:26,454
This new girl's totally wild.

847
00:41:27,830 --> 00:41:29,456
♪ Instead of giving up ♪

848
00:41:29,457 --> 00:41:30,874
WATASHIHA WATASHINOKOTOGA SUKI
KAGUYA

849
00:41:30,875 --> 00:41:31,876
[music stops]

850
00:41:34,128 --> 00:41:35,462
[Kaguya] Hmm…

851
00:41:35,463 --> 00:41:37,297
Your last singing stream was amazing.

852
00:41:37,298 --> 00:41:39,424
I was on the edge of my seat
the whole time.

853
00:41:39,425 --> 00:41:40,509
Totally.

854
00:41:40,510 --> 00:41:43,220
You're awesome at both video games
and singing.

855
00:41:43,221 --> 00:41:45,681
Aw, thanks. Guess I'm multitalented.

856
00:41:46,349 --> 00:41:48,642
[friend 1]
Your original song was fantastic too.

857
00:41:48,643 --> 00:41:50,269
- [friend 2] Super catchy.
- [humming]

858
00:41:50,895 --> 00:41:53,230
Hear that? I'm so happy for you.

859
00:41:53,231 --> 00:41:55,398
Wait. Did you compose that song, Iroha?

860
00:41:55,399 --> 00:41:58,527
Check out beauty and the brains
over here being all modest.

861
00:41:58,528 --> 00:42:01,321
Oh, no. I wrote that song
a really long time ago.

862
00:42:01,322 --> 00:42:03,990
Kaguya, don't put me in the spotlight.
It's unnecessary.

863
00:42:03,991 --> 00:42:05,825
It's not enough. I need to do more.

864
00:42:05,826 --> 00:42:09,371
What should I do?
I need some help. [groaning]

865
00:42:09,372 --> 00:42:12,374
Uh, well,
you've already tried so many things.

866
00:42:12,375 --> 00:42:15,794
I guess the only option left
is for Iroha to finally drop the facade

867
00:42:15,795 --> 00:42:17,295
and take off her costume.

868
00:42:17,296 --> 00:42:18,463
[yelps]

869
00:42:18,464 --> 00:42:20,674
Hey, I'm kidding. I was just kidding.

870
00:42:20,675 --> 00:42:22,008
[Kaguya] Singing is the way to go!

871
00:42:22,009 --> 00:42:24,219
Besides, all the nerds were happy too.

872
00:42:24,220 --> 00:42:25,470
[Iroha] Don't call them nerds.

873
00:42:25,471 --> 00:42:28,056
So, Iroha, can you make me a new song?

874
00:42:28,057 --> 00:42:30,016
Maybe you could sing with me too.

875
00:42:30,017 --> 00:42:33,853
I told you, I can't cut into my work
and study time any more than this.

876
00:42:33,854 --> 00:42:35,356
But you're at the beach right now!

877
00:42:36,107 --> 00:42:39,442
Hmph. True elites don't neglect their
playtime, they just work around it.

878
00:42:39,443 --> 00:42:41,861
They'll even cut back on sleep
if necessary.

879
00:42:41,862 --> 00:42:43,321
[Kaguya] That's super twisted.

880
00:42:43,322 --> 00:42:44,574
[groans]

881
00:42:45,783 --> 00:42:48,995
This is turning into
one big epic fail. [groans]

882
00:42:50,705 --> 00:42:52,622
Nobody can do this but you.

883
00:42:52,623 --> 00:42:55,709
Please help me.
I want you to create a beautiful song.

884
00:42:55,710 --> 00:42:58,587
[groaning]

885
00:42:58,588 --> 00:42:59,672
Well, I…

886
00:43:00,256 --> 00:43:02,215
All right, If I have time.

887
00:43:02,216 --> 00:43:03,842
- Let's go!
- [groaning]

888
00:43:03,843 --> 00:43:05,176
Tag team streaming sensation,

889
00:43:05,177 --> 00:43:07,888
- Kaguya and Iroha!
- Why can't I ever say no to her?

890
00:43:08,389 --> 00:43:10,724
- It's not fair.
- Iroha's a softy.

891
00:43:10,725 --> 00:43:13,144
- Didn't know she was a pushover.
- [chuckling]

892
00:43:13,811 --> 00:43:15,228
[Iroha gasps] What's with the crabs?

893
00:43:15,229 --> 00:43:17,731
- [shrieking]
- They were chilling on the rocks!

894
00:43:17,732 --> 00:43:19,984
I'm gonna gather a bunch of them
and make an army!

895
00:43:21,527 --> 00:43:23,529
- [laughs]
- [yelling]

896
00:43:25,698 --> 00:43:26,782
Uh.

897
00:43:27,450 --> 00:43:30,036
You know, Iroha seems a lot happier.

898
00:43:30,578 --> 00:43:32,037
Before Kaguya showed up,

899
00:43:32,038 --> 00:43:34,539
it seemed like she would
just fade into the background.

900
00:43:34,540 --> 00:43:35,999
[all chuckle]

901
00:43:36,000 --> 00:43:38,252
[both] What's your secret?
Did you use magic?

902
00:43:39,754 --> 00:43:41,213
- Uh.
- [both] Hmm?

903
00:43:42,506 --> 00:43:44,508
[music resumes]

904
00:43:47,928 --> 00:43:50,764
♪ Instead of giving up
When a what-if comes around ♪

905
00:43:50,765 --> 00:43:53,308
♪ I want a what-if
To be a break you found ♪

906
00:43:53,309 --> 00:43:56,311
♪ Don't you think it's a waste
Never to fly ♪

907
00:43:56,312 --> 00:43:58,313
♪ Keeping your feet on the ground ♪

908
00:43:58,314 --> 00:44:00,023
IROHA'S BUSY!
TEACH ME HOW TO GAME!

909
00:44:00,024 --> 00:44:02,485
[Iroha] Okay! Are your ready for an
awesome video game collab stream?

910
00:44:03,194 --> 00:44:05,320
Roka! Mami!

911
00:44:05,321 --> 00:44:07,198
Teach me how to play this!

912
00:44:07,698 --> 00:44:11,326
[Mami] The hottest game that everyone
is playing right now is called KASSEN.

913
00:44:11,327 --> 00:44:12,370
[grunts, gasps]

914
00:44:13,245 --> 00:44:14,329
[yelps]

915
00:44:14,330 --> 00:44:16,123
[screaming]

916
00:44:21,087 --> 00:44:22,837
- [chuckles]
- Whoa.

917
00:44:22,838 --> 00:44:24,923
[Roka]
This is basically a territory battle.

918
00:44:24,924 --> 00:44:27,676
You gotta invade one of the towers
on the left or right.

919
00:44:27,677 --> 00:44:30,595
If you can defeat the ox demon
and capture his territory,

920
00:44:30,596 --> 00:44:32,639
then you unlock a special weapon.

921
00:44:32,640 --> 00:44:34,015
[Kaguya] Here we go!

922
00:44:34,016 --> 00:44:35,935
[Roka] You gotta blast that into the keep!

923
00:44:40,648 --> 00:44:42,065
Ah!

924
00:44:42,066 --> 00:44:44,150
Wow, Kaguya!
You're a natural at this game.

925
00:44:44,151 --> 00:44:45,443
VICTORY

926
00:44:45,444 --> 00:44:46,946
VIEWS

927
00:44:50,032 --> 00:44:51,157
[Kaguya] Kaguya's pro tip.

928
00:44:51,158 --> 00:44:53,535
If you really want to enhance
the flavor of the clam broth,

929
00:44:53,536 --> 00:44:55,328
you can shuck them raw and wash them…

930
00:44:55,329 --> 00:44:56,413
MARRY ME, KAGUYA!

931
00:44:56,414 --> 00:44:57,832
[Iroha grunting]

932
00:44:59,166 --> 00:45:01,127
- [fan 1] Will you marry me?
- [fan 2] I want to marry you.

933
00:45:01,669 --> 00:45:04,463
- [fan 3] Marry me.
- [fans clamoring]

934
00:45:05,339 --> 00:45:06,798
Here's the thing,

935
00:45:06,799 --> 00:45:09,426
none of you guys have ever met me IRL.

936
00:45:09,427 --> 00:45:11,803
I'm kind of selfish
and get violent easily.

937
00:45:11,804 --> 00:45:13,472
I'm a huge pain in the butt.

938
00:45:14,098 --> 00:45:15,224
You're actually aware of that?

939
00:45:15,933 --> 00:45:17,809
I'm just an adorable little troublemaker.

940
00:45:17,810 --> 00:45:19,728
I'LL SPOIL YOU!
STEP ON ME!

941
00:45:20,479 --> 00:45:21,563
- [fan] Marry me.
- Ah-ha!

942
00:45:21,564 --> 00:45:23,982
If you can beat Iro P,
then I'll marry you!

943
00:45:23,983 --> 00:45:26,317
I'm calling it Battle For Kaguya
KASSEN Tourn…

944
00:45:26,318 --> 00:45:27,569
STREAM COMING SOON
LIKE AND SUBSCRIBE PLS!

945
00:45:27,570 --> 00:45:30,947
[groans] What the hell were you thinking?
Cancel that right now!

946
00:45:30,948 --> 00:45:32,574
Sorry I got carried away.

947
00:45:32,575 --> 00:45:34,493
Please protect me, Iro P.

948
00:45:35,244 --> 00:45:36,495
[sighs]

949
00:45:39,081 --> 00:45:40,248
[bell dings]

950
00:45:40,249 --> 00:45:41,541
[yells]

951
00:45:41,542 --> 00:45:43,376
[groaning]

952
00:45:43,377 --> 00:45:44,545
[grunts]

953
00:45:47,298 --> 00:45:50,300
[samurai 1] Watch me.
You gotta dodge and evade like this.

954
00:45:50,301 --> 00:45:51,384
[groans]

955
00:45:51,385 --> 00:45:53,721
[gamer]
What the hell's with that skin's hitbox?

956
00:45:54,638 --> 00:45:56,891
[gamer 2] Oh, no. This is gonna be bad.

957
00:45:57,391 --> 00:45:58,684
[Kaguya] Flawless victory!

958
00:46:04,523 --> 00:46:06,316
[chuckling]

959
00:46:06,317 --> 00:46:09,235
Just so you know,
this can all disappear overnight.

960
00:46:09,236 --> 00:46:10,653
It's a risky business.

961
00:46:10,654 --> 00:46:12,655
True. But it's all still legal, correct?

962
00:46:12,656 --> 00:46:13,949
[groans]

963
00:46:16,410 --> 00:46:17,411
[groans]

964
00:46:19,246 --> 00:46:21,165
At least clean up after yourself.

965
00:46:22,249 --> 00:46:25,044
[Kaguya] But cleaning is so boring.

966
00:46:28,339 --> 00:46:29,756
- [barks]
- [Iroha] Hey,

967
00:46:29,757 --> 00:46:32,258
are you really sure
you want me to go with you?

968
00:46:32,259 --> 00:46:33,344
[chuckles]

969
00:46:34,094 --> 00:46:36,847
Yeah. I-ro-ha!

970
00:46:37,556 --> 00:46:40,017
- [Iroha] What is that?
- It's our special handshake!

971
00:46:41,060 --> 00:46:43,187
You know, 'cause we're besties.

972
00:46:46,982 --> 00:46:47,983
[Iroha] Yeah.

973
00:46:51,028 --> 00:46:53,071
Huh? No! [screams]

974
00:46:53,072 --> 00:46:54,197
I died!

975
00:46:54,198 --> 00:46:56,157
- No way! Seriously?
- [groans]

976
00:46:56,158 --> 00:46:59,119
This is insane!
The developers show no mercy!

977
00:46:59,745 --> 00:47:02,498
[groans]
Will you shut the hell up and go to bed?

978
00:47:03,249 --> 00:47:04,958
Huh? What is it?

979
00:47:04,959 --> 00:47:06,418
[stammers]

980
00:47:08,837 --> 00:47:09,964
[groans]

981
00:47:12,091 --> 00:47:14,134
[Kaguya] Lookee here.
What about this place?

982
00:47:15,636 --> 00:47:18,721
[sighs] You'd go crazy
living in a place like that.

983
00:47:18,722 --> 00:47:20,098
It's so big.

984
00:47:20,099 --> 00:47:21,433
Aw!

985
00:47:24,520 --> 00:47:26,772
- [breathes heavily]
- Did you find something on the ground?

986
00:47:27,523 --> 00:47:28,524
Iroha?

987
00:47:30,025 --> 00:47:31,193
I'm okay.

988
00:47:32,653 --> 00:47:34,404
Iroha? [gasps]

989
00:47:34,405 --> 00:47:35,947
You're burning up! What's wrong?

990
00:47:35,948 --> 00:47:36,949
Iroha?

991
00:47:46,417 --> 00:47:47,876
[grunts]

992
00:47:54,717 --> 00:47:56,677
No. My shift!

993
00:47:57,177 --> 00:47:59,262
Iroha! Are you okay?

994
00:47:59,263 --> 00:48:01,389
I'm fine. I gotta get to work.

995
00:48:01,390 --> 00:48:03,225
- [gasps]
- [groans]

996
00:48:03,892 --> 00:48:06,979
I called them and said you couldn't
make it. I told them you were sick.

997
00:48:07,563 --> 00:48:10,983
Iroha, please. You have to rest.
[whimpering]

998
00:48:11,692 --> 00:48:12,775
SORRY YOU'RE SICK!
YOUR SISTER'S REALLY SWEET.

999
00:48:12,776 --> 00:48:14,611
I put a lot of fluffy items around you.

1000
00:48:14,612 --> 00:48:16,530
So you get comfy cozy, okay?

1001
00:48:20,159 --> 00:48:22,036
Thank you so much, Kaguya.

1002
00:48:22,536 --> 00:48:24,245
Oh! Hospital, hmm.

1003
00:48:24,246 --> 00:48:25,748
Let's go to the hospital, okay?

1004
00:48:27,249 --> 00:48:28,958
I can't. It costs too much.

1005
00:48:28,959 --> 00:48:31,503
Don't you worry about that.
I'll take care of it.

1006
00:48:33,005 --> 00:48:34,006
But…

1007
00:48:34,590 --> 00:48:37,051
I had everything planned out
to the last minute.

1008
00:48:37,968 --> 00:48:39,595
If I take a few days off,

1009
00:48:40,554 --> 00:48:42,348
I'll never be able to catch up.

1010
00:48:42,848 --> 00:48:44,849
And then I'll never be able to

1011
00:48:44,850 --> 00:48:46,351
get a scholarship.

1012
00:48:46,352 --> 00:48:47,353
Uh.

1013
00:48:49,104 --> 00:48:53,400
I get that. But why do you always
have to work so hard all by yourself?

1014
00:48:54,151 --> 00:48:55,778
[crying]

1015
00:48:56,278 --> 00:48:58,405
[Kaguya crying]

1016
00:48:59,365 --> 00:49:02,117
I know I asked too much of you
with the streaming.

1017
00:49:02,785 --> 00:49:03,993
Iroha,

1018
00:49:03,994 --> 00:49:06,163
- I don't want you to die.
- [chuckles]

1019
00:49:09,083 --> 00:49:10,708
So dramatic.

1020
00:49:10,709 --> 00:49:12,251
I'm not going to die.

1021
00:49:12,252 --> 00:49:15,088
But people die so easily in the movies!

1022
00:49:15,089 --> 00:49:16,674
[crying]

1023
00:49:17,841 --> 00:49:18,842
Huh?

1024
00:49:21,720 --> 00:49:26,433
[Iroha] So, when I agreed to cover both
my tuition and living expenses on my own,

1025
00:49:26,934 --> 00:49:29,143
they finally accepted my decision.

1026
00:49:29,144 --> 00:49:33,565
You make it sound so easy,
but no one else ever goes to that extreme.

1027
00:49:34,274 --> 00:49:37,860
My mom did the same thing
and she got by without any problems.

1028
00:49:37,861 --> 00:49:39,947
And there was no way
I was gonna back down.

1029
00:49:41,699 --> 00:49:44,701
I still remember the first time
I woke up in this place.

1030
00:49:44,702 --> 00:49:46,328
First time living alone.

1031
00:49:47,037 --> 00:49:50,998
There was nothing in here.
And I didn't want to rely on anyone.

1032
00:49:50,999 --> 00:49:53,626
When I decided I was going to
take care of myself,

1033
00:49:53,627 --> 00:49:55,546
it gave me this surge of energy.

1034
00:49:56,171 --> 00:49:57,172
Lucky me.

1035
00:49:57,673 --> 00:50:00,007
What are you talking about?
That's not lucky at all!

1036
00:50:00,008 --> 00:50:04,387
I bet even aliens from other planets
think your mom is totally crazy!

1037
00:50:04,388 --> 00:50:09,308
Crazy! Crazy!

1038
00:50:09,309 --> 00:50:12,396
- [groans] Crazy!
- Kaguya…

1039
00:50:13,772 --> 00:50:14,773
Huh?

1040
00:50:15,899 --> 00:50:17,316
[sighs] Sorry.

1041
00:50:17,317 --> 00:50:19,360
Why am I talking about this stuff?

1042
00:50:19,361 --> 00:50:20,778
- [pot boiling]
- Oh!

1043
00:50:20,779 --> 00:50:21,989
Oh, no!

1044
00:50:23,323 --> 00:50:26,242
Today's meal is green onion miso
with ginger and egg-rice porridge.

1045
00:50:26,243 --> 00:50:28,369
[sped-up]
First mix a ton of bonito flakes and…

1046
00:50:28,370 --> 00:50:29,871
[normal] Two eggs for more protein.

1047
00:50:29,872 --> 00:50:32,875
Make sure you blow on it before
you eat it, because it's really hot.

1048
00:50:41,467 --> 00:50:42,509
[gasps]

1049
00:50:43,093 --> 00:50:44,386
It's delicious.

1050
00:50:44,970 --> 00:50:46,013
Hmm.

1051
00:50:46,847 --> 00:50:48,390
Victory!

1052
00:50:52,728 --> 00:50:54,062
[exciting music plays]

1053
00:50:57,858 --> 00:51:00,943
What's up, Tsukuyomi fans? Otako here.
Your good, loyal doggy!

1054
00:51:00,944 --> 00:51:02,111
OTAKO THE LOYAL DOG

1055
00:51:02,112 --> 00:51:03,780
Here to bring you the latest.

1056
00:51:03,781 --> 00:51:05,907
Are you ready for an update
on the Yachiyo Cup?

1057
00:51:05,908 --> 00:51:07,825
Here are the top ten from this week.

1058
00:51:07,826 --> 00:51:09,953
Keep an eye
on the official slate for the top four.

1059
00:51:10,829 --> 00:51:12,497
Is your favorite streamer listed?

1060
00:51:12,498 --> 00:51:14,165
Now, on to the top three!

1061
00:51:14,166 --> 00:51:15,458
LET'S HAVE A WARM, COZY CHAT!

1062
00:51:15,459 --> 00:51:18,544
In third place, the idol with
the soothing voice, Nukumi Yukumo!

1063
00:51:18,545 --> 00:51:20,713
In second, the high spec elf,

1064
00:51:20,714 --> 00:51:21,923
Tereriri Tietate!

1065
00:51:21,924 --> 00:51:23,049
TETETE FOR SHORT!

1066
00:51:23,050 --> 00:51:26,552
Last but not least, as expected,
far ahead of everyone else…

1067
00:51:26,553 --> 00:51:30,640
Who's in first place?
The one and only, Black onyX!

1068
00:51:30,641 --> 00:51:32,476
1ST PLACE
BLACK ONYX

1069
00:51:33,060 --> 00:51:34,310
No competition.

1070
00:51:34,311 --> 00:51:36,437
Is it time to go home yet?

1071
00:51:36,438 --> 00:51:39,315
Thank you all so much
for your continued support.

1072
00:51:39,316 --> 00:51:42,193
Has it been decided that these
are the final top three?

1073
00:51:42,194 --> 00:51:44,487
Not just yet.
There's a brand-new team in town

1074
00:51:44,488 --> 00:51:47,114
that's crushing the competition right now.

1075
00:51:47,115 --> 00:51:48,241
Do you know who they are?

1076
00:51:48,242 --> 00:51:51,077
I'm counting on some wild shake-ups
and shifting scales.

1077
00:51:51,078 --> 00:51:53,455
I'm looking forward to the final outcome!

1078
00:51:54,414 --> 00:51:55,541
[both] Yay!

1079
00:52:01,922 --> 00:52:03,882
Hey, girl. How are you feeling?

1080
00:52:04,967 --> 00:52:05,968
I'm fine now.

1081
00:52:06,718 --> 00:52:07,885
1ST PLACE
BLACK ONYX

1082
00:52:07,886 --> 00:52:11,097
[groans] How am I supposed to
compete with them?

1083
00:52:11,098 --> 00:52:13,349
[Roka] Black onyX is tough to beat.

1084
00:52:13,350 --> 00:52:16,227
Well, of course. It's because of Mikado.

1085
00:52:16,228 --> 00:52:18,604
[groans] Mami, how could you betray me?

1086
00:52:18,605 --> 00:52:20,940
I'm rooting for you
as my second place pick.

1087
00:52:20,941 --> 00:52:24,110
I'm trying to win.
Therefore, you have to root for me only!

1088
00:52:24,111 --> 00:52:26,571
[Mami, in Japanese] ♪ To, to, to the top ♪

1089
00:52:26,572 --> 00:52:29,991
Damn it! Mikado and I
should just fight it out. Pow!

1090
00:52:29,992 --> 00:52:33,703
A match between Kaguya and Mikado
isn't a bad idea.

1091
00:52:33,704 --> 00:52:35,539
It'd be the game of the century.

1092
00:52:36,039 --> 00:52:37,248
Hell yeah! [laughs]

1093
00:52:37,249 --> 00:52:40,501
Terrible idea.
He's on a completely different level.

1094
00:52:40,502 --> 00:52:41,752
He's a pro gamer.

1095
00:52:41,753 --> 00:52:43,255
Oh, come on!

1096
00:52:43,797 --> 00:52:45,424
[grunts] Let's do it.

1097
00:52:46,091 --> 00:52:48,635
I'm putting my foot down. No, no, no!

1098
00:52:49,845 --> 00:52:51,096
Iroha, I want you to help.

1099
00:52:51,597 --> 00:52:53,973
Wait, no. No, no, no.

1100
00:52:53,974 --> 00:52:55,893
I don't want you to collapse or anything.

1101
00:52:56,435 --> 00:52:58,477
However… [groans]

1102
00:52:58,478 --> 00:53:01,273
Maybe playing a game
would be a nice break?

1103
00:53:01,773 --> 00:53:03,316
- [scoffs]
- [stammers]

1104
00:53:03,317 --> 00:53:05,903
Would you even care
if someone came and took me away?

1105
00:53:07,779 --> 00:53:10,489
Surprisingly,
no one's come to retrieve you yet.

1106
00:53:10,490 --> 00:53:12,116
[grumbles] Well, sure.

1107
00:53:12,117 --> 00:53:14,994
But you never know, they might show up
one day out of the blue!

1108
00:53:14,995 --> 00:53:17,914
[groans] I wish they'd come sooner
rather than later.

1109
00:53:17,915 --> 00:53:19,749
Please, take her away!

1110
00:53:19,750 --> 00:53:21,460
Hey! Now you're just being mean.

1111
00:53:22,586 --> 00:53:25,880
Question. How long have you been here
and you still don't know who you are?

1112
00:53:25,881 --> 00:53:27,716
- [Kaguya grunting]
- Huh?

1113
00:53:28,383 --> 00:53:31,344
[Kaguya, singsongy] Happy ending!
I need a happy ending!

1114
00:53:31,345 --> 00:53:32,970
- I need a happy ending!
- [gasps]

1115
00:53:32,971 --> 00:53:35,139
- [Iroha] I can't hear you!
- [Mami grunting]

1116
00:53:35,140 --> 00:53:37,225
…gonna be a magical happy ending!

1117
00:53:38,727 --> 00:53:39,728
Huh?

1118
00:53:40,395 --> 00:53:43,523
TO LADY KAGUYA

1119
00:53:44,066 --> 00:53:45,441
[shrieks]

1120
00:53:45,442 --> 00:53:47,276
Huh, you're kidding, right?

1121
00:53:47,277 --> 00:53:48,402
[groans]

1122
00:53:48,403 --> 00:53:50,655
MESSAGE FROM BLACK ONYX
MIKADO AKIRA

1123
00:53:50,656 --> 00:53:51,906
I'VE GOT A LITTLE PROPOSAL…

1124
00:53:51,907 --> 00:53:54,575
[Mami] Whoa, check this out.
I caught a really big one!

1125
00:53:54,576 --> 00:53:56,411
HOW ABOUT A KASSEN SHOWDOWN,

1126
00:53:58,622 --> 00:53:59,872
[commentator] Whoo-hoo!

1127
00:53:59,873 --> 00:54:02,541
Get ready!
The main event is about to begin!

1128
00:54:02,542 --> 00:54:04,835
The reigning champion, Black onyX
has challenged,

1129
00:54:04,836 --> 00:54:07,672
and proposed marriage to the rising stars
Kaguya and Iro P,

1130
00:54:07,673 --> 00:54:10,508
who have been climbing the ranks
at an unprecedented rate!

1131
00:54:10,509 --> 00:54:13,135
[Otako] Mikado's fandom
was briefly troubled by the news,

1132
00:54:13,136 --> 00:54:15,012
but brushed it off as just joking around.

1133
00:54:15,013 --> 00:54:16,639
[commentator] So, grab some popcorn,

1134
00:54:16,640 --> 00:54:18,307
because the biggest
KASSEN battle of the year

1135
00:54:18,308 --> 00:54:21,061
to decide their destiny, is happening now!

1136
00:54:24,356 --> 00:54:27,942
Hi, there.
I'm your commentator, Koto Okkoteru.

1137
00:54:27,943 --> 00:54:30,112
And I'm your good, loyal doggy, Otako!

1138
00:54:31,154 --> 00:54:32,279
[Koto] With only one hour left

1139
00:54:32,280 --> 00:54:34,907
until the results
of the Yachiyo Cup are announced.

1140
00:54:34,908 --> 00:54:37,451
[Otako] Could the results of this match
bring Kaguya and Iro P out on top?

1141
00:54:37,452 --> 00:54:38,536
43RD PLACE
KAGUYA/IRO P

1142
00:54:38,537 --> 00:54:39,996
The rules are SENGOKU,

1143
00:54:39,997 --> 00:54:42,748
a best two out of three,
with three players on each team.

1144
00:54:42,749 --> 00:54:45,460
[Koto] Right.
We're just waiting on Black onyX.

1145
00:54:46,586 --> 00:54:47,713
[all] Huh?

1146
00:54:48,755 --> 00:54:50,465
[fast-paced music plays]

1147
00:54:51,383 --> 00:54:54,302
[Koto] Wait a minute.
Where are we, on the island of ogres?

1148
00:54:57,014 --> 00:54:59,808
[Koto gasps] Whoa!

1149
00:55:00,308 --> 00:55:01,977
They were right here on the stage.

1150
00:55:06,773 --> 00:55:10,276
And Black onyX is here!

1151
00:55:10,277 --> 00:55:12,112
[crowd cheers]

1152
00:55:13,613 --> 00:55:14,947
[Mikado] Why, hello.

1153
00:55:14,948 --> 00:55:16,782
- [chuckles]
- I'm glad you're here.

1154
00:55:16,783 --> 00:55:18,701
Thank you for accepting this match.

1155
00:55:18,702 --> 00:55:21,621
Oh, uh, Mikado,
I'm a really big fan of yours.

1156
00:55:22,789 --> 00:55:24,206
MAMIMAMI

1157
00:55:24,207 --> 00:55:26,292
Mami, my apologies.

1158
00:55:26,293 --> 00:55:28,210
But I won't go easy on you.

1159
00:55:28,211 --> 00:55:29,295
[gasps]

1160
00:55:29,296 --> 00:55:31,882
He said my name.

1161
00:55:34,468 --> 00:55:35,469
[Iroha] Mami?

1162
00:55:36,053 --> 00:55:37,219
Mami!

1163
00:55:37,220 --> 00:55:40,556
So, there's my beautiful princess, Kaguya.

1164
00:55:40,557 --> 00:55:42,808
Shut up, Mikado! Get ready to fight!

1165
00:55:42,809 --> 00:55:46,104
[chuckles] I just love
your fighting stance. It's really cute.

1166
00:55:46,605 --> 00:55:48,522
Kaguya, if I win,

1167
00:55:48,523 --> 00:55:50,357
won't you please marry me?

1168
00:55:50,358 --> 00:55:53,361
[Iroha] As if!
That's never gonna happen. [yells]

1169
00:55:54,946 --> 00:55:57,239
[grunts] Feisty.

1170
00:55:57,240 --> 00:55:59,575
If Iroha says no, the answer's no!

1171
00:55:59,576 --> 00:56:02,328
[Iroha stammers] You idiot!
How many times do I have to tell you?

1172
00:56:02,329 --> 00:56:04,039
[Kaguya] Uh,
I think we should check on Mami.

1173
00:56:09,044 --> 00:56:10,628
[Iroha] No good. She's not waking up.

1174
00:56:10,629 --> 00:56:12,464
No! But we need three people!

1175
00:56:15,550 --> 00:56:17,468
Ta-da!

1176
00:56:17,469 --> 00:56:18,761
You rang?

1177
00:56:18,762 --> 00:56:21,222
Really? Yachiyo's gonna join the party?

1178
00:56:21,223 --> 00:56:22,390
[chuckles]

1179
00:56:22,974 --> 00:56:26,268
How quickly you forget.
I was on your side last time, remember?

1180
00:56:26,269 --> 00:56:27,854
[Iroha grunts]

1181
00:56:28,438 --> 00:56:29,439
Huh?

1182
00:56:30,148 --> 00:56:32,943
Let's win this game! [chuckles]

1183
00:56:37,989 --> 00:56:40,283
[Iroha] So, do we have a strategy?
What should we do?

1184
00:56:41,952 --> 00:56:46,289
Rush in like hi-yah! And then we run.
Rapid-fire moves. Bam!

1185
00:56:46,998 --> 00:56:49,292
- Yeah!
- [groans]

1186
00:56:50,001 --> 00:56:52,671
- [horn blows]
- [Koto] All right, here we go!

1187
00:56:53,964 --> 00:56:56,007
[adventurous music plays]

1188
00:57:09,312 --> 00:57:10,729
[Koto] Huh, whoa!

1189
00:57:10,730 --> 00:57:13,607
TriDEnt! It's TriDEnt!

1190
00:57:13,608 --> 00:57:16,736
Black onyX is separating
into different lanes!

1191
00:57:17,487 --> 00:57:20,990
[Otako] TriDEnt means taking on
multiple enemies all by yourself.

1192
00:57:20,991 --> 00:57:24,493
It's not something just anyone
can pull off without serious confidence.

1193
00:57:24,494 --> 00:57:26,745
Well, that's an interesting approach.

1194
00:57:26,746 --> 00:57:29,248
They're underestimating us.

1195
00:57:29,249 --> 00:57:31,168
Huh? [grunts]

1196
00:57:33,503 --> 00:57:35,421
We can't fly anymore.

1197
00:57:35,422 --> 00:57:37,424
- Let's land.
- Uh-huh.

1198
00:57:41,386 --> 00:57:43,722
[Kaguya] Wait for me!

1199
00:57:49,352 --> 00:57:50,353
[grunts]

1200
00:57:57,319 --> 00:57:58,486
[grunts]

1201
00:57:58,487 --> 00:58:00,654
[both straining]

1202
00:58:00,655 --> 00:58:02,781
So, Kaguya said your name's Iroha.

1203
00:58:02,782 --> 00:58:03,866
[Iroha] Nope.

1204
00:58:03,867 --> 00:58:05,577
Sorry, I'm afraid you're mistaken.

1205
00:58:06,203 --> 00:58:07,287
[grunts]

1206
00:58:08,663 --> 00:58:10,414
Iroha!

1207
00:58:10,415 --> 00:58:11,665
What did I say?

1208
00:58:11,666 --> 00:58:13,084
[Mikado] Wake up. Hello.

1209
00:58:13,793 --> 00:58:17,671
I really appreciate you wearing this skin.
It's way too easy to hit.

1210
00:58:17,672 --> 00:58:19,424
You sure you don't regret wearing that?

1211
00:58:20,050 --> 00:58:21,593
Come on. Show me what you got.

1212
00:58:24,721 --> 00:58:28,433
Uh, what?
Iro P actually took off her costume!

1213
00:58:28,975 --> 00:58:31,645
All right. Knew it was you.

1214
00:58:32,479 --> 00:58:34,355
I'm glad to see you're doing well.

1215
00:58:34,356 --> 00:58:36,733
Yeah. Well, it's all thanks to you!

1216
00:58:41,112 --> 00:58:44,198
Why don't you come here
and give your big brother a hug?

1217
00:58:44,199 --> 00:58:46,575
Or would you rather
have a nice pat on the head?

1218
00:58:46,576 --> 00:58:48,620
What? Big brother?

1219
00:58:49,329 --> 00:58:51,039
[fast-paced music plays]

1220
00:58:59,839 --> 00:59:02,133
There you go. Got ya!

1221
00:59:09,975 --> 00:59:13,144
Your sniping skills are truly terrifying.

1222
00:59:14,604 --> 00:59:17,607
Looks like it's impossible
to hit her the usual way.

1223
00:59:18,608 --> 00:59:20,776
[Mikado] By the way,
Mom's been worried about you.

1224
00:59:20,777 --> 00:59:22,653
You should at least contact her.

1225
00:59:22,654 --> 00:59:25,323
[Iroha] Sorry, I've been a little busy
with my own life!

1226
00:59:26,032 --> 00:59:27,866
The apple doesn't fall far from the tree.

1227
00:59:27,867 --> 00:59:30,911
You both take things too seriously.
That's why you don't get along.

1228
00:59:30,912 --> 00:59:32,956
Mom's just waiting for you to screw up.

1229
00:59:33,498 --> 00:59:35,875
Shut up! Stop trying to get in my head!

1230
00:59:38,253 --> 00:59:39,503
[Kaguya screams]

1231
00:59:39,504 --> 00:59:41,423
You should handle the situation better.

1232
00:59:46,845 --> 00:59:48,388
Just like me.

1233
00:59:49,097 --> 00:59:51,181
[Koto] Insta-kill!

1234
00:59:51,182 --> 00:59:53,810
- [Otako] That was in record time.
- [groans]

1235
01:00:01,234 --> 01:00:04,904
[Koto] Into the bottom lane,
Yachiyo has also defeated the archdemon!

1236
01:00:05,739 --> 01:00:06,948
[grunts]

1237
01:00:07,532 --> 01:00:09,618
[Koto] Noi manages to slow her down.

1238
01:00:10,118 --> 01:00:11,744
[Otako] And not a moment too soon.

1239
01:00:11,745 --> 01:00:12,870
Ow.

1240
01:00:12,871 --> 01:00:16,750
Well played, Noi. The whole time
your goal was to hold me back. [groans]

1241
01:00:18,460 --> 01:00:20,587
[Koto] Noi has taken the tower!

1242
01:00:23,965 --> 01:00:25,591
[Iroha] They took the tower?

1243
01:00:25,592 --> 01:00:26,884
We're in trouble already, aren't we?

1244
01:00:26,885 --> 01:00:27,968
- Ow!
- [grunts]

1245
01:00:27,969 --> 01:00:30,221
[Mikado] Focus, ladies.
Don't get distracted now.

1246
01:00:31,139 --> 01:00:32,848
- Too predictable.
- [Kaguya shouts]

1247
01:00:32,849 --> 01:00:33,892
You need some new moves!

1248
01:00:34,976 --> 01:00:36,645
That actually hurts, you know?

1249
01:00:40,231 --> 01:00:41,232
[strains]

1250
01:00:42,859 --> 01:00:43,860
[bell tolls]

1251
01:00:44,486 --> 01:00:46,904
[Otako] The end-of-round-one TriDEnt
is still in place,

1252
01:00:46,905 --> 01:00:48,989
and they've taken both towers. Incredible!

1253
01:00:48,990 --> 01:00:51,992
[Koto] Kaguya and Iro P
are definitely holding their own!

1254
01:00:51,993 --> 01:00:54,913
However, Black onyX is just too strong!

1255
01:00:59,125 --> 01:01:01,293
[Iroha] There's a huge gap
between our skill differences.

1256
01:01:01,294 --> 01:01:02,378
There's no chance.

1257
01:01:02,379 --> 01:01:03,587
[Yachiyo] I'm so sorry.

1258
01:01:03,588 --> 01:01:06,423
I fought like a sea slug the entire time.

1259
01:01:06,424 --> 01:01:09,343
Not at all, Yachiyo!
You're the strongest out of all of us.

1260
01:01:09,344 --> 01:01:10,470
Hmm.

1261
01:01:11,805 --> 01:01:14,057
Oh, hey, is Mikado a…

1262
01:01:15,475 --> 01:01:16,726
[dramatic music playing]

1263
01:01:18,478 --> 01:01:19,937
[Otako] Welcome to round two!

1264
01:01:19,938 --> 01:01:23,857
Black onyX has once again decided
to continue with the TriDEnt setup!

1265
01:01:23,858 --> 01:01:27,069
[Mikado] Kaguya, I know you must be
frustrated after round one,

1266
01:01:27,070 --> 01:01:30,532
but continue with this strategy,
it'll be a repeat of last time.

1267
01:01:31,157 --> 01:01:32,491
Hmm?

1268
01:01:32,492 --> 01:01:33,493
[Iroha grunts]

1269
01:01:36,746 --> 01:01:37,747
[grunts]

1270
01:01:38,415 --> 01:01:40,165
So where's Kaguya?

1271
01:01:40,166 --> 01:01:41,459
She went back to the moon.

1272
01:01:45,004 --> 01:01:46,506
[chuckles] Don't joke!

1273
01:01:47,048 --> 01:01:49,008
[Mikado] The hammer isn't exactly
a stealthy weapon.

1274
01:01:51,469 --> 01:01:52,679
Where is she?

1275
01:01:53,430 --> 01:01:54,806
Huh? Up there?

1276
01:01:55,974 --> 01:01:57,474
There we go.

1277
01:01:57,475 --> 01:01:58,601
[shouts]

1278
01:01:59,227 --> 01:02:01,396
[Mikado] Rai,
we need support in the top lane!

1279
01:02:01,980 --> 01:02:03,523
Noi's getting taken out.

1280
01:02:05,567 --> 01:02:07,652
Don't lose focus now, big brother.

1281
01:02:08,278 --> 01:02:09,779
Nice. Well done.

1282
01:02:10,447 --> 01:02:13,616
Noi's accuracy is too good.
Someone close in on him or something.

1283
01:02:16,202 --> 01:02:18,288
[shouting]

1284
01:02:32,385 --> 01:02:34,345
Now it's our turn to take the lead.

1285
01:02:35,597 --> 01:02:36,806
Till next time.

1286
01:02:37,599 --> 01:02:39,517
[both panting]

1287
01:02:49,360 --> 01:02:51,780
Just a little more to go.
We got this in the bag.

1288
01:02:53,865 --> 01:02:55,115
[breathes shakily]

1289
01:02:55,116 --> 01:02:57,035
I knew this was too much for me.

1290
01:02:59,496 --> 01:03:01,539
- [Kaguya shouts]
- [Mikado grunts]

1291
01:03:04,417 --> 01:03:06,710
[hums, laughs]

1292
01:03:06,711 --> 01:03:10,923
[Koto] Comeback!
Team Kaguya and Iro P has won round two!

1293
01:03:10,924 --> 01:03:12,341
[squeals]

1294
01:03:12,342 --> 01:03:14,718
Mikado, you really suck.

1295
01:03:14,719 --> 01:03:17,430
[Koto]
Kaguya's clever tactic actually worked!

1296
01:03:18,223 --> 01:03:19,932
[Otako] She took advantage of the fact

1297
01:03:19,933 --> 01:03:22,851
that the 2D map lacks
height and altitude data.

1298
01:03:22,852 --> 01:03:25,103
[Koto gasps] I never thought of that!

1299
01:03:25,104 --> 01:03:26,730
[laughs] Genius!

1300
01:03:26,731 --> 01:03:28,357
[Otako] Round three
will decide the winner!

1301
01:03:28,358 --> 01:03:30,735
Yay, yay, yay, yay!

1302
01:03:32,862 --> 01:03:34,947
Hats off to you, Kaguya.

1303
01:03:34,948 --> 01:03:38,617
I wonder what would've happened if
I changed my strategy in round two though.

1304
01:03:38,618 --> 01:03:42,037
Hmm. We both hate to lose,
don't we, Mikado?

1305
01:03:42,038 --> 01:03:44,498
If I were me,
why would I ever change my strategy?

1306
01:03:44,499 --> 01:03:46,416
I mean, if it isn't broke,
don't fix it, right?

1307
01:03:46,417 --> 01:03:49,670
So, have I shattered your image
of the Kaguya you see on my streams?

1308
01:03:49,671 --> 01:03:50,754
[laughs]

1309
01:03:50,755 --> 01:03:53,842
Well, you've certainly changed
my perspective.

1310
01:03:54,592 --> 01:03:56,427
- There's more to you than meets the eye.
- [Noi sighs]

1311
01:03:57,428 --> 01:03:59,681
Don't worry. We'll take care of Yachiyo.

1312
01:04:00,348 --> 01:04:03,475
[Noi grunts] You sure you can handle
this all by yourself, Mikado?

1313
01:04:03,476 --> 01:04:04,727
Yep.

1314
01:04:05,520 --> 01:04:06,813
[Noi] All righty, then.

1315
01:04:13,194 --> 01:04:15,487
[parent] So, you're the lead in this,
aren't you, Iroha?

1316
01:04:15,488 --> 01:04:17,614
That's wonderful. Lots of luck.

1317
01:04:17,615 --> 01:04:19,449
Well, I, uh…

1318
01:04:19,450 --> 01:04:23,161
Mami said she really wanted the lead,
so I said it was okay.

1319
01:04:23,162 --> 01:04:24,997
- [thud]
- [chair scrapes]

1320
01:04:24,998 --> 01:04:27,249
[parent] So you'll just give anything
away if someone asks for it,

1321
01:04:27,250 --> 01:04:28,543
even if it's important?

1322
01:04:31,921 --> 01:04:33,840
Hey, Mom. It's okay.

1323
01:04:34,424 --> 01:04:36,384
There are plenty of things
she won't give away.

1324
01:04:39,220 --> 01:04:41,681
[brother]
Mom, I'm going to Tokyo next week.

1325
01:04:42,515 --> 01:04:43,766
[Mom] Really? That sudden?

1326
01:04:44,767 --> 01:04:45,935
[brother] It's what I want.

1327
01:04:47,353 --> 01:04:48,438
[Mom] All right.

1328
01:04:52,525 --> 01:04:55,778
[young Iroha] Why'd he leave?
Now I'm gonna be all alone.

1329
01:04:57,572 --> 01:04:58,573
Why?

1330
01:04:59,157 --> 01:05:00,574
[Koto] Here we go!

1331
01:05:00,575 --> 01:05:02,326
Each team has taken a tower,

1332
01:05:02,327 --> 01:05:04,996
but the battle is getting intense
near team Kaguya's keep.

1333
01:05:16,299 --> 01:05:17,300
[groans]

1334
01:05:17,926 --> 01:05:20,385
[Mikado] Iroha gets emotional
way too easily,

1335
01:05:20,386 --> 01:05:23,181
and Kaguya's too self-centered and brash.

1336
01:05:23,765 --> 01:05:25,266
Is this over yet?

1337
01:05:26,517 --> 01:05:29,394
So, Iroha, about those weapons?

1338
01:05:29,395 --> 01:05:30,897
[Iroha] I'm totally useless.

1339
01:05:31,564 --> 01:05:33,358
But I don't want to give up!

1340
01:05:36,319 --> 01:05:37,527
Iroha!

1341
01:05:37,528 --> 01:05:38,946
Remember, you're never alone.

1342
01:05:38,947 --> 01:05:42,450
You can always rely on Kaguya and myself.
So, no worries.

1343
01:05:44,118 --> 01:05:45,535
- Mmm. Understood.
- Uh…

1344
01:05:45,536 --> 01:05:47,412
I'll leave this to you, Yachiyo.

1345
01:05:47,413 --> 01:05:49,122
[Kaguya groans]

1346
01:05:49,123 --> 01:05:53,126
Respectfully acknowledged,
and now let the festival begin!

1347
01:05:53,127 --> 01:05:55,545
Kaguya and Iro P
are closing in on a tower!

1348
01:05:55,546 --> 01:05:59,174
But what awaits them is going to be
an intense showdown with Mikado.

1349
01:05:59,175 --> 01:06:00,426
[crowd cheering]

1350
01:06:05,848 --> 01:06:07,767
Well, you took your time.

1351
01:06:08,351 --> 01:06:09,727
[Iroha] Why are you over here?

1352
01:06:10,353 --> 01:06:13,730
If you'd just attack the keep
from the middle, you would've won.

1353
01:06:13,731 --> 01:06:15,857
Come on. Where's the fun in that?

1354
01:06:15,858 --> 01:06:19,278
We wouldn't be Black onyX
if we didn't keep everyone on their toes.

1355
01:06:22,490 --> 01:06:23,658
- [Mikado grunts]
- [Iroha, Kaguya grunt]

1356
01:06:26,703 --> 01:06:28,413
[Kaguya wails]

1357
01:06:30,999 --> 01:06:32,458
[Kaguya shouts]

1358
01:06:34,919 --> 01:06:36,504
No fair! You dodged!

1359
01:06:45,430 --> 01:06:46,514
[breathing shakily]

1360
01:06:47,849 --> 01:06:49,267
[Iroha] He's too good at this.

1361
01:06:51,185 --> 01:06:52,437
Makes sense.

1362
01:06:53,021 --> 01:06:55,606
He's been playing video games
for as long as I've known him.

1363
01:06:58,651 --> 01:06:59,986
We can't win.

1364
01:07:03,948 --> 01:07:06,491
[Otako] Yachiyo, Rai, and Noi
have zero lives left,

1365
01:07:06,492 --> 01:07:08,702
which means it's game over
for those players!

1366
01:07:08,703 --> 01:07:13,081
The fate of this game now lies
in the hands of the remaining three.

1367
01:07:13,082 --> 01:07:14,958
[shouts]

1368
01:07:14,959 --> 01:07:16,377
[screams]

1369
01:07:17,795 --> 01:07:19,297
Damn it. [inhales sharply]

1370
01:07:19,922 --> 01:07:21,382
We'll still win.

1371
01:07:21,966 --> 01:07:23,050
[young Iroha grumbles]

1372
01:07:23,051 --> 01:07:24,552
[both laugh]

1373
01:07:25,136 --> 01:07:26,137
[chuckles]

1374
01:07:26,721 --> 01:07:27,847
[groans]

1375
01:07:29,140 --> 01:07:33,019
Just so we're clear on this, if we win,
you'll do whatever we want, right?

1376
01:07:33,895 --> 01:07:34,896
[scoffs]

1377
01:07:36,606 --> 01:07:37,857
[triumphant music plays]

1378
01:07:48,242 --> 01:07:49,243
[Iroha shouts]

1379
01:07:50,578 --> 01:07:52,579
They switched weapons! [laughs]

1380
01:07:52,580 --> 01:07:53,581
[Iroha grunts]

1381
01:08:00,171 --> 01:08:04,049
[Mikado] Kaguya's breakthrough power is
the only thing that can destroy the keep.

1382
01:08:04,050 --> 01:08:07,136
Therefore, Iroha will sacrifice herself
when the time comes.

1383
01:08:08,805 --> 01:08:10,972
I guess, in that case…

1384
01:08:10,973 --> 01:08:13,101
- all I gotta do is stop Kaguya.
- [Kaguya screams]

1385
01:08:14,977 --> 01:08:16,562
This game is over!

1386
01:08:17,897 --> 01:08:19,397
[Iroha] With Kaguya…

1387
01:08:19,398 --> 01:08:20,982
[Mikado grunting]

1388
01:08:20,983 --> 01:08:22,401
Where'd this wire come from?

1389
01:08:23,486 --> 01:08:25,154
Wait, Kaguya was the bait?

1390
01:08:26,280 --> 01:08:27,281
[Iroha] If it's Kaguya…

1391
01:08:28,157 --> 01:08:29,449
Iroha!

1392
01:08:29,450 --> 01:08:30,951
I know exactly what she's thinking.

1393
01:08:30,952 --> 01:08:33,079
I know her like no one else does!

1394
01:08:36,666 --> 01:08:39,127
- [crowd cheering]
- [Otako] Incredible!

1395
01:08:43,464 --> 01:08:45,007
See? I knew you could do it.

1396
01:08:47,760 --> 01:08:49,053
[Kaguya pants]

1397
01:08:50,429 --> 01:08:52,265
Iroha! [laughs]

1398
01:08:52,765 --> 01:08:54,058
We did it!

1399
01:08:54,642 --> 01:08:56,060
Nothing can stop us.

1400
01:08:56,561 --> 01:08:57,603
[Iroha] No doubt.

1401
01:08:58,146 --> 01:09:00,148
[energetic music playing]

1402
01:09:00,982 --> 01:09:02,567
[soldiers scream]

1403
01:09:03,818 --> 01:09:04,819
Oh…

1404
01:09:05,611 --> 01:09:06,612
Mm-hmm.

1405
01:09:07,196 --> 01:09:08,447
- [Kaguya shouting]
- [soldiers groaning]

1406
01:09:10,032 --> 01:09:11,284
[screams]

1407
01:09:16,747 --> 01:09:19,834
Iroha, if you're in danger, don't worry.
I'll help you out.

1408
01:09:20,668 --> 01:09:23,420
You better not make a mistake,
or I'll leave you behind.

1409
01:09:23,421 --> 01:09:24,671
Why would you do that?

1410
01:09:24,672 --> 01:09:26,841
[laughing]

1411
01:09:28,217 --> 01:09:30,845
[laughs] Let's go!

1412
01:09:31,429 --> 01:09:32,930
Those two are amazing together.

1413
01:09:33,931 --> 01:09:35,975
- [gasps]
- I'm definitely a fan for sure.

1414
01:09:37,852 --> 01:09:38,853
[Mikado grunts]

1415
01:09:39,353 --> 01:09:42,939
[Koto] Mikado is quickly dashing
toward team Kaguya's keep.

1416
01:09:42,940 --> 01:09:46,359
[Kaguya] Check out these moves.
This is my moment to shine.

1417
01:09:46,360 --> 01:09:49,488
[Koto] Looks at her go.
Kaguya's moving at the speed of light.

1418
01:09:53,284 --> 01:09:56,370
Ha-ha! I got you.

1419
01:09:57,413 --> 01:09:58,581
Uh…

1420
01:09:59,624 --> 01:10:01,041
[Koto wails]

1421
01:10:01,042 --> 01:10:02,877
It's a lightning mine trap!

1422
01:10:04,795 --> 01:10:05,962
Hmm.

1423
01:10:05,963 --> 01:10:07,797
Oh, uh… Damn it.

1424
01:10:07,798 --> 01:10:09,966
[Koto] Mikado's almost there!

1425
01:10:09,967 --> 01:10:11,636
[dramatic music plays]

1426
01:10:12,595 --> 01:10:16,223
[Koto] Yeah! What a turn of events!
The game is over!

1427
01:10:16,224 --> 01:10:19,267
The winner is Black onyX!

1428
01:10:19,268 --> 01:10:22,270
[crowd cheering]

1429
01:10:22,271 --> 01:10:23,605
Uh…

1430
01:10:23,606 --> 01:10:26,692
[wails] We lost! No fair.

1431
01:10:27,360 --> 01:10:28,443
[whimpers]

1432
01:10:28,444 --> 01:10:32,030
Hold on. The results of
the Yachiyo Cup aren't final.

1433
01:10:32,031 --> 01:10:33,074
Who will win?

1434
01:10:40,957 --> 01:10:43,042
[Yachiyo] What a good game, everyone.

1435
01:10:44,085 --> 01:10:47,212
I had so much fun playing KASSEN with you,

1436
01:10:47,213 --> 01:10:49,089
but the night isn't over yet.

1437
01:10:49,090 --> 01:10:51,007
It's the moment
you've all been waiting for,

1438
01:10:51,008 --> 01:10:52,550
and here we go!

1439
01:10:52,551 --> 01:10:55,888
The lucky streamer
collaborating with me is…

1440
01:10:57,223 --> 01:10:59,474
Drumroll, please…

1441
01:10:59,475 --> 01:11:00,643
- [drumroll begins]
- [chuckles]

1442
01:11:03,104 --> 01:11:06,231
[Yachiyo] This talented streamer gained
the most followers throughout the event.

1443
01:11:06,232 --> 01:11:07,607
YACHIYO CUP RESULTS!

1444
01:11:07,608 --> 01:11:08,776
[drumroll continues]

1445
01:11:10,111 --> 01:11:11,362
[Yachiyo] Who will it be?

1446
01:11:11,946 --> 01:11:14,282
The anticipation is killing me.

1447
01:11:14,907 --> 01:11:19,120
The winner of the Yachiyo Cup is…

1448
01:11:25,876 --> 01:11:28,503
Kaguya and Iro P!

1449
01:11:28,504 --> 01:11:33,216
Congratulations!

1450
01:11:33,217 --> 01:11:35,928
[crowd cheering]

1451
01:11:37,930 --> 01:11:40,141
What? Didn't we lose though?

1452
01:11:40,766 --> 01:11:42,225
I guess not.

1453
01:11:42,226 --> 01:11:44,394
[squeals, laughs]

1454
01:11:44,395 --> 01:11:45,478
We did it!

1455
01:11:45,479 --> 01:11:48,816
[gasps] I can't believe we won.

1456
01:11:52,653 --> 01:11:55,405
Yay! Iroha!

1457
01:11:55,406 --> 01:11:57,490
- This is all thanks to you!
- [gasps]

1458
01:11:57,491 --> 01:12:00,328
What? No. It was all you.

1459
01:12:00,911 --> 01:12:02,871
[viewer 1] O-M-G, Iro P is the GOAT!

1460
01:12:02,872 --> 01:12:05,415
[viewer 2] She was awesome.
I'm so glad I followed her.

1461
01:12:05,416 --> 01:12:07,500
[viewer 3] Wait,
she writes songs for Kaguya too?

1462
01:12:07,501 --> 01:12:09,544
- [viewer 1] For reals?
- [viewer 2] I just love her smile.

1463
01:12:09,545 --> 01:12:11,047
- [chuckles]
- I'm a huge fan now.

1464
01:12:12,048 --> 01:12:16,551
[crowd chanting] Iro P! Kaguya!
Iro P! Kaguya!

1465
01:12:16,552 --> 01:12:18,595
I can't wait to sing with you.

1466
01:12:18,596 --> 01:12:24,017
[crowd chanting] Iro P! Kaguya!
Iro P! Kaguya!

1467
01:12:24,018 --> 01:12:26,102
Gross.
We don't have to get married, do we?

1468
01:12:26,103 --> 01:12:27,313
Uh…

1469
01:12:29,273 --> 01:12:30,274
Hmm.

1470
01:12:31,525 --> 01:12:34,152
It's funny,
this doesn't feel like a victory.

1471
01:12:34,153 --> 01:12:36,154
- Uh… Hmm.
- Uh…

1472
01:12:36,155 --> 01:12:37,489
[chuckles] Well, don't worry.

1473
01:12:37,490 --> 01:12:40,158
I never planned on marrying you
in the first place.

1474
01:12:40,159 --> 01:12:41,577
I knew it all along.

1475
01:12:42,286 --> 01:12:43,287
[chuckles]

1476
01:12:44,080 --> 01:12:46,414
So? Iroha, what was your wish?

1477
01:12:46,415 --> 01:12:48,125
Wait, are you serious?

1478
01:12:48,626 --> 01:12:51,336
I, um… I want to move to a bigger place.

1479
01:12:51,337 --> 01:12:54,798
So, I was wondering if you could be
my co-signer.

1480
01:12:54,799 --> 01:12:56,800
Sure you don't want me to buy you a house?

1481
01:12:56,801 --> 01:12:58,343
- Uh…
- I want a house. [groans]

1482
01:12:58,344 --> 01:13:00,387
You rich kids are all the same.

1483
01:13:00,388 --> 01:13:01,931
Thanks, but no thanks.

1484
01:13:02,890 --> 01:13:05,725
All righty, then. See you later.

1485
01:13:05,726 --> 01:13:07,645
I'm gonna go chat with my fans.

1486
01:13:11,315 --> 01:13:14,025
Did you really mean it?
We're getting a bigger place?

1487
01:13:14,026 --> 01:13:17,278
Of course. You keep buying more stuff,
and we have no room.

1488
01:13:17,279 --> 01:13:18,696
A new home!

1489
01:13:18,697 --> 01:13:21,408
- [Yachiyo] Just the girls I'm looking for.
- [Kaguya, Iroha exclaim]

1490
01:13:21,409 --> 01:13:22,451
- [laughs]
- [both grunt]

1491
01:13:23,285 --> 01:13:25,537
Good job. Congratulations.

1492
01:13:25,538 --> 01:13:29,916
Not bad out there,
but if you ask me, you just got lucky.

1493
01:13:29,917 --> 01:13:32,752
- [chuckles] Alley-oop.
- [screams] Stop it.

1494
01:13:32,753 --> 01:13:34,921
- [exclaiming]
- [grunts] Put me down.

1495
01:13:34,922 --> 01:13:37,841
Iroha, Kaguya, you were very impressive.

1496
01:13:37,842 --> 01:13:40,010
[chuckles, sighs]

1497
01:13:40,719 --> 01:13:43,847
Nah, my skills were so weak
compared to yours.

1498
01:13:43,848 --> 01:13:46,099
Yachiyo, how can I learn to move like you?

1499
01:13:46,100 --> 01:13:50,019
Practice makes perfect, as they say.
You just have to get out there and do it.

1500
01:13:50,020 --> 01:13:52,648
- Ebb and flow like the waves of the ocean.
- [whimpers]

1501
01:13:53,190 --> 01:13:55,733
You're perfect,
so that's easy for you to say.

1502
01:13:55,734 --> 01:13:57,152
Uh… [chuckles]

1503
01:13:57,153 --> 01:14:00,947
I'm not perfect. One of my weaknesses is
I can be very indecisive.

1504
01:14:00,948 --> 01:14:04,742
But you're strong. The reason
you're strong is because you're Kaguya.

1505
01:14:04,743 --> 01:14:06,494
And Kaguya is strong.

1506
01:14:06,495 --> 01:14:08,455
Sorry, not following ya.

1507
01:14:08,456 --> 01:14:11,041
- [grunts] Stop poking me. Let me go.
- [chuckles]

1508
01:14:12,835 --> 01:14:16,588
Now then,
as we reach the climax of our story,

1509
01:14:16,589 --> 01:14:19,174
from here on out,
things might get a little intense.

1510
01:14:19,175 --> 01:14:22,052
I sincerely hope you'll follow our tale
to the very end.

1511
01:14:23,554 --> 01:14:25,013
Yo!

1512
01:14:25,014 --> 01:14:28,349
Are you both prepared to be tossed around
by the tidal waves of fate?

1513
01:14:28,350 --> 01:14:30,101
Yeah! [exclaims]

1514
01:14:30,102 --> 01:14:31,687
- [chuckles]
- Ah…

1515
01:14:32,771 --> 01:14:34,023
Time for bed.

1516
01:14:36,275 --> 01:14:39,195
[giggles, yawns]

1517
01:14:40,279 --> 01:14:42,990
Good night. See you later.

1518
01:14:49,371 --> 01:14:51,040
Is this reality?

1519
01:14:51,749 --> 01:14:53,209
Virtual reality!

1520
01:14:56,921 --> 01:14:59,215
[gasps]

1521
01:15:03,010 --> 01:15:04,720
All right, meet you over there.

1522
01:15:10,267 --> 01:15:12,269
[energetic music playing]

1523
01:15:14,522 --> 01:15:15,814
- You got it?
- Yup.

1524
01:15:16,565 --> 01:15:19,108
There, the fridge can go
in the back of the kitchen.

1525
01:15:19,109 --> 01:15:20,193
'Kay.

1526
01:15:20,194 --> 01:15:21,779
[exclaiming, laughing]

1527
01:15:24,823 --> 01:15:27,992
I feel fantastic,
like everything is perfect, you know?

1528
01:15:27,993 --> 01:15:30,328
[Iroha]
Meanwhile, I'm one big stress ball.

1529
01:15:30,329 --> 01:15:32,081
[chuckles]

1530
01:15:33,666 --> 01:15:38,003
Wow! This is amazing! [laughs]

1531
01:15:45,719 --> 01:15:47,179
MATH I+A

1532
01:15:48,889 --> 01:15:49,890
[sighs]

1533
01:15:51,267 --> 01:15:53,476
We ran out of shampoo,
so I'm gonna run to the store.

1534
01:15:53,477 --> 01:15:55,728
I want to go with you
'cause I'll be lonely!

1535
01:15:55,729 --> 01:15:58,856
Mmm. Oh, no. We still have
a ton of unpacking to do.

1536
01:15:58,857 --> 01:16:00,650
[groans]

1537
01:16:00,651 --> 01:16:04,279
PANCAKE MIX

1538
01:16:04,280 --> 01:16:05,780
I should get that for her.

1539
01:16:05,781 --> 01:16:08,616
[grunts] No, no, wait a minute.
What am I thinking?

1540
01:16:08,617 --> 01:16:09,867
Iroha!

1541
01:16:09,868 --> 01:16:12,412
Kaguya, where did you come from? [groans]

1542
01:16:12,413 --> 01:16:14,707
Bored without you,
so I wanted to come find you.

1543
01:16:18,961 --> 01:16:21,963
Hey, hey… [laughs]

1544
01:16:21,964 --> 01:16:23,965
What are you doing?
Stop it, that's dangerous!

1545
01:16:23,966 --> 01:16:27,468
- [both clamor, shout]
- ♪ Happy synthesizer, hear it now ♪

1546
01:16:27,469 --> 01:16:29,470
♪ I'll make a joyful melody ♪

1547
01:16:29,471 --> 01:16:31,431
♪ I'll play it for you ♪

1548
01:16:31,432 --> 01:16:33,057
♪ You don't need to wear a brave face ♪

1549
01:16:33,058 --> 01:16:34,809
- Wah!
- ♪ You don't need to hide from me ♪

1550
01:16:34,810 --> 01:16:38,771
♪ All you have to do is be
The person you are ♪

1551
01:16:38,772 --> 01:16:41,399
♪ I'm not that smart or talented
But there's one thing I can do ♪

1552
01:16:41,400 --> 01:16:42,483
Yummy!

1553
01:16:42,484 --> 01:16:45,486
♪ So whatever it's worth
I'll do it for you ♪

1554
01:16:45,487 --> 01:16:47,322
Let's go, Kaguya! Number one!

1555
01:16:47,323 --> 01:16:49,866
Ten more and I'll be the best!

1556
01:16:49,867 --> 01:16:51,869
[both laughing]

1557
01:16:53,996 --> 01:16:56,998
IROHA

1558
01:16:56,999 --> 01:16:58,667
- [grunting]
- [game beeps]

1559
01:16:59,335 --> 01:17:00,544
- Mmm?
- [footsteps approaching]

1560
01:17:01,462 --> 01:17:04,881
Iroha, what's this?

1561
01:17:04,882 --> 01:17:07,551
Mmm, stop snooping through my files.

1562
01:17:08,552 --> 01:17:09,636
Uh…

1563
01:17:09,637 --> 01:17:11,554
- UNTITLED (COLLAB WITH IROHA).
- WAV

1564
01:17:11,555 --> 01:17:14,892
It looks like it's only half done.
Where's the rest?

1565
01:17:15,643 --> 01:17:18,729
Sorry.
I don't have any free time to finish this.

1566
01:17:20,064 --> 01:17:22,982
Never mind that. Tomorrow's the big day.

1567
01:17:22,983 --> 01:17:24,276
We should get some sleep.

1568
01:17:25,069 --> 01:17:27,695
It's not fair, the songs for the concert
are super hard,

1569
01:17:27,696 --> 01:17:30,657
but since Yachiyo's AI,
she can handle them no problem.

1570
01:17:30,658 --> 01:17:31,741
Mmm.

1571
01:17:31,742 --> 01:17:35,578
So much has happened since you arrived
that I can barely keep up with it all.

1572
01:17:35,579 --> 01:17:38,831
Iroha, are you sure you're gonna be
okay with tomorrow's schedule?

1573
01:17:38,832 --> 01:17:39,833
Uh…

1574
01:17:41,960 --> 01:17:44,295
Well, if it's just this once.

1575
01:17:44,296 --> 01:17:46,131
CONCERT
MOCK EXAM

1576
01:17:50,511 --> 01:17:51,803
- [giggles]
- Ugh…

1577
01:17:51,804 --> 01:17:54,639
For real? What's the point
in having separate rooms?

1578
01:17:54,640 --> 01:17:57,142
Why me? [chuckles]

1579
01:18:03,857 --> 01:18:07,360
[trills] Crab! [trills] Rabbit!

1580
01:18:07,361 --> 01:18:09,697
Oh, yeah. That's really cute. Adorable.

1581
01:18:10,280 --> 01:18:12,657
All this practicing is making me hungry.

1582
01:18:12,658 --> 01:18:14,992
Do you want to get some pancakes
when the concert's done?

1583
01:18:14,993 --> 01:18:16,327
Uh… Hmm.

1584
01:18:16,328 --> 01:18:19,622
That sounds like a good idea.
I was too nervous to eat today.

1585
01:18:19,623 --> 01:18:21,624
[trills] A loach!

1586
01:18:21,625 --> 01:18:23,584
- Uh…
- Sorry for the wait.

1587
01:18:23,585 --> 01:18:27,422
Pancakes sound absolutely delicious!
I'd love to have some too!

1588
01:18:27,423 --> 01:18:28,881
You wanna eat with us?

1589
01:18:28,882 --> 01:18:30,925
[chuckles] Oh, my, my…

1590
01:18:30,926 --> 01:18:33,594
I'm a performer
who only exists in the digital seas,

1591
01:18:33,595 --> 01:18:34,762
so, alas, I don't eat.

1592
01:18:34,763 --> 01:18:37,098
No! What kind of torture is that?

1593
01:18:37,099 --> 01:18:39,977
There's no way I'd be able to handle that!

1594
01:18:42,855 --> 01:18:45,232
Now then, shall we go?

1595
01:18:45,816 --> 01:18:47,735
- [breathing heavily]
- [giggles] Oh?

1596
01:18:48,235 --> 01:18:49,862
[exhales deeply] Hmm.

1597
01:18:50,362 --> 01:18:52,406
- [gasps, laughs]
- Oh.

1598
01:18:56,285 --> 01:18:57,369
[Kaguya] Hmm.

1599
01:19:12,926 --> 01:19:15,386
I still get nervous
every time I'm up here.

1600
01:19:15,387 --> 01:19:16,638
It's the atmosphere.

1601
01:19:19,933 --> 01:19:21,184
Yachiyo.

1602
01:19:21,185 --> 01:19:22,770
Yes, what's on your mind?

1603
01:19:23,520 --> 01:19:27,940
Your debut song, "Remember,"
why don't you sing it anymore?

1604
01:19:27,941 --> 01:19:29,192
[chuckles]

1605
01:19:29,193 --> 01:19:32,612
That song's job is already done.
It's found its proper place.

1606
01:19:32,613 --> 01:19:33,614
[gasps]

1607
01:19:34,448 --> 01:19:36,617
- Ready? It's time!
- [Kaguya squeals]

1608
01:19:37,534 --> 01:19:39,327
[crowd cheering]

1609
01:19:39,328 --> 01:19:41,245
[Yachiyo] Hi, everyone!

1610
01:19:41,246 --> 01:19:43,624
Tell me, how's it going out there?

1611
01:19:45,667 --> 01:19:47,294
Is life treating you well?

1612
01:19:48,045 --> 01:19:50,296
Or do you maybe feel like crying?

1613
01:19:50,297 --> 01:19:51,714
[audience member 1] We love you so much!

1614
01:19:51,715 --> 01:19:55,219
There, there. It'll be okay.

1615
01:19:56,053 --> 01:19:57,930
Even if the journey gets lonely,

1616
01:19:58,639 --> 01:20:02,643
the memories of happier times
will light your way and guide your path.

1617
01:20:03,143 --> 01:20:04,144
[chuckles]

1618
01:20:04,770 --> 01:20:08,649
I want to make this
a memory you will never forget.

1619
01:20:10,025 --> 01:20:12,736
So please, will you dance with me?

1620
01:20:15,280 --> 01:20:19,283
♪ You know that I'm
The world's number-one best princess ♪

1621
01:20:19,284 --> 01:20:21,619
- ♪ That's how you need to treat me ♪
- [Kaguya giggles]

1622
01:20:21,620 --> 01:20:25,874
♪ 'Cause you gotta be obsessed ♪

1623
01:20:27,543 --> 01:20:28,752
♪ Got it? ♪

1624
01:20:43,851 --> 01:20:47,270
♪ Number 1, you gotta notice
When I come into the room ♪

1625
01:20:47,271 --> 01:20:48,604
♪ With a different hairdo ♪

1626
01:20:48,605 --> 01:20:52,400
♪ Number 2, you've got to notice
When I get cute, new shoes ♪

1627
01:20:52,401 --> 01:20:54,527
♪ Number 3
You gotta say some special things to me ♪

1628
01:20:54,528 --> 01:20:56,904
♪ Just a little talking sweet
Is all you gotta do ♪

1629
01:20:56,905 --> 01:20:58,406
♪ If you understand ♪

1630
01:20:58,407 --> 01:21:00,992
♪ I don't know what you're waiting for
Boy, just grab my hand ♪

1631
01:21:00,993 --> 01:21:02,326
Hey, come on!

1632
01:21:02,327 --> 01:21:03,578
♪ And it's not like I'm selfish ♪

1633
01:21:03,579 --> 01:21:05,329
♪ I just want a little bit of spice ♪

1634
01:21:05,330 --> 01:21:08,374
♪ I want you to think
That I'm the cutest girl ♪

1635
01:21:08,375 --> 01:21:10,878
♪ That you've ever seen
In all of your life ♪

1636
01:21:11,712 --> 01:21:16,424
Hey, hey, it's okay if you love me
more than anyone else in the world!

1637
01:21:16,425 --> 01:21:20,636
♪ You know that I'm
The world's number-one best princess ♪

1638
01:21:20,637 --> 01:21:23,014
♪ Notice me
Hey, hey, hey, hey! ♪

1639
01:21:23,015 --> 01:21:24,599
♪ You better not make a girl wait ♪

1640
01:21:24,600 --> 01:21:28,269
♪ Number 1, for sure
You better bet that I'm ready to go ♪

1641
01:21:28,270 --> 01:21:30,688
- ♪ Are you listening? ♪
- [Kaguya vocalizes, laughs]

1642
01:21:30,689 --> 01:21:34,902
♪ I got an appetite for something sweet ♪

1643
01:21:36,403 --> 01:21:37,738
♪ You know I want it now! ♪

1644
01:21:41,116 --> 01:21:42,159
[Yachiyo] Yeah!

1645
01:21:44,244 --> 01:21:45,829
Hey, baby

1646
01:21:46,413 --> 01:21:49,290
- [Yachiyo] This next one's a new song.
- [Kaguya] Here we go!

1647
01:21:49,291 --> 01:21:50,292
[crowd cheering]

1648
01:21:52,711 --> 01:21:53,794
Breakdown!

1649
01:21:53,795 --> 01:21:54,796
[song ends]

1650
01:21:55,547 --> 01:21:57,341
["Ex-Otogibanashi" plays]

1651
01:22:02,971 --> 01:22:06,307
♪ There's a story that's told
And it's as old as time ♪

1652
01:22:06,308 --> 01:22:08,017
♪ Everybody knows ♪

1653
01:22:08,018 --> 01:22:12,189
♪ Kaguya, the princess
She herself was the one who had said it ♪

1654
01:22:13,148 --> 01:22:17,361
♪ I don't want it to end like that
I refuse for it to end that way ♪

1655
01:22:18,195 --> 01:22:19,946
♪ Would you just nod your head ♪

1656
01:22:19,947 --> 01:22:22,282
♪ And sit back
And accept that it's only fate? ♪

1657
01:22:23,200 --> 01:22:28,245
♪ It's not a story someone wrote
'Cause your life is up to you ♪

1658
01:22:28,246 --> 01:22:33,376
♪ You can write your own
Only you and me ♪

1659
01:22:33,377 --> 01:22:38,089
♪ It's a journey we go through
It's nostalgic and it's new ♪

1660
01:22:38,090 --> 01:22:42,636
♪ That's the kind
Kind of song that we sing ♪

1661
01:22:43,470 --> 01:22:46,222
♪ I pictured this year with you
Before a million times ♪

1662
01:22:46,223 --> 01:22:49,058
♪ But you know it's still
My sweetest memory ♪

1663
01:22:49,059 --> 01:22:51,352
♪ Seven sparkling colors shining bright ♪

1664
01:22:51,353 --> 01:22:54,105
♪ Lighting up our special, sweet fantasy ♪

1665
01:22:54,106 --> 01:22:56,399
♪ Yeah, you know it, I'm the heroine ♪

1666
01:22:56,400 --> 01:22:59,110
♪ And I'll pierce your heart
With the strongest melody ♪

1667
01:22:59,111 --> 01:23:01,612
♪ Don't pretend you don't know who I am ♪

1668
01:23:01,613 --> 01:23:04,198
♪ Say my name, say my name
'Cause I deserve the fame ♪

1669
01:23:04,199 --> 01:23:06,743
♪ I'm the best
I'm the princess every single day! ♪

1670
01:23:07,494 --> 01:23:09,954
♪ Hey, you only get one go around ♪

1671
01:23:09,955 --> 01:23:12,498
♪ So you better live
Right here, right now ♪

1672
01:23:12,499 --> 01:23:14,500
- ♪ Now ♪
- [Kaguya giggles]

1673
01:23:14,501 --> 01:23:17,004
♪ We only get one life, you know ♪

1674
01:23:17,587 --> 01:23:22,758
♪ And for forever I waited
For this very opportunity ♪

1675
01:23:22,759 --> 01:23:27,305
♪ It's the sweet fantasy ♪

1676
01:23:28,390 --> 01:23:31,100
♪ 'Cause that's me ♪

1677
01:23:31,101 --> 01:23:33,894
♪ It's the sweet ♪

1678
01:23:33,895 --> 01:23:40,861
♪ Fantasy ♪

1679
01:23:41,695 --> 01:23:42,778
[song ends]

1680
01:23:42,779 --> 01:23:45,072
- [crowd cheering]
- [audience member 2] Yachiyo!

1681
01:23:45,073 --> 01:23:46,658
[audience member 3] Kaguya!

1682
01:23:47,367 --> 01:23:49,369
[both panting]

1683
01:23:52,372 --> 01:23:55,834
[chuckles] Oh, man. That was awesome.

1684
01:23:56,418 --> 01:23:58,127
Iroha, love you.

1685
01:23:58,128 --> 01:23:59,587
You what?

1686
01:23:59,588 --> 01:24:03,174
You know,
I think maybe I should just marry you.

1687
01:24:03,175 --> 01:24:04,676
Wha…

1688
01:24:06,678 --> 01:24:07,679
- [giggles]
- No, then?

1689
01:24:08,638 --> 01:24:11,724
I guess, if you pay half the rent
and bills and stuff,

1690
01:24:11,725 --> 01:24:13,809
I don't mind us living together.

1691
01:24:13,810 --> 01:24:15,062
Wait, really?

1692
01:24:18,148 --> 01:24:20,150
[thunder rumbling]

1693
01:24:22,402 --> 01:24:23,862
[mysterious music playing]

1694
01:24:27,407 --> 01:24:29,200
[bystander 1] The Internet went out.

1695
01:24:29,201 --> 01:24:30,202
[bystander 2] What is that?

1696
01:24:35,791 --> 01:24:37,208
- [shouts]
- [exclaiming]

1697
01:24:37,209 --> 01:24:38,210
Uh, I'm sorry.

1698
01:24:44,883 --> 01:24:46,842
Uh… [gasps, groans]

1699
01:24:46,843 --> 01:24:48,845
[crowd gasping, shouting]

1700
01:24:53,266 --> 01:24:54,434
[Iroha] Huh, what are those?

1701
01:24:59,314 --> 01:25:00,607
Uh… [gasps]

1702
01:25:02,025 --> 01:25:03,110
Kaguya!

1703
01:25:03,735 --> 01:25:04,861
[gasps]

1704
01:25:22,462 --> 01:25:25,257
Come on, now. That's no way to behave.

1705
01:25:27,884 --> 01:25:30,178
We are sorry.

1706
01:25:32,639 --> 01:25:34,558
- [crowd exclaiming]
- [gasps]

1707
01:25:35,350 --> 01:25:38,520
You really never know
what's going to happen next!

1708
01:25:39,062 --> 01:25:41,981
- So stay tuned for more updates.
- That's part of the show?

1709
01:25:41,982 --> 01:25:45,734
- I don't know.
- I guess Yachiyo loves a show.

1710
01:25:45,735 --> 01:25:49,113
[giggles] Hey, I hope you all
enjoyed the performance.

1711
01:25:49,114 --> 01:25:50,657
- [Kaguya] Uh…
- [crowd cheering]

1712
01:25:51,449 --> 01:25:53,660
[gasps] Yachiyo, what was that?

1713
01:25:54,369 --> 01:25:55,619
Hmm.

1714
01:25:55,620 --> 01:25:59,623
It's possible it was a glitch
or just some kids messing around?

1715
01:25:59,624 --> 01:26:01,418
I'll look into it!

1716
01:26:04,713 --> 01:26:06,173
And in other news,

1717
01:26:07,132 --> 01:26:10,593
Tachikawa City, Tokyo experienced
a widespread failure…

1718
01:26:10,594 --> 01:26:11,886
- I…
- …of communication devices

1719
01:26:11,887 --> 01:26:13,555
at 10:00 p.m. this evening.

1720
01:26:14,347 --> 01:26:16,558
- I can't believe the concert's over.
- Hmm.

1721
01:26:17,142 --> 01:26:21,020
Yeah, but there are still lots and lots
of things that I want to do,

1722
01:26:21,021 --> 01:26:23,982
and more ingredients
are getting delivered tomorrow!

1723
01:26:24,608 --> 01:26:26,568
Such a greedy little monster.

1724
01:26:27,777 --> 01:26:30,154
- [roars]
- [chuckles]

1725
01:26:30,155 --> 01:26:31,405
The hijacking will be investigated…

1726
01:26:31,406 --> 01:26:32,573
MYSTERY NETWORK OUTAGE

1727
01:26:32,574 --> 01:26:33,908
You feeling okay?

1728
01:26:33,909 --> 01:26:35,284
TACHIKAWA, TOKYO

1729
01:26:35,285 --> 01:26:37,244
- Several surveillance cameras…
- [Kaguya] I'm just tired, that's all.

1730
01:26:37,245 --> 01:26:38,913
…recorded the same eerie footage.

1731
01:26:38,914 --> 01:26:40,915
Good night!

1732
01:26:40,916 --> 01:26:44,293
[anchor] This strange image of the moon
was recorded from a digital sign in town.

1733
01:26:44,294 --> 01:26:46,420
- [sighs]
- Citizens who were wearing smart contacts…

1734
01:26:46,421 --> 01:26:48,255
MOM - MISSED CALLS (10)

1735
01:26:48,256 --> 01:26:50,382
…have reported their concern
after witnessing…

1736
01:26:50,383 --> 01:26:51,718
"What I want to do…"

1737
01:26:52,427 --> 01:26:54,262
[anchor] Stay tuned for the weather…

1738
01:27:02,604 --> 01:27:04,855
- What on earth is that?
- Hmm?

1739
01:27:04,856 --> 01:27:09,068
Sweet sea bream!
Is it okay if I grill it over charcoal?

1740
01:27:09,069 --> 01:27:10,320
Not okay.

1741
01:27:10,820 --> 01:27:12,572
[sighs] I'm going out for a while.

1742
01:27:13,573 --> 01:27:16,493
[Kaguya] Hmm? Have fun!

1743
01:27:17,285 --> 01:27:18,453
See you later.

1744
01:27:21,206 --> 01:27:22,665
[door closes]

1745
01:27:22,666 --> 01:27:23,750
Hmm.

1746
01:27:24,251 --> 01:27:25,252
Hmm.

1747
01:27:26,544 --> 01:27:27,754
[gasps]

1748
01:27:32,384 --> 01:27:33,385
Hmm?

1749
01:27:34,219 --> 01:27:36,762
The same goes for,
"su," "sasu," and "shimu."

1750
01:27:36,763 --> 01:27:40,308
They can all be used to mean something
that is outside of one's own control.

1751
01:27:40,850 --> 01:27:44,437
For example, in the case of
"se tamou" or "rare tamou"…

1752
01:27:46,731 --> 01:27:49,275
Yesterday's concert was amazing.

1753
01:27:49,276 --> 01:27:51,110
You were both so good.

1754
01:27:51,111 --> 01:27:54,989
Iroha, your performance was so good,
you brought us to tears! [giggles]

1755
01:27:54,990 --> 01:27:57,284
I'd give it a gold star for sure.

1756
01:27:58,618 --> 01:28:00,286
[chuckles] Thank you.

1757
01:28:00,287 --> 01:28:02,330
So, anyway, where's Kaguya?

1758
01:28:03,456 --> 01:28:05,834
She was filleting a fish last I saw her.

1759
01:28:06,626 --> 01:28:07,793
- Eh…
- Hmm…

1760
01:28:07,794 --> 01:28:08,877
Hmm?

1761
01:28:08,878 --> 01:28:11,463
9/1 - FIREWORKS FESTIVAL

1762
01:28:11,464 --> 01:28:14,467
[Roka] How about some fireworks
to end summer with a bang?

1763
01:28:15,093 --> 01:28:18,679
It's about an hour away by train.
All of us?

1764
01:28:18,680 --> 01:28:22,766
[Mami] No, no. We have
an important mission to take care of.

1765
01:28:22,767 --> 01:28:26,312
[Roka] We completely neglected
all our summer homework.

1766
01:28:26,313 --> 01:28:27,814
So what do you think?

1767
01:28:28,356 --> 01:28:30,025
It's your call.

1768
01:28:33,903 --> 01:28:34,904
[chuckles]

1769
01:28:40,493 --> 01:28:41,577
Mmm.

1770
01:28:41,578 --> 01:28:42,661
DAY OFF
MOCK EXAM

1771
01:28:42,662 --> 01:28:44,539
Looks like I have my own trouble.

1772
01:28:49,419 --> 01:28:52,129
Hey, Kaguya. How's it going out here?

1773
01:28:52,130 --> 01:28:54,466
Oh. [giggles]
Iroha, you are right on time.

1774
01:28:54,966 --> 01:28:56,593
- Here.
- [bites, chews]

1775
01:28:57,302 --> 01:28:59,136
Tasty. What is it?

1776
01:28:59,137 --> 01:29:01,765
And tomorrow,
I'll make ramen from scratch! [chuckles]

1777
01:29:02,474 --> 01:29:03,892
Awesome.

1778
01:29:04,893 --> 01:29:05,894
Mmm.

1779
01:29:08,396 --> 01:29:09,397
Want to go?

1780
01:29:11,149 --> 01:29:12,483
I…

1781
01:29:12,484 --> 01:29:15,612
Yay! Yay! Yay!

1782
01:29:17,655 --> 01:29:18,990
[gentle music playing]

1783
01:29:21,326 --> 01:29:22,827
I love it!

1784
01:29:24,162 --> 01:29:26,288
You don't think I look a bit weird?

1785
01:29:26,289 --> 01:29:27,456
No!

1786
01:29:27,457 --> 01:29:30,168
- You look great in anything!
- [groans]

1787
01:29:33,463 --> 01:29:35,882
[Kaguya giggles]

1788
01:29:40,970 --> 01:29:42,639
[humming and laughing]

1789
01:29:50,855 --> 01:29:53,108
[gasps]

1790
01:29:55,276 --> 01:29:56,277
RAINBOW MIX

1791
01:29:57,862 --> 01:30:00,572
[Kaguya] There's really no substitute
for real life.

1792
01:30:00,573 --> 01:30:01,657
[exclaims]

1793
01:30:01,658 --> 01:30:03,200
[Iroha] Sure, but Tsukuyomi
is pretty good too, right?

1794
01:30:03,201 --> 01:30:04,202
LIGHT BULB SODA

1795
01:30:10,667 --> 01:30:12,961
Wow, this is so fun!

1796
01:30:13,628 --> 01:30:15,213
A kingdom of fun.

1797
01:30:17,549 --> 01:30:20,260
Hey, are you copying me? [laughs]

1798
01:30:22,428 --> 01:30:24,847
You never take that thing off, do you?

1799
01:30:24,848 --> 01:30:26,140
Uh, oh…

1800
01:30:26,141 --> 01:30:29,310
It makes me feel calm.
It's like a little piece of home.

1801
01:30:37,068 --> 01:30:39,653
[announcer] Welcome to
the 25th Satomi Fireworks Festival.

1802
01:30:39,654 --> 01:30:42,239
Hey, did you know, on the moon
we don't have any sense of taste

1803
01:30:42,240 --> 01:30:43,699
or temperature?

1804
01:30:43,700 --> 01:30:46,577
Everyone just repeats their roles
over and over again.

1805
01:30:46,578 --> 01:30:47,911
It's so boring.

1806
01:30:47,912 --> 01:30:50,205
[announcer] With the hope
that each light will become a flower…

1807
01:30:50,206 --> 01:30:52,291
I can't imagine what that's like.

1808
01:30:52,292 --> 01:30:54,334
[announcer]
So with no further ado, is everyone ready?

1809
01:30:54,335 --> 01:30:56,379
I was always the odd one.

1810
01:30:58,006 --> 01:31:00,967
- [spectator 1] Oh, there they are.
- [spectator 2] Look, it's starting.

1811
01:31:01,467 --> 01:31:04,345
[spectators gasping, laughing]

1812
01:31:06,806 --> 01:31:07,891
[giggles]

1813
01:31:09,934 --> 01:31:12,144
[Kaguya] It gets lonely and boring.

1814
01:31:12,145 --> 01:31:16,190
Having to repeat the same things
every day, it was killing me.

1815
01:31:16,191 --> 01:31:19,318
Finally, I'd had enough.
I wanted to go somewhere. Anywhere.

1816
01:31:19,319 --> 01:31:20,402
FIREWORKS FESTIVAL

1817
01:31:20,403 --> 01:31:22,196
[Kaguya]
I looked out the window into your world

1818
01:31:22,197 --> 01:31:24,364
at all the people
doing whatever they pleased.

1819
01:31:24,365 --> 01:31:28,870
Their lives were complex, fleeting
and, best of all, free.

1820
01:31:30,663 --> 01:31:31,706
But…

1821
01:31:32,207 --> 01:31:36,252
I could tell they were also
holding back their emotions.

1822
01:31:37,045 --> 01:31:39,255
Waiting for something more important.

1823
01:31:40,548 --> 01:31:42,758
Then what? You grew up?

1824
01:31:42,759 --> 01:31:44,928
[laughs] I'm copying you.

1825
01:31:47,263 --> 01:31:49,515
- Can I ask you something?
- What?

1826
01:31:50,892 --> 01:31:52,894
Do you love your mom, Iroha?

1827
01:31:58,983 --> 01:32:01,277
[Iroha] Do I love her?

1828
01:32:02,987 --> 01:32:05,698
I don't know. I really don't.

1829
01:32:06,449 --> 01:32:08,326
[inhales sharply, sobs]

1830
01:32:10,078 --> 01:32:11,496
So many times…

1831
01:32:12,455 --> 01:32:16,083
I thought it would be easier
if I could just hate her.

1832
01:32:16,084 --> 01:32:17,085
[sobs]

1833
01:32:17,877 --> 01:32:21,630
You know something,
now I'm feeling even more sorry for you.

1834
01:32:21,631 --> 01:32:25,259
Sorry I brought it up.
I'm surprised you didn't get mad at me.

1835
01:32:25,260 --> 01:32:27,761
"You just don't understand, Kaguya."

1836
01:32:27,762 --> 01:32:29,931
That's what you wanted to say, right?

1837
01:32:32,600 --> 01:32:33,685
[Iroha] No…

1838
01:32:34,769 --> 01:32:36,604
I didn't want to say that.

1839
01:32:37,146 --> 01:32:39,482
You just don't understand yet.

1840
01:32:41,859 --> 01:32:43,861
[Iroha] I never wanted to say that.

1841
01:32:45,488 --> 01:32:46,739
[Kaguya] I see.

1842
01:32:49,826 --> 01:32:50,827
[Iroha] Kaguya.

1843
01:32:52,620 --> 01:32:53,955
Are you going home?

1844
01:32:54,831 --> 01:32:58,458
[Kaguya] Well, I kinda ditched work
to come here, so…

1845
01:32:58,459 --> 01:33:00,962
It's like forced deportation. [chuckles]

1846
01:33:03,589 --> 01:33:06,551
Guess I am Princess Kaguya, after all.

1847
01:33:10,013 --> 01:33:13,182
During the next full moon,
they'll come for me.

1848
01:33:14,183 --> 01:33:16,601
They'll come to our house?

1849
01:33:16,602 --> 01:33:19,730
Mmm, they'll probably come to Tsukuyomi.

1850
01:33:19,731 --> 01:33:22,900
The virtual world is much closer
to the moon than your world.

1851
01:33:25,945 --> 01:33:27,488
[Iroha] You could just run away again.

1852
01:33:28,448 --> 01:33:30,991
There's no way
you're the real Princess Kaguya.

1853
01:33:30,992 --> 01:33:33,411
You're too crazy and chaotic.

1854
01:33:33,911 --> 01:33:36,956
There's no way that you're the same person
from the fairy tale.

1855
01:33:37,623 --> 01:33:38,624
[giggles]

1856
01:33:39,375 --> 01:33:42,711
[Kaguya] And so the chaotic Princess
Kaguya was summoned back to the moon,

1857
01:33:42,712 --> 01:33:46,340
but she swore that she would
make her final days an absolute blast.

1858
01:33:46,341 --> 01:33:47,424
[giggles]

1859
01:33:47,425 --> 01:33:49,385
That's how it should have ended.

1860
01:33:50,303 --> 01:33:52,304
That's the ending for me.

1861
01:33:52,305 --> 01:33:55,849
Enjoying every second
as I charge towards destiny.

1862
01:33:55,850 --> 01:33:56,851
[gasps]

1863
01:33:58,978 --> 01:34:00,979
But if I'm being honest,

1864
01:34:00,980 --> 01:34:04,025
I wanted to spend more time
singing with you, Iroha!

1865
01:34:04,859 --> 01:34:07,153
- All the new songs as well.
- Huh.

1866
01:34:08,613 --> 01:34:11,406
I know. When they do come,

1867
01:34:11,407 --> 01:34:13,910
let's do a big concert, okay?

1868
01:34:17,663 --> 01:34:19,623
[Kaguya screams]

1869
01:34:19,624 --> 01:34:22,668
I felt that one! And smell that smoke!

1870
01:34:23,252 --> 01:34:26,422
[gasps] It's amazing!

1871
01:34:34,972 --> 01:34:36,808
We should probably head home

1872
01:34:38,101 --> 01:34:39,769
before it gets too late.

1873
01:34:46,609 --> 01:34:48,902
[Iroha] Guess real life
is finally catching up with me.

1874
01:34:48,903 --> 01:34:50,278
KAGUYA ANNOUNCES HER GRADUATION!

1875
01:34:50,279 --> 01:34:52,240
Time to go back to my old self.

1876
01:34:53,157 --> 01:34:55,701
I can get back to studying and work.

1877
01:34:59,831 --> 01:35:00,956
[Kaguya] Crabs!

1878
01:35:00,957 --> 01:35:02,874
- [Iroha] I'm home.
- Crabs, crabs.

1879
01:35:02,875 --> 01:35:04,459
Hi.

1880
01:35:04,460 --> 01:35:06,129
- [laughs]
- What are you doing?

1881
01:35:07,255 --> 01:35:08,506
Playing with the crabs.

1882
01:35:09,090 --> 01:35:10,091
Uh…

1883
01:35:10,883 --> 01:35:12,176
Want to make a song?

1884
01:35:12,802 --> 01:35:14,302
- A new one?
- What?

1885
01:35:14,303 --> 01:35:15,470
Really?

1886
01:35:15,471 --> 01:35:17,222
Yahoo! [laughing]

1887
01:35:17,223 --> 01:35:19,350
I can't promise you
it'll be any good though.

1888
01:35:20,309 --> 01:35:21,560
What should we write?

1889
01:35:21,561 --> 01:35:25,273
I know, how about that song
you never finished?

1890
01:35:26,107 --> 01:35:27,525
Uh, hmm…

1891
01:35:28,359 --> 01:35:29,360
Mmm…

1892
01:35:34,240 --> 01:35:35,407
Hmm…

1893
01:35:35,408 --> 01:35:37,243
Iroha! Let's… Uh…

1894
01:35:38,828 --> 01:35:40,496
- [sighs]
- Oh. [chuckles]

1895
01:35:41,289 --> 01:35:42,290
[cackles]

1896
01:35:43,749 --> 01:35:45,668
EASY CHAR SIU
LOTS OF PORK BELLY

1897
01:35:46,961 --> 01:35:48,086
Hmm.

1898
01:35:48,087 --> 01:35:50,798
I wonder if I can take InuDOGE home too.

1899
01:36:04,645 --> 01:36:06,396
[Mikado] Aw, man!

1900
01:36:06,397 --> 01:36:09,691
I can't believe
that Kaguya's really a moon princess.

1901
01:36:09,692 --> 01:36:10,693
It makes sense.

1902
01:36:11,277 --> 01:36:13,653
Wow, so then Kaguya really was
from the moon.

1903
01:36:13,654 --> 01:36:16,449
No wonder her skin was perfect,
even at the beach.

1904
01:36:17,825 --> 01:36:21,204
Yachiyo, do you think
we'll be able to protect Kaguya?

1905
01:36:21,787 --> 01:36:22,871
I looked into it,

1906
01:36:22,872 --> 01:36:25,917
but I can't even figure out how
they managed to get into Tsukuyomi.

1907
01:36:26,792 --> 01:36:27,959
I'm sorry.

1908
01:36:27,960 --> 01:36:29,003
[Iroha] It's okay.

1909
01:36:30,213 --> 01:36:33,757
Well, they can't grab her
in the real world, ain't that right?

1910
01:36:33,758 --> 01:36:36,010
So how about
we just take them out in here?

1911
01:36:38,304 --> 01:36:39,430
I'll help too.

1912
01:36:40,139 --> 01:36:41,933
I don't know how useful I'll be…

1913
01:36:43,851 --> 01:36:44,894
but I'll do my best.

1914
01:36:45,686 --> 01:36:48,021
Okay. Let's get ready. Noi?

1915
01:36:48,022 --> 01:36:50,440
Aw, man. That thing's such a pain though.

1916
01:36:50,441 --> 01:36:52,943
- [Mikado] Just follow orders.
- [Noi] Okay, okay.

1917
01:36:52,944 --> 01:36:53,945
[Roka] Iroha.

1918
01:36:56,280 --> 01:36:58,324
Let's all go to the beach again next year.

1919
01:36:58,824 --> 01:37:00,284
And the hot springs too!

1920
01:37:01,118 --> 01:37:02,286
[Iroha] Thank you.

1921
01:37:04,080 --> 01:37:05,205
Oh, mmm…

1922
01:37:05,206 --> 01:37:08,751
I'm sorry, Yachiyo.
Can I ask you for one more favor?

1923
01:37:16,509 --> 01:37:19,469
- Huh? Oh.
- [pop music plays through headphones]

1924
01:37:19,470 --> 01:37:22,389
[gasps] Wow, is that the song?

1925
01:37:22,390 --> 01:37:23,516
Yeah…

1926
01:37:25,351 --> 01:37:29,188
It's actually a song
I had been working on with my dad.

1927
01:37:29,897 --> 01:37:31,148
It's my first song.

1928
01:37:32,233 --> 01:37:36,279
After my Dad died,
I wrote a few other songs,

1929
01:37:37,613 --> 01:37:41,659
but they never felt quite right,
so I stopped writing.

1930
01:37:44,203 --> 01:37:48,040
But now I can't remember
just how the song ends.

1931
01:37:48,916 --> 01:37:50,167
[sighs] Hmm.

1932
01:37:50,668 --> 01:37:52,377
Don't worry. That's why I'm here.

1933
01:37:52,378 --> 01:37:54,379
I'll write the rest of the lyrics for you.

1934
01:37:54,380 --> 01:37:57,632
Together, I just know
we're gonna make your dad proud.

1935
01:37:57,633 --> 01:37:58,967
♪ Smack your hand up the wall ♪

1936
01:37:58,968 --> 01:38:04,139
♪ And add some spice
To make your life feel way more exciting ♪

1937
01:38:04,140 --> 01:38:06,309
That works, right?

1938
01:38:07,101 --> 01:38:09,645
[chuckles] Maybe it does.

1939
01:38:10,187 --> 01:38:14,524
Oh, guess what, Yachiyo agreed
to produce our next live concert.

1940
01:38:14,525 --> 01:38:17,277
What? No way! You asked her?

1941
01:38:17,278 --> 01:38:19,779
Leave everything to me!

1942
01:38:19,780 --> 01:38:22,825
Awesome! I have to start coming up
with the choreography!

1943
01:38:23,326 --> 01:38:24,410
Uh…

1944
01:38:25,328 --> 01:38:28,873
[chuckles] Well, in that case,
I'd better finish this song.

1945
01:38:29,498 --> 01:38:31,791
[sighing]

1946
01:38:31,792 --> 01:38:32,793
[desk clatters]

1947
01:38:33,377 --> 01:38:35,503
On second thought, maybe that's too much.

1948
01:38:35,504 --> 01:38:37,298
One chorus at a time.

1949
01:38:37,923 --> 01:38:39,425
[energetic pop music playing]

1950
01:38:40,134 --> 01:38:41,135
[gasps]

1951
01:38:43,638 --> 01:38:44,639
[music stops]

1952
01:38:46,265 --> 01:38:47,558
[energetic melody plays]

1953
01:38:50,269 --> 01:38:51,979
[soft melody plays]

1954
01:38:52,605 --> 01:38:54,607
[no audible dialogue]

1955
01:38:57,526 --> 01:38:58,819
The same melody?

1956
01:39:00,988 --> 01:39:01,989
But why?

1957
01:39:10,122 --> 01:39:13,376
[Kaguya hums melody]

1958
01:39:17,213 --> 01:39:19,631
Check, check, check. Mic test!

1959
01:39:19,632 --> 01:39:21,717
[humming]

1960
01:39:23,552 --> 01:39:24,553
[gasps]

1961
01:39:25,471 --> 01:39:26,472
Kaguya?

1962
01:39:28,224 --> 01:39:29,349
[breathes shakily]

1963
01:39:29,350 --> 01:39:30,393
- Yeah?
- [yelps]

1964
01:39:30,935 --> 01:39:31,936
[groans]

1965
01:39:32,436 --> 01:39:34,187
Don't scare me like that.

1966
01:39:34,188 --> 01:39:35,690
[gasps, chuckles]

1967
01:39:38,317 --> 01:39:40,236
Here, this is for you.

1968
01:39:40,778 --> 01:39:42,738
- Oh. You're sure?
- [chuckles]

1969
01:39:43,781 --> 01:39:44,865
Thank you.

1970
01:39:52,206 --> 01:39:54,250
[Kaguya] The concert's gonna be here?

1971
01:39:55,459 --> 01:39:57,461
That's what Iroha wanted.

1972
01:39:58,421 --> 01:39:59,630
Yachiyo!

1973
01:40:01,716 --> 01:40:04,802
[chuckles] Nothing to worry about,
you little cutie.

1974
01:40:05,428 --> 01:40:08,013
[FUSHI] Hey, don't get too cocky,
you little mutt.

1975
01:40:08,931 --> 01:40:09,932
[InuDOGE barks]

1976
01:40:11,392 --> 01:40:15,271
I wonder if they'd love me more,
if I was just like you, Yachiyo.

1977
01:40:16,814 --> 01:40:18,148
Hmm.

1978
01:40:18,149 --> 01:40:21,819
No, no.
This is all happening thanks to you.

1979
01:40:23,237 --> 01:40:24,905
Off you go, Kaguya.

1980
01:40:26,282 --> 01:40:30,243
It's all going to work out,
because I know you.

1981
01:40:30,244 --> 01:40:31,245
[chuckles]

1982
01:40:31,996 --> 01:40:34,497
That's reckless. [laughs]

1983
01:40:34,498 --> 01:40:37,543
But, sometimes, that's the best way to be.

1984
01:40:39,378 --> 01:40:41,880
[Otako] What a crazy turn of events!

1985
01:40:41,881 --> 01:40:45,383
It's the graduation concert
of the superstar Kaguya,

1986
01:40:45,384 --> 01:40:47,886
the girl who came out of nowhere
and touched all our hearts.

1987
01:40:47,887 --> 01:40:50,513
But this is not the time to cry.

1988
01:40:50,514 --> 01:40:54,893
Kaguya's last show, let's make it count!

1989
01:40:54,894 --> 01:40:56,019
- [crowd cheering]
- [fan 1] Kaguya!

1990
01:40:56,020 --> 01:40:57,229
[fan 2] I love you!

1991
01:41:05,821 --> 01:41:09,450
Everybody, thank you!

1992
01:41:10,367 --> 01:41:12,828
Looks like it's time to say goodbye,

1993
01:41:13,370 --> 01:41:15,747
but please don't be sad.

1994
01:41:15,748 --> 01:41:17,708
Graduations are happy events.

1995
01:41:18,542 --> 01:41:20,628
So please see me off with a smile.

1996
01:41:21,128 --> 01:41:22,296
- [whooshing overhead]
- Uh…

1997
01:41:27,551 --> 01:41:29,052
[all giggle]

1998
01:41:29,053 --> 01:41:30,054
[Mami, Roka] Yay!

1999
01:41:31,263 --> 01:41:33,097
Mind if we join you?

2000
01:41:33,098 --> 01:41:37,519
Kaguya, we're gonna do our best
to keep you with us.

2001
01:41:37,520 --> 01:41:38,603
[gasps]

2002
01:41:38,604 --> 01:41:39,688
[Iroha] And if we win,

2003
01:41:40,314 --> 01:41:43,399
we can celebrate with pancakes
and shopping at Donki.

2004
01:41:43,400 --> 01:41:46,152
It's not "if" we win, you know?

2005
01:41:46,153 --> 01:41:47,487
[Iroha scoffs]

2006
01:41:47,488 --> 01:41:50,448
I see… Okay!

2007
01:41:50,449 --> 01:41:52,367
[laughing]

2008
01:41:52,368 --> 01:41:55,955
This is freedom!

2009
01:42:01,085 --> 01:42:02,711
[mysterious music playing]

2010
01:42:10,219 --> 01:42:12,221
[pop music playing]

2011
01:42:16,517 --> 01:42:19,019
[Iroha] Are they here to take Kaguya home?

2012
01:42:22,273 --> 01:42:24,441
[Mikado] Time to get this party started!

2013
01:42:29,071 --> 01:42:33,032
♪ No matter what tomorrow holds ♪

2014
01:42:33,033 --> 01:42:35,034
♪ Let's live in the moment ♪

2015
01:42:35,035 --> 01:42:38,788
♪ So we can smile and joy unfolds ♪

2016
01:42:38,789 --> 01:42:42,375
♪ It's my decision, not a game ♪

2017
01:42:42,376 --> 01:42:44,794
♪ But I end up dreaming ♪

2018
01:42:44,795 --> 01:42:48,131
♪ About a day that stays the same ♪

2019
01:42:48,132 --> 01:42:50,717
♪ With many more impulsive melodies ♪

2020
01:42:50,718 --> 01:42:53,261
♪ With heartfelt songs
And tender harmonies ♪

2021
01:42:53,262 --> 01:42:57,724
♪ The brightest symphony
For us to say goodbye ♪

2022
01:42:57,725 --> 01:43:02,395
♪ The scenes I carried in my mind
I long to see one day ♪

2023
01:43:02,396 --> 01:43:05,857
♪ Were more beautiful and hard to define ♪

2024
01:43:05,858 --> 01:43:10,112
♪ Free in many different ways ♪

2025
01:43:11,822 --> 01:43:17,035
♪ When a thousand years are gone
And ten thousand fade from sight ♪

2026
01:43:17,036 --> 01:43:21,831
♪ Still this single second lives on
Forever, shining through the night ♪

2027
01:43:21,832 --> 01:43:26,461
♪ A time to start anew
And a time when things are through ♪

2028
01:43:26,462 --> 01:43:29,839
♪ Now I see you looking at me gently ♪

2029
01:43:29,840 --> 01:43:32,759
♪ And it warms my heart ♪

2030
01:43:32,760 --> 01:43:35,386
♪ So if this is my fate
Then I will embrace the call… ♪

2031
01:43:35,387 --> 01:43:41,184
- [Iroha] I won't let this end badly!
- ♪ I'll try to open myself to it all ♪

2032
01:43:41,185 --> 01:43:45,063
♪ Ah, look how this land
Fills up with colors ♪

2033
01:43:45,064 --> 01:43:46,689
♪ That have re-emerged ♪

2034
01:43:46,690 --> 01:43:53,404
♪ Bringing a light to all the tears
And smiles in all the world ♪

2035
01:43:53,405 --> 01:43:54,406
[music ends]

2036
01:44:05,000 --> 01:44:06,876
[sighs, grunts]

2037
01:44:06,877 --> 01:44:07,878
["Reply" plays]

2038
01:44:34,363 --> 01:44:39,910
♪ In your eyes I can see
All the quiet in the world ♪

2039
01:44:40,494 --> 01:44:44,957
♪ And how did I never see before ♪

2040
01:44:45,874 --> 01:44:47,084
[Kaguya] Iroha,

2041
01:44:48,043 --> 01:44:50,212
you're more beautiful than you know.

2042
01:44:51,088 --> 01:44:53,841
I fell in love with you
the moment I saw you.

2043
01:44:56,051 --> 01:44:59,053
♪ I know I've been self-obsessed ♪

2044
01:44:59,054 --> 01:45:01,889
♪ I know that I screwed around ♪

2045
01:45:01,890 --> 01:45:07,353
♪ But we've gotta catch that colorfulness
That's nowhere to be found ♪

2046
01:45:07,354 --> 01:45:08,479
♪ Let's go ♪

2047
01:45:08,480 --> 01:45:11,524
♪ 'Cause there's nothing better
In this world ♪

2048
01:45:11,525 --> 01:45:13,985
♪ Than right here, right now ♪

2049
01:45:13,986 --> 01:45:16,779
♪ Gotta hold on tight to the moment ♪

2050
01:45:16,780 --> 01:45:19,449
♪ Hold on to the golden days we find ♪

2051
01:45:19,450 --> 01:45:22,076
♪ Come on, let's share all our dreams ♪

2052
01:45:22,077 --> 01:45:24,954
♪ And we can act like queens and kings ♪

2053
01:45:24,955 --> 01:45:26,706
♪ And we can keep ourselves ♪

2054
01:45:26,707 --> 01:45:31,044
♪ Surrounded by the love
We find in everyday things ♪

2055
01:45:31,045 --> 01:45:34,422
♪ Every memory is a sweet daydream ♪

2056
01:45:34,423 --> 01:45:37,008
♪ I cherish all of ours ♪

2057
01:45:37,009 --> 01:45:39,010
♪ We can keep them all in our hearts ♪

2058
01:45:39,011 --> 01:45:41,721
♪ Protected like the treasures
That they are ♪

2059
01:45:41,722 --> 01:45:44,724
♪ Come on, let's party some more ♪

2060
01:45:44,725 --> 01:45:47,727
♪ And when we're done, sing an encore ♪

2061
01:45:47,728 --> 01:45:51,189
♪ And we'll get everything
We're wishing for ♪

2062
01:45:51,190 --> 01:45:55,652
♪ We're shining stars
When we sing our song ♪

2063
01:46:09,958 --> 01:46:10,959
[music ends]

2064
01:46:23,764 --> 01:46:25,890
[ethereal chiming]

2065
01:46:25,891 --> 01:46:27,559
You've traveled a long way.

2066
01:46:28,769 --> 01:46:30,978
I'm sorry that I ran away,

2067
01:46:30,979 --> 01:46:35,067
but I've had such an awesome time
while I was here.

2068
01:46:35,692 --> 01:46:36,902
[ethereal chiming]

2069
01:46:48,831 --> 01:46:50,207
No, wait.

2070
01:46:55,295 --> 01:46:58,465
Don't go. There's more you wanted to do.

2071
01:47:04,012 --> 01:47:07,099
This was the best graduation ever!

2072
01:47:07,683 --> 01:47:09,852
So many memories I'll never forget.

2073
01:47:10,686 --> 01:47:13,730
Thank you, everyone!

2074
01:47:14,314 --> 01:47:16,691
- [fan 3] Kaguya!
- [fan 4] I love you!

2075
01:47:16,692 --> 01:47:19,819
- [fan 5] Don't go. [cries]
- [laughs]

2076
01:47:19,820 --> 01:47:22,614
Saying goodbye is hard,
and all things end.

2077
01:47:23,907 --> 01:47:25,367
Don't forget…

2078
01:47:28,704 --> 01:47:31,039
Iroha. I love you.

2079
01:47:32,958 --> 01:47:35,586
- Bye-bye!
- [crowd cheering]

2080
01:47:49,349 --> 01:47:50,350
[whimpers]

2081
01:48:04,823 --> 01:48:07,909
[fan 6] What a show!
It's like she really was Princess Kaguya.

2082
01:48:07,910 --> 01:48:10,328
- [fan 7] It's like a dream!
- [fan 8] I'll never recover! [cries]

2083
01:48:10,329 --> 01:48:13,665
No, is this really your last bow?

2084
01:48:19,338 --> 01:48:22,007
Listen, all of you fought well.

2085
01:48:23,133 --> 01:48:24,468
Thank you so much.

2086
01:48:25,219 --> 01:48:26,220
[chuckles]

2087
01:48:27,054 --> 01:48:28,055
Hmm.

2088
01:48:29,014 --> 01:48:31,266
It's time to go home.

2089
01:48:32,392 --> 01:48:33,435
- I'm sorry.
- [all gasp]

2090
01:48:51,995 --> 01:48:55,081
- [vocalizes]
- [Iroha] Spends my money without asking.

2091
01:48:55,082 --> 01:48:56,999
- [laughs]
- Does whatever she wants.

2092
01:48:57,000 --> 01:48:58,459
Never cleans up.

2093
01:48:58,460 --> 01:48:59,752
NO MAYO/KETCHUP ALLOWED

2094
01:48:59,753 --> 01:49:01,505
[Iroha] She's such a pain.

2095
01:49:05,968 --> 01:49:07,386
- [sighs]
- Seriously…

2096
01:49:09,429 --> 01:49:11,306
the absolute worst.

2097
01:49:11,932 --> 01:49:13,100
- [phone buzzes]
- [gasps]

2098
01:49:16,144 --> 01:49:19,605
YOU'VE RECEIVED A PAYMENT

2099
01:49:19,606 --> 01:49:21,483
HERE'S ALL THE MONEY I OWE YOU!
SORRY FOR THE TROUBLE!

2100
01:49:26,113 --> 01:49:27,614
I can't spend that.

2101
01:49:30,742 --> 01:49:33,870
Oh, you dummy. It's too much.

2102
01:50:00,063 --> 01:50:01,272
[sighs]

2103
01:50:01,273 --> 01:50:03,150
[calm music playing]

2104
01:50:09,573 --> 01:50:10,656
TARGET SCHOOL LIST

2105
01:50:10,657 --> 01:50:11,991
[teacher]
So you decided on law school, huh?

2106
01:50:11,992 --> 01:50:14,578
Sorry it took so long.
There's been a lot going on.

2107
01:50:15,579 --> 01:50:17,622
You've always been a perfect student.

2108
01:50:18,165 --> 01:50:20,249
I'm glad you had a distraction.

2109
01:50:20,250 --> 01:50:22,835
Yeah, but that's behind me now.

2110
01:50:22,836 --> 01:50:24,296
I'm all ready to get to work.

2111
01:50:26,423 --> 01:50:30,260
Is there any advice on
how to prep for entrance exams?

2112
01:50:32,179 --> 01:50:33,180
Of course!

2113
01:50:34,389 --> 01:50:36,390
I'm sorry I ghosted you.

2114
01:50:36,391 --> 01:50:38,226
So mean.

2115
01:50:38,935 --> 01:50:41,270
I was gonna go break down your door.

2116
01:50:41,271 --> 01:50:42,814
I'm really, really sorry.

2117
01:50:44,775 --> 01:50:46,651
[chuckles] All that matters…

2118
01:50:47,194 --> 01:50:49,571
Is that our friend is feeling better.

2119
01:50:50,906 --> 01:50:51,907
[gasps]

2120
01:50:52,407 --> 01:50:53,408
[sobs]

2121
01:50:54,701 --> 01:50:58,413
[Yachiyo] Just like that, the fairy-tale
days of life with Kaguya were over.

2122
01:50:58,914 --> 01:51:01,124
Life went back to normal for Iroha.

2123
01:51:03,877 --> 01:51:07,339
That was the story of Iroha
and Princess Kaguya.

2124
01:51:09,424 --> 01:51:12,843
[Iroha] Kaguya, you may not be with me,

2125
01:51:12,844 --> 01:51:15,430
but I'll carry you in my heart forever!

2126
01:51:18,433 --> 01:51:21,269
AND SHE LIVED HAPPILY EVER AFTER

2127
01:51:22,062 --> 01:51:27,359
"COOLNESS" IS THE THEME OF
THE BLACK ONYX SPECIAL 3RD LIVE.

2128
01:51:28,402 --> 01:51:30,529
There's no way
I'm letting it end like this.

2129
01:51:31,238 --> 01:51:32,321
I can't!

2130
01:51:32,322 --> 01:51:33,782
[energetic music playing]

2131
01:51:41,623 --> 01:51:43,707
I need more time to decide.

2132
01:51:43,708 --> 01:51:45,043
[teacher] Take all the time you need.

2133
01:51:47,170 --> 01:51:50,048
[Kaguya] I wanted to spend more time
singing with you, Iroha.

2134
01:51:51,925 --> 01:51:53,301
[Iroha] I want that too.

2135
01:51:54,010 --> 01:51:55,303
I want…

2136
01:51:57,472 --> 01:51:58,473
[grunts]

2137
01:52:00,100 --> 01:52:01,976
I don't need a happy ending.

2138
01:52:01,977 --> 01:52:04,228
A normal ending is perfectly fine with me.

2139
01:52:04,229 --> 01:52:06,148
I HAVE A MIGRAINE,
SO I'LL NEED TO MISS WORK…

2140
01:52:08,233 --> 01:52:10,025
[Kaguya] That's the ending for me!

2141
01:52:10,026 --> 01:52:13,655
Enjoying every second
as I charge towards destiny!

2142
01:52:18,493 --> 01:52:20,369
MOM - SWIPE TO ANSWER

2143
01:52:20,370 --> 01:52:21,955
I don't think so.

2144
01:52:22,622 --> 01:52:23,706
No.

2145
01:52:23,707 --> 01:52:26,208
[line ringing]

2146
01:52:26,209 --> 01:52:28,295
[no audible dialogue]

2147
01:52:36,136 --> 01:52:38,387
[Mom] All right. Go ahead.

2148
01:52:38,388 --> 01:52:39,389
[gasps]

2149
01:52:43,518 --> 01:52:44,603
I did it.

2150
01:52:53,570 --> 01:52:54,613
I told her.

2151
01:53:08,251 --> 01:53:12,297
♪ All that I wanted from you ♪

2152
01:53:13,048 --> 01:53:17,260
♪ Was to get back to us too ♪

2153
01:53:17,886 --> 01:53:22,057
♪ And it might sound so cliche ♪

2154
01:53:22,891 --> 01:53:27,062
♪ But we felt right yesterday ♪

2155
01:53:27,854 --> 01:53:32,942
♪ Let me know how you really feel ♪

2156
01:53:32,943 --> 01:53:38,113
♪ And we can make this dream a reality ♪

2157
01:53:38,114 --> 01:53:40,699
[gasps] Iroha!

2158
01:53:40,700 --> 01:53:41,909
[Iroha] ♪ Hey there ♪

2159
01:53:41,910 --> 01:53:46,664
♪ We can make this moment now
The greatest in the world ♪

2160
01:53:46,665 --> 01:53:50,251
- [Kaguya] Well, in that case, let's go!
- [Iroha singing]

2161
01:53:50,252 --> 01:53:52,253
♪ We can walk together down the road ♪

2162
01:53:52,254 --> 01:53:55,089
♪ If we can just let our hearts sing ♪

2163
01:53:55,090 --> 01:53:57,967
♪ Keep all of our faces smiling ♪

2164
01:53:57,968 --> 01:53:59,677
♪ And we can keep ourselves ♪

2165
01:53:59,678 --> 01:54:04,723
♪ Surrounded by the love
We find in everyday things ♪

2166
01:54:04,724 --> 01:54:05,934
[sighs]

2167
01:54:09,729 --> 01:54:11,897
YACHIYO RUNAMI - SENDING…

2168
01:54:11,898 --> 01:54:12,982
UNABLE TO SEND

2169
01:54:12,983 --> 01:54:16,026
[gasps, sighs]

2170
01:54:16,027 --> 01:54:17,611
[chiming]

2171
01:54:17,612 --> 01:54:21,658
[Yachiyo] I've been practicing
the Loach Scooping dance lately!

2172
01:54:22,158 --> 01:54:25,119
It's pretty funny!
Do you want me to show you?

2173
01:54:25,120 --> 01:54:28,665
Here we go! Hey there!

2174
01:54:29,249 --> 01:54:30,333
Come on!

2175
01:54:30,959 --> 01:54:34,129
- [sighs]
- Let's go. Come on.

2176
01:54:37,382 --> 01:54:39,801
Come back. How are you all by yourself?

2177
01:54:52,272 --> 01:54:53,815
Tell me where she is.

2178
01:54:58,695 --> 01:54:59,988
[sighs]

2179
01:55:00,739 --> 01:55:02,114
I'll find her myself.

2180
01:55:02,115 --> 01:55:04,743
Don't be dumb. Where would you even look?

2181
01:55:07,370 --> 01:55:10,332
I don't care.
I'll search the whole world if I have to.

2182
01:55:12,459 --> 01:55:13,919
[FUSHI] Open your eyes.

2183
01:55:18,340 --> 01:55:21,050
Over here!

2184
01:55:21,051 --> 01:55:23,469
Hey! [groans]

2185
01:55:23,470 --> 01:55:25,472
Let me get dressed first.

2186
01:55:52,582 --> 01:55:53,959
- [door unlocks]
- [gasps]

2187
01:56:28,243 --> 01:56:29,536
That's how you get in.

2188
01:56:31,579 --> 01:56:32,580
[grunts]

2189
01:56:48,096 --> 01:56:49,097
Kaguya?

2190
01:56:56,021 --> 01:56:57,313
[gasps]

2191
01:56:58,273 --> 01:56:59,441
Yachiyo.

2192
01:57:00,316 --> 01:57:03,695
Are you… Are you Kaguya?

2193
01:57:05,030 --> 01:57:07,282
I know it must sound crazy, but…

2194
01:57:08,366 --> 01:57:09,659
are you?

2195
01:57:19,377 --> 01:57:20,587
[gentle music playing]

2196
01:57:22,130 --> 01:57:23,506
A long time ago,

2197
01:57:24,007 --> 01:57:27,801
Kaguya was once again on the moon
working as a corporate slave

2198
01:57:27,802 --> 01:57:30,305
when a beautiful song reached her ears.

2199
01:57:30,930 --> 01:57:33,474
She decided right then to return to Earth.

2200
01:57:33,475 --> 01:57:36,685
So, she wrapped up all of her work
with lightning speed

2201
01:57:36,686 --> 01:57:38,521
and handed everything over.

2202
01:57:39,064 --> 01:57:42,608
Sadly, too many Earth years had gone by.

2203
01:57:42,609 --> 01:57:47,322
Not to worry, because the moon's
technology can transcend time itself.

2204
01:57:48,615 --> 01:57:52,077
Princess Kaguya traveled through time
to get here.

2205
01:57:52,577 --> 01:57:54,661
But before she could arrive,

2206
01:57:54,662 --> 01:57:58,041
her ship crashed into a giant asteroid.

2207
01:58:01,836 --> 01:58:04,171
When she finally got to Earth,

2208
01:58:04,172 --> 01:58:08,676
she had gone back too far.
8,000 years in the past.

2209
01:58:12,013 --> 01:58:14,932
There was not enough power
left in her broken ship,

2210
01:58:14,933 --> 01:58:17,893
and only InuDOGE, her faithful companion,

2211
01:58:17,894 --> 01:58:19,270
ended up with a body.

2212
01:58:20,939 --> 01:58:23,649
Her only way to communicate
with the world,

2213
01:58:23,650 --> 01:58:26,568
- was through the body of the sea slug.
- I give glory to you.

2214
01:58:26,569 --> 01:58:28,947
Listen up! All you gotta do is go west.

2215
01:58:29,531 --> 01:58:31,407
That will solve everything. [grunts]

2216
01:58:38,373 --> 01:58:39,790
[Yachiyo] Time passed,

2217
01:58:39,791 --> 01:58:43,794
and people developed the technology
to give shape to the invisible,

2218
01:58:43,795 --> 01:58:46,464
and connect with each other
across the world.

2219
01:58:47,298 --> 01:58:48,549
YACHI8000:
WHY'S IT STILL 1995? :(

2220
01:58:48,550 --> 01:58:51,427
[Yachiyo] It was similar to
the world of the moon she knew so well.

2221
01:58:52,178 --> 01:58:53,554
For the first time,

2222
01:58:53,555 --> 01:58:56,515
Kaguya discovered it was possible
to connect to the world

2223
01:58:56,516 --> 01:58:58,601
without a body of her own.

2224
01:59:00,311 --> 01:59:04,065
Finally, in the guise of
the songstress of Tsukuyomi,

2225
01:59:04,566 --> 01:59:07,610
she was able to
reunite once more with Iroha.

2226
01:59:08,987 --> 01:59:12,114
So, there we go, it's not
the simplest happy ending,

2227
01:59:12,115 --> 01:59:13,949
but we got there. [chuckles]

2228
01:59:13,950 --> 01:59:15,160
Uh, yep.

2229
01:59:16,661 --> 01:59:18,288
[Iroha] What about my Kaguya?

2230
01:59:19,747 --> 01:59:23,375
[Yachiyo] She's on her journey
of reincarnation once again.

2231
01:59:23,376 --> 01:59:27,046
It is a cycle.
One of a destiny that we cannot escape.

2232
01:59:28,923 --> 01:59:31,718
That doesn't make any sense.

2233
01:59:32,385 --> 01:59:34,261
- [footsteps approach]
- [pants]

2234
01:59:34,262 --> 01:59:35,805
It's just a fairy tale.

2235
01:59:36,389 --> 01:59:38,308
Don't think too hard about it.

2236
01:59:39,184 --> 01:59:41,811
Let's just celebrate our reunion.

2237
01:59:45,648 --> 01:59:49,819
You know, I've always loved
the view from up here.

2238
01:59:52,864 --> 01:59:53,907
But how?

2239
01:59:54,782 --> 01:59:57,159
How can you smile all the time?

2240
01:59:57,160 --> 01:59:59,329
That's just part of my nature.

2241
02:00:01,789 --> 02:00:02,790
But…

2242
02:00:05,543 --> 02:00:07,253
I made a promise…

2243
02:00:08,421 --> 02:00:11,632
that there'd be a happy ending for us.

2244
02:00:11,633 --> 02:00:14,844
And even though I tried to come back
when I heard your song…

2245
02:00:16,763 --> 02:00:18,973
Sorry, I messed up.

2246
02:00:19,974 --> 02:00:21,851
The sparkling Princess Kaguya…

2247
02:00:23,728 --> 02:00:26,064
is an old lady.

2248
02:00:28,066 --> 02:00:29,150
[gasps]

2249
02:00:30,151 --> 02:00:31,777
Kaguya…

2250
02:00:31,778 --> 02:00:35,323
I've never seen that look
on your face before.

2251
02:00:41,704 --> 02:00:42,705
[Yachiyo] Iroha…

2252
02:00:43,581 --> 02:00:47,335
If it's too much for you,
you can easily forget.

2253
02:00:48,378 --> 02:00:50,671
FUSHI can help…

2254
02:00:50,672 --> 02:00:52,047
- Yachiyo!
- [gasps]

2255
02:00:52,048 --> 02:00:53,508
[Iroha groans, scoffs]

2256
02:00:56,970 --> 02:00:58,345
[groans]

2257
02:00:58,346 --> 02:01:00,305
Eight thousand years…

2258
02:01:00,306 --> 02:01:02,724
I want to know everything that happened.

2259
02:01:02,725 --> 02:01:04,269
I'll stay up all night.

2260
02:01:06,354 --> 02:01:09,190
[laughs] Well, there's quite a lot.

2261
02:01:15,154 --> 02:01:16,155
Right!

2262
02:01:18,491 --> 02:01:21,411
[humming]

2263
02:01:22,954 --> 02:01:26,748
Sorry. I guess I still get
quite nostalgic for this place.

2264
02:01:26,749 --> 02:01:28,042
- You know?
- [grunts]

2265
02:01:28,626 --> 02:01:30,169
It's all fake, though.

2266
02:01:30,670 --> 02:01:31,754
I don't care!

2267
02:01:33,506 --> 02:01:34,589
Where to begin?

2268
02:01:34,590 --> 02:01:37,302
How about the time
I went fishing with the Jomon people?

2269
02:01:37,885 --> 02:01:41,221
That long-horned creature…
Now that's a story I remember.

2270
02:01:41,222 --> 02:01:42,889
And then that shrimp
with the long whiskers…

2271
02:01:42,890 --> 02:01:45,559
[dialogue speeds up rapidly]

2272
02:01:45,560 --> 02:01:46,935
…that was a blast.

2273
02:01:46,936 --> 02:01:48,770
But Sho was such a mess!

2274
02:01:48,771 --> 02:01:50,188
- [groans]
- You know,

2275
02:01:50,189 --> 02:01:53,108
you could die from lack of sleep, Iroha.

2276
02:01:53,109 --> 02:01:54,192
[groans]

2277
02:01:54,193 --> 02:01:56,571
The Edo period. Okay, keep going!

2278
02:01:58,072 --> 02:02:00,324
- Go to sleep. Go to sleep.
- Huh?

2279
02:02:00,325 --> 02:02:04,162
Oh, no. Looks like
it's just about my bedtime.

2280
02:02:05,288 --> 02:02:07,497
[yawns]

2281
02:02:07,498 --> 02:02:09,208
Sorry about that.

2282
02:02:13,796 --> 02:02:14,797
[Iroha sighs]

2283
02:02:15,882 --> 02:02:17,800
You were always so happy.

2284
02:02:19,385 --> 02:02:21,721
You grew up to be just like me.

2285
02:02:24,098 --> 02:02:27,893
FUSHI. Yachiyo's hiding something from me,

2286
02:02:27,894 --> 02:02:29,187
isn't she?

2287
02:02:31,022 --> 02:02:34,567
If she didn't tell you, then I…

2288
02:02:36,152 --> 02:02:38,278
Show me, FUSHI.

2289
02:02:38,279 --> 02:02:40,114
I want to know everything.

2290
02:02:41,699 --> 02:02:45,035
[FUSHI] I don't know if a human body
could handle it all.

2291
02:02:45,036 --> 02:02:46,621
[Iroha] This is non-negotiable.

2292
02:02:49,040 --> 02:02:54,754
Yachiyo, she looked truly happy
for the first time in a really long time.

2293
02:02:58,299 --> 02:03:04,222
[inhales deeply] Here we go!

2294
02:03:07,558 --> 02:03:08,559
[gasps]

2295
02:03:13,856 --> 02:03:14,857
[gasps]

2296
02:03:19,570 --> 02:03:22,240
[Kaguya] I wonder where Yachiyo is now…

2297
02:03:23,324 --> 02:03:24,617
Please come out.

2298
02:03:25,785 --> 02:03:26,994
Help me.

2299
02:03:27,870 --> 02:03:29,163
Kaguya!

2300
02:03:30,706 --> 02:03:33,835
[Kaguya] Believe it or not,
a girl came out of the utility pole!

2301
02:03:36,462 --> 02:03:38,839
[Empress Jingu]
You truly are a sign of good luck.

2302
02:03:38,840 --> 02:03:42,259
[Fujiwara] Compared to how I feel now,
after having met you…

2303
02:03:42,260 --> 02:03:44,220
There must be someone you're looking for.

2304
02:03:44,804 --> 02:03:46,179
[Empress Jingu] Life is hard.

2305
02:03:46,180 --> 02:03:48,849
But even when it's painful,
I smile through.

2306
02:03:48,850 --> 02:03:52,019
I had hoped to see the era
that would make you smile.

2307
02:03:52,979 --> 02:03:54,605
This is where I belong.

2308
02:03:56,232 --> 02:03:58,775
[Carter] The best wine
gets better over time.

2309
02:03:58,776 --> 02:04:00,695
It's not all bad, you know.

2310
02:04:01,446 --> 02:04:02,905
[groans]

2311
02:04:04,365 --> 02:04:06,032
[Kaguya] I'm such a dummy.

2312
02:04:06,033 --> 02:04:08,661
Why did it take me so long to realize it?

2313
02:04:10,288 --> 02:04:12,081
That Yachiyo…

2314
02:04:12,999 --> 02:04:14,083
She is…

2315
02:04:17,086 --> 02:04:18,129
[chuckles]

2316
02:04:19,547 --> 02:04:21,214
[Iroha] I get it now.

2317
02:04:21,215 --> 02:04:22,550
That's why Yachiyo

2318
02:04:23,634 --> 02:04:25,927
is always smiling so brightly,

2319
02:04:25,928 --> 02:04:27,305
why she's so happy.

2320
02:04:33,060 --> 02:04:34,270
[laughs]

2321
02:04:36,189 --> 02:04:39,566
[water rushing]

2322
02:04:39,567 --> 02:04:42,111
[glass shatters]

2323
02:04:43,154 --> 02:04:46,072
[Yachiyo] Iroha! Iroha!

2324
02:04:46,073 --> 02:04:47,074
Iroha!

2325
02:04:48,117 --> 02:04:49,577
[grunts, groans]

2326
02:05:02,381 --> 02:05:05,051
You know, I grew up too.

2327
02:05:06,010 --> 02:05:08,304
I was even able to talk to my mom.

2328
02:05:09,305 --> 02:05:13,184
Even after Kaguya left,
it was a perfectly happy ending.

2329
02:05:14,101 --> 02:05:16,979
And now the story is over.

2330
02:05:22,818 --> 02:05:24,654
[breathes shakily]

2331
02:05:26,948 --> 02:05:27,949
[sobs]

2332
02:05:28,908 --> 02:05:30,451
I want her back.

2333
02:05:31,577 --> 02:05:33,746
[gasps, sighs]

2334
02:05:35,623 --> 02:05:41,254
I thought that I could be happy
with this ending.

2335
02:05:44,340 --> 02:05:49,678
♪ Hey there
We can make this moment now ♪

2336
02:05:49,679 --> 02:05:52,640
♪ The greatest in the world ♪

2337
02:05:53,683 --> 02:05:55,560
I remembered every word.

2338
02:05:57,770 --> 02:06:01,856
♪ In our hearts
We've all got a song ♪

2339
02:06:01,857 --> 02:06:05,695
♪ It's a precious melody ♪

2340
02:06:06,737 --> 02:06:10,615
♪ Straight from your soul ♪

2341
02:06:10,616 --> 02:06:13,327
♪ Singing so sweet ♪

2342
02:06:14,537 --> 02:06:17,290
I survived because of this song.

2343
02:06:27,717 --> 02:06:32,305
I always wondered if your hands
would be warm to touch.

2344
02:06:33,931 --> 02:06:38,436
I want to eat pancakes with you once more.

2345
02:06:42,481 --> 02:06:44,149
Right, okay.

2346
02:06:44,150 --> 02:06:45,276
Here's the thing.

2347
02:06:45,776 --> 02:06:49,530
I know that our story is not over yet.

2348
02:06:53,284 --> 02:06:56,329
I found something else that I want to do.

2349
02:06:56,912 --> 02:07:00,291
So you have to stick with me
until we get the real happy ending.

2350
02:07:03,753 --> 02:07:06,672
[upbeat electronic music plays]

2351
02:07:09,467 --> 02:07:12,637
[no audible dialogue]

2352
02:07:15,139 --> 02:07:16,140
SHUT UP…

2353
02:07:16,849 --> 02:07:18,309
[no audible dialogue]

2354
02:07:19,226 --> 02:07:21,646
KURAKAWA HIGH SCHOOL

2355
02:07:26,609 --> 02:07:28,735
[no audible dialogue]

2356
02:07:28,736 --> 02:07:31,155
[music continues]

2357
02:07:37,370 --> 02:07:40,039
TEN YEARS LATER

2358
02:07:41,791 --> 02:07:44,543
Big brother, we're so close
to the final breakthrough.

2359
02:07:45,127 --> 02:07:47,672
- Huh?
- Let me be more clear.

2360
02:07:48,297 --> 02:07:51,633
I need you to invest in me.
I won't let you down!

2361
02:07:51,634 --> 02:07:53,093
Hang on a second.

2362
02:07:53,094 --> 02:07:55,512
What do you think I am,
some kind of billionaire?

2363
02:07:55,513 --> 02:07:58,808
You'll figure it out.
I believe in you. You can do it!

2364
02:07:59,600 --> 02:08:02,144
- You know, you…
- [Iroha] I what?

2365
02:08:02,895 --> 02:08:04,063
Nothing.

2366
02:08:04,689 --> 02:08:06,816
Okay, I'll figure something out.

2367
02:08:07,775 --> 02:08:10,194
Can I have an avatar body as well?

2368
02:08:10,695 --> 02:08:12,529
Noi and I will help out too.

2369
02:08:12,530 --> 02:08:13,613
[Noi] Huh? I will?

2370
02:08:13,614 --> 02:08:15,865
[Rai] It's nice to do a good deed
every now and then.

2371
02:08:15,866 --> 02:08:19,035
- [chuckles]
- Yeah, helping's not really my thing.

2372
02:08:19,036 --> 02:08:21,372
- [Akira] All right, we'll be back soon.
- [Rai] Excuse us.

2373
02:08:21,872 --> 02:08:24,457
- Wait a minute, was that…
- [Iroha] My brother.

2374
02:08:24,458 --> 02:08:27,043
[giggles]

2375
02:08:27,044 --> 02:08:29,088
I can see why he's popular.

2376
02:08:30,005 --> 02:08:32,382
[Mami] That means
the other two with him were…

2377
02:08:32,383 --> 02:08:33,883
[Mami shrieks]

2378
02:08:33,884 --> 02:08:36,721
Guess you're not shy anymore, Iroha.

2379
02:08:37,430 --> 02:08:40,682
Well, a lot has happened over the years.

2380
02:08:40,683 --> 02:08:44,437
You never know,
I might have surpassed even you, Yachiyo.

2381
02:08:44,937 --> 02:08:47,063
Okay, work's done for the day.

2382
02:08:47,064 --> 02:08:50,067
Time to head home.
Gotta have a work-life balance.

2383
02:08:55,865 --> 02:08:56,866
Morning!

2384
02:09:01,454 --> 02:09:03,830
[groans]

2385
02:09:03,831 --> 02:09:05,541
Wow, it's heavy.

2386
02:09:06,709 --> 02:09:09,252
It fits you better than the last model.

2387
02:09:09,253 --> 02:09:10,921
Oh! Pancakes!

2388
02:09:11,714 --> 02:09:13,965
We haven't quite worked out
the sense of taste.

2389
02:09:13,966 --> 02:09:17,011
Oh, I don't want to wait another second!

2390
02:09:19,180 --> 02:09:21,265
[chuckles]

2391
02:09:21,974 --> 02:09:25,977
[Otako] I can't believe I'm alive to
see this day… Kaguya's comeback concert!

2392
02:09:25,978 --> 02:09:28,688
Airing in both the real world
and Tsukuyomi!

2393
02:09:28,689 --> 02:09:30,775
And Yachiyo will be dancing with her!

2394
02:09:31,901 --> 02:09:34,027
[Kaguya] It's been so long!

2395
02:09:34,028 --> 02:09:35,403
[Iroha] Only 8,000 years.

2396
02:09:35,404 --> 02:09:37,489
[Yachiyo] That's only last week for me.

2397
02:09:37,490 --> 02:09:40,658
[giggling]

2398
02:09:40,659 --> 02:09:42,161
[crowd cheering]

2399
02:09:43,662 --> 02:09:45,623
Let's go!

2400
02:09:51,128 --> 02:09:55,174
[Kaguya] So what do you think?
Is this the story's happily ever after?

2401
02:09:56,008 --> 02:09:59,385
What if after the concert,
they have a fight and break up?

2402
02:09:59,386 --> 02:10:02,097
[laughs] There's just
no way to know for sure.

2403
02:10:02,598 --> 02:10:04,892
It's the same for your story, right?

2404
02:10:05,643 --> 02:10:09,188
For now, this is the end of our story.

2405
02:10:10,314 --> 02:10:11,315
The title?

2406
02:10:12,399 --> 02:10:13,859
The title is…

2407
02:10:14,360 --> 02:10:16,946
COSMIC PRINCESS KAGUYA!

2408
02:10:39,385 --> 02:10:42,512
♪ I feel like when we parted was longer ♪

2409
02:10:42,513 --> 02:10:45,932
♪ Longer ago than it must've been ♪

2410
02:10:45,933 --> 02:10:49,519
♪ Kept that sad, lonely light
All sealed away inside ♪

2411
02:10:49,520 --> 02:10:53,022
♪ And I stamped my foot
Till my heel hurt ♪

2412
02:10:53,023 --> 02:10:57,110
♪ Oh, I could still see it
When I was with you ♪

2413
02:10:57,111 --> 02:11:00,488
♪ Now I can't see it again anymore ♪

2414
02:11:00,489 --> 02:11:04,117
♪ Staring off at that comet
Invisible and bright ♪

2415
02:11:04,118 --> 02:11:07,620
♪ Now I'm searching desperately
For it still ♪

2416
02:11:07,621 --> 02:11:11,124
♪ I sang and I sang so many songs ♪

2417
02:11:11,125 --> 02:11:14,961
♪ Melodies that I can't ever sing again ♪

2418
02:11:14,962 --> 02:11:18,423
♪ I wasn't lonely even a bit ♪

2419
02:11:18,424 --> 02:11:22,010
♪ Now I know what it's like
To be lonely for real ♪

2420
02:11:22,011 --> 02:11:26,097
♪ Don't know how long it's been
Don't know how far I've gone ♪

2421
02:11:26,098 --> 02:11:29,809
♪ I don't even know
What's right or what's wrong ♪

2422
02:11:29,810 --> 02:11:33,229
♪ I don't even have
The time to stop and think ♪

2423
02:11:33,230 --> 02:11:37,025
♪ I'm just making my feet
Keep walking on ♪

2424
02:11:37,026 --> 02:11:40,737
♪ I want to spend my time
Just having fun ♪

2425
02:11:40,738 --> 02:11:44,324
♪ Brushing all my troubles off
With a laugh ♪

2426
02:11:44,325 --> 02:11:47,702
♪ It'll be okay
This pain won't go away ♪

2427
02:11:47,703 --> 02:11:51,624
♪ Even if I forget, it'll stay with me ♪

2428
02:11:52,124 --> 02:11:55,251
♪ We built a road of pretty ideals, but ♪

2429
02:11:55,252 --> 02:11:58,671
♪ Here comes reality wiping it clean ♪

2430
02:11:58,672 --> 02:12:02,258
♪ But our memories linger
Shining in our wake ♪

2431
02:12:02,259 --> 02:12:06,596
♪ They'll keep lighting the way
Forevermore ♪

2432
02:12:06,597 --> 02:12:09,807
♪ Oh, why did we end up
Losing each other? ♪

2433
02:12:09,808 --> 02:12:13,186
♪ Why did we have to part ways
Back then? ♪

2434
02:12:13,187 --> 02:12:14,938
♪ Now that sad, lonely light ♪

2435
02:12:14,939 --> 02:12:16,856
♪ Makes my shadow stretch and grow ♪

2436
02:12:16,857 --> 02:12:20,526
♪ Looming tall and deep there
In front of me ♪

2437
02:12:20,527 --> 02:12:23,863
♪ Sometimes there's
A fever burning inside ♪

2438
02:12:23,864 --> 02:12:27,700
♪ And I'll try to sleep
When I find the time ♪

2439
02:12:27,701 --> 02:12:31,162
♪ Even knowing that all this
Is only a dream ♪

2440
02:12:31,163 --> 02:12:34,832
♪ I want to find you there
And set out again ♪

2441
02:12:34,833 --> 02:12:38,920
♪ Far, far away from
The boundless open sky ♪

2442
02:12:38,921 --> 02:12:42,507
♪ Even in the endless depths of the dark ♪

2443
02:12:42,508 --> 02:12:45,885
♪ All I need to do
Is think about those stars ♪

2444
02:12:45,886 --> 02:12:49,806
♪ And I'm there
In the glow of the galaxy ♪

2445
02:12:49,807 --> 02:12:53,476
♪ Even if I stop just crying
All the time ♪

2446
02:12:53,477 --> 02:12:57,105
♪ Even if I buy a new pair of shoes ♪

2447
02:12:57,106 --> 02:13:00,483
♪ It'll be okay
This pain won't go away ♪

2448
02:13:00,484 --> 02:13:04,278
♪ Even if I forget, it'll stay with me ♪

2449
02:13:04,279 --> 02:13:06,197
♪ I know there was something ♪

2450
02:13:06,198 --> 02:13:07,991
♪ You wanted to tell me ♪

2451
02:13:07,992 --> 02:13:10,494
♪ All that time ago ♪

2452
02:13:11,662 --> 02:13:14,998
♪ It was probably some old silly cliche ♪

2453
02:13:14,999 --> 02:13:19,586
♪ But I wanna know
I've gotta know ♪

2454
02:13:33,225 --> 02:13:36,644
♪ I know that our meetings and partings ♪

2455
02:13:36,645 --> 02:13:40,481
♪ Are always two parts of a single whole ♪

2456
02:13:40,482 --> 02:13:43,901
♪ That invisible comet
Is still out there ♪

2457
02:13:43,902 --> 02:13:47,947
♪ It's invisible, so it's never gone ♪

2458
02:13:47,948 --> 02:13:51,576
♪ A or B or C
I don't know which is right ♪

2459
02:13:51,577 --> 02:13:55,288
♪ I don't know what answers everyone had ♪

2460
02:13:55,289 --> 02:13:58,666
♪ I don't even have
The time to stop and check ♪

2461
02:13:58,667 --> 02:14:02,545
♪ I'm just living my life
With all I've got ♪

2462
02:14:02,546 --> 02:14:06,174
♪ Even if I stop just crying
All the while ♪

2463
02:14:06,175 --> 02:14:09,844
♪ Even if I brush things off
With a smile ♪

2464
02:14:09,845 --> 02:14:13,222
♪ It'll be okay
This pain won't go away ♪

2465
02:14:13,223 --> 02:14:17,060
♪ Even if I forget, it'll stay with me ♪

2466
02:14:17,061 --> 02:14:20,480
♪ It'll be all right
I see this ray of light ♪

2467
02:14:20,481 --> 02:14:22,941
♪ And I know at the start ♪

2468
02:14:23,859 --> 02:14:27,780
♪ You're standing there ♪

2469
02:15:17,538 --> 02:15:21,750
♪ Melting, I feel like I might melt away ♪

2470
02:15:38,392 --> 02:15:39,560
♪ Melting ♪

2471
02:15:43,939 --> 02:15:45,857
♪ Each morning when I wake up ♪

2472
02:15:45,858 --> 02:15:49,443
♪ The very first thing I think of is you ♪

2473
02:15:49,444 --> 02:15:52,364
♪ Just you, always you ♪

2474
02:15:54,241 --> 02:15:56,200
♪ I thought I'd make a change ♪

2475
02:15:56,201 --> 02:15:59,662
♪ Kept hoping you'd notice
And ask me "What's up?" ♪

2476
02:15:59,663 --> 02:16:02,666
♪ "Why did you cut your bangs?" ♪

2477
02:16:04,001 --> 02:16:06,711
♪ My pretty flowy pink skirt ♪

2478
02:16:06,712 --> 02:16:09,172
♪ My shiny flower hairpin ♪

2479
02:16:09,173 --> 02:16:11,716
♪ I'll put them on when I go out ♪

2480
02:16:11,717 --> 02:16:13,384
♪ Today ♪

2481
02:16:13,385 --> 02:16:17,514
♪ I just want to look so cute for you ♪

2482
02:16:25,063 --> 02:16:29,233
♪ Melting, I feel like I might melt away ♪

2483
02:16:29,234 --> 02:16:32,528
♪ Can't ever tell you I love you ♪

2484
02:16:32,529 --> 02:16:35,323
♪ Can't tell you how I feel, but ♪

2485
02:16:35,324 --> 02:16:39,619
♪ Melting, can't even look you
In the eye ♪

2486
02:16:39,620 --> 02:16:41,746
♪ I'm not in love with love ♪

2487
02:16:41,747 --> 02:16:45,541
♪ I'm just in love with you ♪

2488
02:16:45,542 --> 02:16:50,129
♪ You're all that I've got
In my heart now ♪

2489
02:16:50,130 --> 02:16:51,256
♪ I love you ♪

2490
02:17:01,725 --> 02:17:03,726
♪ The weather forecast ♪

2491
02:17:03,727 --> 02:17:04,852
♪ Was lying to me ♪

2492
02:17:04,853 --> 02:17:08,356
♪ It's raining cats and dogs out here ♪

2493
02:17:08,357 --> 02:17:10,317
♪ Right now ♪

2494
02:17:11,985 --> 02:17:14,111
♪ Right there in my school bag ♪

2495
02:17:14,112 --> 02:17:15,321
♪ My umbrella is packed ♪

2496
02:17:15,322 --> 02:17:17,323
♪ But I'm not pleased at all ♪

2497
02:17:17,324 --> 02:17:20,159
♪ I let out a sigh ♪

2498
02:17:20,160 --> 02:17:21,744
♪ That's when you show up ♪

2499
02:17:21,745 --> 02:17:24,080
♪ "I guess I'll have to share" ♪

2500
02:17:24,081 --> 02:17:26,999
♪ "You can come walk under mine with me" ♪

2501
02:17:27,000 --> 02:17:31,254
♪ You give a little smile
You're right there by my side ♪

2502
02:17:31,255 --> 02:17:35,132
♪ I can hear the sound
Of me falling in love ♪

2503
02:17:35,133 --> 02:17:38,011
♪ The sound of me falling in love ♪

2504
02:17:41,640 --> 02:17:42,890
♪ Falling in love ♪

2505
02:17:42,891 --> 02:17:47,186
♪ Melting, I feel like I might suffocate ♪

2506
02:17:47,187 --> 02:17:48,896
♪ My right hand's at my side ♪

2507
02:17:48,897 --> 02:17:50,439
♪ It's touching you ♪

2508
02:17:50,440 --> 02:17:52,400
♪ And trembling ♪

2509
02:17:52,401 --> 02:17:54,193
♪ My heart is beating loud ♪

2510
02:17:54,194 --> 02:17:57,571
♪ Beneath this shared umbrella ♪

2511
02:17:57,572 --> 02:17:59,240
♪ Now I'm so close to you ♪

2512
02:17:59,241 --> 02:18:00,741
♪ I could reach my hand ♪

2513
02:18:00,742 --> 02:18:03,327
♪ Oh, gosh, what now? ♪

2514
02:18:03,328 --> 02:18:08,249
♪ I just want my feelings to reach you ♪

2515
02:18:08,250 --> 02:18:10,334
♪ God, if you can hear me, please ♪

2516
02:18:10,335 --> 02:18:12,128
♪ Let time stand still ♪

2517
02:18:12,129 --> 02:18:13,838
♪ Feel like I could cry ♪

2518
02:18:13,839 --> 02:18:17,591
♪ But I'm happy ♪

2519
02:18:17,592 --> 02:18:19,636
♪ It might just kill me! ♪

2520
02:19:00,761 --> 02:19:04,972
♪ Melting
We're almost to the station now ♪

2521
02:19:04,973 --> 02:19:06,640
♪ We'll never meet again ♪

2522
02:19:06,641 --> 02:19:08,267
♪ You're here right now ♪

2523
02:19:08,268 --> 02:19:11,145
♪ So close and yet so far, so ♪

2524
02:19:11,146 --> 02:19:12,229
♪ Melting ♪

2525
02:19:12,230 --> 02:19:15,358
♪ Let's hold hands
While you walk with me! ♪

2526
02:19:15,359 --> 02:19:17,318
♪ Oh, tell me, do we really ♪

2527
02:19:17,319 --> 02:19:21,280
♪ Have to say goodbye now? ♪

2528
02:19:21,281 --> 02:19:22,406
♪ Please hold me tight ♪

2529
02:19:22,407 --> 02:19:25,910
♪ Wrap me in your arms this instant! ♪

2530
02:19:25,911 --> 02:19:27,120
♪ Just kidding ♪

2531
02:19:42,886 --> 02:19:45,054
[Yachiyo] Even after 8,000 years,

2532
02:19:45,055 --> 02:19:48,850
all I can think about is eating fluffy,
yummy pancakes.

2533
02:19:50,018 --> 02:19:53,270
I'll never forget those delicious,
perfect, happy…

2534
02:19:53,271 --> 02:19:56,107
- [Iroha] You're so extra!
- [Yachiyo laughs]

2535
02:19:56,108 --> 02:19:59,778
[Iroha, Yachiyo laughing]

